kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"VER. 2025.03\n\nRules and Regulations Outrance rules and regulations","page_from":1,"page_to":2,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a200b774b3254215653456fc7d6df36c22759421c0b05172a8941624ee45203d","has_figures":true,"extraction":"mixed"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General provisions","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b4f55b0721414150889a4410e85c6e0e88af141e828fa703c7c8c6661d2ce077","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Types of fights","body":"Outrance fights may be held in two ways:","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"19ac942cb2a7e28918b5338959b582e607ca1c8402f0ff171ad5b1cf59edbf60","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.1","title":null,"body":"Matched fights: one single fight between 2 competitors.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.1.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e268dc9008ec91154fa155d20c6b74c358fdfc6e36f155c52f2c3099fcc80a7f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.2","title":null,"body":"Tournament: a series of fights between multiple competitors.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.1.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3795db96cb2361dc4e282417a23884570b755156a268ac3ed22bd6756336077f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Weight categories","body":"Outrance fights are held in different categories based on the weight of participants.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"faaa29fe71d03af042f4159c017440d99b0c0dd5c7053538f653b20731cb1896","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.1","title":"For men","body":"● Lightweight: Up to a maximum of 75 kg.\n● Middleweight: Over 75 kg up to a maximum of 85 kg.\n● Light Heavyweight: Over 85 kg up to a maximum of 95 kg.\n● Heavyweight: Over 95 kg up to a maximum of 105 kg.\n● Super Heavyweight Over 105 kg up to a maximum of 115 kg.\n● Ultra Heavyweight: Over 115 kg.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d59bf3754501de0d395687974395f37f966bce7e4b5343eb9619a94d160f7ec2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.2","title":"For women","body":"● Featherweight: Up to a maximum of 60 kg.\n● Lightweight: Over 60 kg up to a maximum of 70 kg.\n● Middleweight: Over 70 kg up to a maximum of 80 kg.\n● Light Heavyweight: over 80 kg up to a maximum of 90 kg.\n● Heavyweight: over 90 kg.\n\nMen Women\n\nFeatherweight <60kg\n\nLightweight   <75kg   60 - 70 kg\n\nMiddleweight   75 - 85 kg   70 - 80 kg\n\nLight Heavyweight   85 - 95 kg   80 - 90 kg\n\nHeavyweight   95 -105 kg   >90 kg\n\nSuper Heavyweight 105 -115 kg\n\nUltra Heavyweight >115kg","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"74fd53dc413f5ae6ac32a7fae3b1834d24636e731ddc212a06857683a721f016","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.3","title":"Open Weight category","body":"Should both participants agree, there may be a difference in the weight of competitors not based on the previously mentioned weight categories. This will not generate a Weight Modifier if agreed upon in advance","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"55e1bccdfafd750eb406cac55859f1a55b8ae6e2b09ef29e36b42d4d7d572d90","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.4","title":"Weigh-in procedure","body":"The weigh-in will be done on the day of competition to assign competitors to the proper category. If a competitor misses the weigh-in, they may have to forfeit their fight or the tournament.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"efc395af2b7535de66af2031f3c3a043b5757698a3167071338ce47a76d9addc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"Divisions","body":"Division 1 is for more experienced competitors and will be rewarded more League points for this format (Defined as fighters with over 2 years competitive experience or fighters with demonstrable international experience.) Division 2 is for less experienced competitors, structured to be more forgiving to newcomers to the ruleset. (Defined as fighters with under 2 years competitive experience and no or minimal international competitive experience.) Division 2 fighters can elect to fight in Division 1 should they choose to.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["2"],"content_sha256":"e650db16fbb44bfec8ed2c1d0d8f720794c29d4b0da37e10a9540575d75ee556","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4","title":"Criteria for participation","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"edd00c26c8fa62226bfbe13f60e726ef0f3a3e8a7b0ff0dda90d9b5b35edcdcc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4.1","title":"Legal age","body":"Competitors must be of legal age according to the laws of both their country and the country in which the competition is held.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5507f8e1e4a9801c69d3cf8c0f06f5512a804c7dcd1abb7eb76ad2705dd09475","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4.2","title":"Medical fitness","body":"Competitors must declare themselves medically fit to fight before the competition.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"de75ce1b68b7a6e112ceef2deab16d0f98d96032c83f49aff64df00177da6bfe","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4.3","title":"Medical support","body":"Each competition should have professional medical support provided by the organizer of the event.\nIn case of an injury, members of the medical support team may decide to withdraw the injured competitor from competition.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"07e80c2c6cb89011da06ab0170a49000008bde0aae1a72ff1bbe9f6a4765f89c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Marshals committee","body":"During an event, it is allowed to combine some of the marshals’ duties, for example the duties of the timekeeper may be combined with the secretary, and technical marshal with any other duties (knight marshal, line marshal, etc.).\nA marshals committee should consist of:","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e32308a38003194e2d5b0583dbf8556f50f08f376c7fc5fd65775c4fcfaa15d0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"One (1) senior knight marshal","body":"The senior knight marshal:\n● is responsible for the work of the marshals committee during the competition,\n● takes the lead in the consideration by the Marshals Committee of any appeal submitted by competitors,\n● has the final say in all matters related to the consideration of said protests, and in the interpretation of the rules,\n● Is responsible for reviewing circumstances related to competitor stoppage, cornerman stoppage and TKO stoppage.\n● Where only one knight marshal is present, they can perform the senior knight marshal duties.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"74465fb3bb18d2f0e98d7205b95547efa15163392c9a3df773e4b2cddfb10c65","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"One (1) knight marshal","body":"The knight marshal:\n● is responsible for checking the readiness of competitors, marshals, and timekeeper before the fight,\n● gives the command to start, suspend and stop the fight,\n● controls the course of the fight by:\n○ counting time of clinches, ○ reacting to breakages of armor and weapon, losses of weapon, use of unauthorized techniques, ○ assessing knockout (KO) and technical knockout (TKO) of competitors,\n● has the right to give verbal warnings, yellow and red cards (disqualification), and to expel corner men.\n● checks the condition of the list between the rounds of a fight,\n● announces the winner according to the result of points counted by the line marshals.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f8e342dbc793daf87c49cbb738a46387886a51dce9c484ada9d694ec06ccc22e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Three (3) or five (5) line marshals","body":"The line marshals:\n● review objectively all the actions made by both competitors during the fight,\n● take note of loss of weapons and armor failure,\n\n● each keep scores independently. They are not allowed to contact other line marshals during the round and should be located on different sides of the list.","page_from":7,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e112f7df1ed687216952b75724ff922066bfdbdd1b680d4368cef9dc0a2fe495","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"One (1) timekeeper","body":"The timekeeper:\n● counts down the time of each round of the fight and of each break between rounds,\n● counts down the time allotted for repairment/replacement of broken equipment,\n● announces the end of the round and the end of the break between rounds with the command ”Time” and the sound of a gong or similar device.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e89a6ed87c8584615a5d813381d37eba90a33c08c1ecaffa85b41d664956f587","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.5","title":"One (1) secretary","body":"The secretary:\n● records the results of each round of the fight based on points counted by the line marshals,\n● makes notes in the fight protocol. All yellow and red cards should be marked in the protocol for further calculations,\n● takes notes if any medical conditions forbids a competitor to continue fighting,\n● calls competitors to the list according to the order of the fights, in case there's no announcer/herald of the event.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"97071dc977933bfe41cc002e8306a0a250ead8ff900ef8a2a2e7a27870e633e5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.6","title":"One (1) technical marshal","body":"The technical marshal:\n● checks the safety of the offensive and defensive equipment of each competitor,\n● inspects the general appearance and historical accuracy of armor and weapon,\n● have the right to demand the replacement of a selected element of equipment if it does not meet requirements of safety, appearance, or historical accuracy,\n● checks the equipment before each fight, and after a fight if a competitor requests it.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"21bb961f594d735d778559542c072f94cee7dcccb64060e0d341d7a4201cc210","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.7","title":"One (1) video supervisor","body":"The video supervisor:\n● checks and reviews all appeals given to the knight marshal,\n● discusses and makes decisions on all appeals with the knight marshal.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1f5c68a6f7292fbb8a3e7fe35cc35654c8a1e847720bb1841eee36e14c7da021","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"General commands","body":"Commands reserved for the knight marshal","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f71b1f955f02c7cdc6fe6712829a77d5c1c54f33022bf14edfda1228b761fb19","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"“Fight”","body":"Purpose: Initializes the fight at the beginning of the round or after any suspension of the fight.\nUsage: Start or resume the fight.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9e45b65ec70d9a916631eb6dccfb76a3a503ad748f0f76a61d91a2069baf09f7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"“Stop fight”","body":"Purpose: Stops the fight at the end of the round or when the fight is finished due to KO (Knockout) or TKO (Technical Knockout).\nUsage: Conclude the fight.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3b9dc97224ea393412aa5865b5223dbea0b74721fa4f85450c7b71f591c00e77","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"“Break”","body":"Purpose: Pauses the fight and separates both competitors.\nUsage: Temporarily stops the fight, creating a break between the competitors.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"924bd548f9de9c4dfaa081266e7ab56494fc6a967a647cfebf50b722a7b800ed","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"“Hold”","body":"Purpose: Pauses the fight but holds competitors' positions for a re-arm of the weapon or to move both competitors to the middle of the list when needed.\nUsage: Temporarily halts the action, keeping the competitors in their current positions for specific adjustments.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"08d830c80ec51e119c6bc47a84459ef8548b23b082baf185fb40896100a81879","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"“Breakdown of weapon/armor”","body":"Purpose: Announces the breakdown of part of the equipment.\nUsage: After the “Break” command has been given, indicates a specific issue with a competitor's weapon or armor that requires attention.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"41a4cfe376a7997a01b3ee393462b4407646e08d345d499030c05de71d080b6b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.6","title":"“Loss of weapon”","body":"Purpose: Used when one of the competitors loses their weapon.\nUsage: After the “Hold” command has been given, indicates that a competitor has lost their weapon during the paused state.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"27798fe49e21aefc8c78c8d2e5b4660f0e63c4ef763d61056dde570c3ae88f3d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.7","title":"“Knockout”","body":"Purpose: Used when one of the competitors is subject to a KO or TKO and after the “Stop fight” command has been given.\nUsage: Declares the end of the fight due to a knockout or technical knockout.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0fa9f68bd5d618e969740a3fdafe0dbf1f91d159b7998976c0de470d878df8e6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.8","title":"“Time”","body":"Purpose: Announces the flow of time during the fight.\nUsage:\n● To signify the end of a round or the end of a break between rounds.\n● If there was a breakdown of equipment, and the competitor has been granted time to repair it.\n● This command keeps track of the time progression during the fight.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.8","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ba665144d3d651cc7b513268368310c9b24a07c18a66232fc68a92c0939f92c2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Fight procedures","body":"A fight against an opponent consists of multiple rounds. The time duration of rounds and breaks and the number of rounds in a fight depends on the tournament type and Division. Below are the number of rounds and the round time durations.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bd0c91ac9ce102cdc85aa144fb1b8be011d086cb3be95ebb8246a3d59b6dc3a8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Matched fights","body":"Matched fights are competitive “Matches” where opponents are paired based on factors like skill, weight, experience, or age to ensure fairness and balance in the contest.\n\nDivision 1:Matched\n● 3 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds)\n● 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds) Division 2:\n● 3 rounds of 1 minute and 30 seconds (90 seconds)\n● 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds)","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:4.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0cc429e94cdc1384a0c644c93a70ccb3a6aa2e8231ff143b490af34d39b8ca58","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Tournament fights","body":"Division 1:\n● 2 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds)\n● 1 break of 45 seconds Division 2:\n● 2 rounds of 1 minute and 30 seconds (90 seconds)\n● 1 break of 45 seconds\n\nMatched fights Tournament fights\n\nDivision 1 3 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds) 2 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds) 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds) 1 break of 45 seconds\n\nDivision 2 3 rounds of 1m30s (90 seconds) 2 rounds of 1m30s (90 seconds) 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds) 1 break of 45 seconds\n\nImportant!\nFor tournament fights, if after two rounds the fight is a draw, a 3rd round will be fought.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:4.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:4","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"37d84b49bd9c84da095ae31ebf4864c397afca1ff2a738fc3ac4c6ccdcee6659","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Competitors","body":"","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e3207a0ba88189b190d7e840fa8cd17cecedf7325a32cac518c1d7a2fa68a2f0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"Knowledge and respect of the rules","body":"All competitors are obligated to know the rules and regulations and to strictly obey them.\nThey shall obey commands given by the knight marshal.\nThey shall defend themselves at all times unless under the direct instruction of the knight marshal to “Stop Fight”, “Break” or “Hold”.\nThey shall be polite to other participants, marshals, and spectators.\nSwearing, rudeness, and other impolite actions may be penalized by the knight marshal with a verbal warning, yellow card, or even disqualification if they are persistent.\nIn the case above, actions taken outside the list, the knight marshal may demand penalizing them by the event organizer and/or League.\nAll competitors shall use a set of armor, weapon, and clothes that fulfill all technical safety requirements.\nThey shall come to the list within one (1) minute after being called by the herald/secretary/announcer of the event.\nThey should have a set of spare weapons and elements of armor, along with the necessary repair kit that allows making urgent repairs.\nEach competitor should have at least one (1) corner man. A competitor has a maximum of two\n(2) corner men.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"22b49d81ab498de451b093aec260a29aeeade9a62ab6f5986e45758c1f3c2b09","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"Competitor stoppage","body":"A competitor may stop the fight to yield during a round. They signal the knight marshal by throwing their weapon to the surface of the list and/or shouting “Stop fighting”.\nA competitor may forfeit before the fight has started because of:\n● TKO armor/weapon failure: The competitor is unable to continue the fight because of their damaged armor/weapon.\n● Medical retirement: The competitor is unable to continue the fight for a medical reason (e.g., injury).\nImportant!\nA competitor that yields or forfeits will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"02c042857fbe0d20c7cf6162deb04c0efeda153f91445d7f6b8d58f39e88ebfd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Appeal submission","body":"The competitor may submit an appeal protest to the marshals committee if, in their opinion, an action or actions taken by the opponent or any marshal contradicts the rules.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c45d80723513688b9a4109bd9e32f82996be57bea35eca8ea30e2398745c10da","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"6","title":"Corner support","body":"","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7ad0120d16aa8ae47c5fc116019e402797e46689352d9f7cdd4b6efd7b951c6e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.1","title":"Knowledge and respect of rules","body":"All corner men are obligated to know the rules and regulations and to strictly obey them.\nThey shall obey commands given by the knight marshal.\nThey shall help their competitor to the limits of the list and aid them in preparations before the fight.\nThey shall be ready during the fight to make repairs/exchanges of damaged equipment or weapons according to the Marshal's demands.\nThey shall only enter the list in the time between rounds or at the demand of the knight marshal to aid the competitor in repairing/exchanging damaged equipment.\nThey shall be polite to other participants, marshals, and spectators.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f6c8e5bf4b24e3ae0ad0d9450156977d7c8ef708c2299a30e18365ca06bcc610","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.2","title":"Right to demand stoppage","body":"A corner man has the right to demand to stop the fight. They signal the above demand by throwing a white towel/flag onto the surface of the list.\nThey have the right to demand to stop the fight in the following cases:\n● They recognize and accept the defeat of their competitor (TKO).\n● Their competitor is unable to continue fighting caused by the breakdown or loss of the element of their equipment (TKO armor/weapons failure).\n● The competitor is unable to continue the fight due to an injury or other medical causes (Medical Retirement).\nImportant !\nIf one of their corner men demand to stop the fight, the competitor will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review of corner men stoppage.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"382ff724c7652b61a080c251d04bcdba49486b5e593236374f086574a4505f20","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.3","title":"Appeal submission","body":"The corner man has the right to submit an appeal in the name of their competitor (if they cannot do it by themselves) if, in their opinion, an action or actions taken by the opponent or any marshal contradicts the rules. See Section 16","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["16"],"content_sha256":"e8ebf367dfcfd33df7b92ca4f8df978f36e460aa36ed5ff4fe5037dd11909c25","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"7","title":"List requirements","body":"","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e6051cb2c8ed6ec153e10cdbe0fb713927f4be536f4c587c32a17b21800a3e0b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.1","title":"Size","body":"The list can be made of any suitable rigid structure.\nWidth: 5 meters minimum.\nLength: 10 meters maximum.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6d9d1d6aa3296f89ff4544c71aba17e8b3f1f6bb98c627010908e9dfc485b352","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.2","title":"List fence","body":"Height: between 0.9 meter (minimum) and 1.3 meters (maximum).\nIt should prevent competitors from coming out of the list’s limits.\nIt should be visible.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"05df3bc9d71ba6a710b3e1e7b9b7baa91f4b107c2bfa8b31f2c3b7c6b393cd34","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.3","title":"List boundaries","body":"Boundaries of the lists should be properly seated on the ground.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7b390e7aed015fd92b457b0178a979765f4f0f6e0ebca4d5ef9d6fab02b203ba","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.4","title":"Surface quality","body":"The surface of lists should be dense and plain.\nIt should prevent competitors from slipping.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"20b53862e65b488b5c1b43350b188cb6185ef179c3985a6abc80b039dbdb2a51","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.5","title":"Lighting","body":"The light source should be located above the list.\nPositioned at a height that prevents competitors from being blinded by it.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"475587dcf937a30a9dad124fc0d75fe53f0f417f38142038e7c95afa5404a2ce","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.6","title":"Signalization tools","body":"It is recommended to place a white towel in the competitors’ corners for the corner men to use if they want to demand the stoppage of the fight.\nIt is recommended to make a clear and visible mark for the starting corner of each competitor.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"618d6b5de589c3a03dae7beed0958ec661eb7d9e2ce2792882fbb9b45224c320","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.7","title":"Safety zone","body":"The organizer must provide a 2m-wide safety zone by placing a barrier around every side of the list.\nOnly the marshals committee, the corner men, and accredited photo/videographers are permitted into the safety zone.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"edabb1365adfec42fc8ed7444841faec2ec956ba0ac1c454c90401783243d9e3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"8","title":"Authorized Equipment","body":"","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"496113a9bf833af881f77398b1f661869429b298a41f0628eb03be0b3182b7fb","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.1","title":"General requirements","body":"Technical and Authentic Compliance: all equipment must meet Buhurt International technical and authentic requirements.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c2a33aa57bffd4dd2212fa3416e3f2904006d88a8867af42924d3db0b277cb7b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":54,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.2","title":"Specifics on weapons and shields","body":"All Buhurt International weapons and shields are permitted.\nAny combination of these weapons is allowed.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b5d16a12999435d5aaacdcf80f49c4f65b99af51a8e6fed84710beb965f00cc3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":55,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.3","title":"Changes of equipment","body":"Participants are allowed to change elements of their equipment (armor or weapon) during intervals or due to breakage.\nThe supervision of the technical marshal is required for any change of equipment.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9547ab66402d5b6c8277ec3c1aed95f501f5c8d34553d5ef515b3b16cd27a1a7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":56,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.4","title":"Marshal authority","body":"The knight marshal and the technical marshal have the authority to demand changes to any element of armor or weapon for safety, aesthetic, or historical accuracy reasons.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"669e5d812acc64ba965a196e018973f027a1c33448ee85091a9548f29c4574e2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":57,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"9","title":"Authorized fighting techniques","body":"These rules aim to define a set of permitted and prohibited actions to ensure the safety of participants while engaging in combat. The guidelines cover striking, grabbing, and various techniques to maintain a fair and controlled environment during the event.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1861a2154f2bbcf34e37cc997c6643f96ef5b019a8e2929c7c33df875eddc258","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":58,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.1","title":"Permitted strikes","body":"Strikes are permitted with any part of the weapon, the shield, and with various body parts (arms, legs and head), whether standing or on the ground.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"463db0f2c4d6dc5f420f3e37e115cf0fdc213c676848695c010941c52f145953","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":59,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.2","title":"Permitted strike zones","body":"Strikes are allowed to any area not mentioned as a prohibited strike zone (See section 12 below).","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["12"],"content_sha256":"afc6275d61f3b495ee306879ae2f24a0208bf60c39f1b100a77c25d335ac68ce","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":60,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.3","title":"Weapon-grabbing","body":"Competitors are allowed to grab their own weapon and weapon blade with their hands.\nCompetitors are allowed to grab their opponent’s weapon (except by the blade) and shield with a free hand.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6e569761abb23e15a2f3c8ac06ebaee7357ee44260f7fd4f1fe5187ea9b63e28","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":61,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.4","title":"Techniques and moves","body":"Back heels, wrestling throws, and clinches are allowed.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0a2aaeee61085e518170add53a4f62b09ac68e73802b845bf174a1a03916c7b0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":62,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"10","title":"Prohibited fighting techniques","body":"These rules aim to ensure the safety, fairness, and adherence to a set of standards during the combat activities in the specified event.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e038657ba34ff935e5dd7db58723d75750050d961d2b268d63075fe5abc85ed5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":63,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.1","title":"Unlisted techniques","body":"Any actions not listed in section 9 of the rules are prohibited. Only authorized techniques are permitted.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["9"],"content_sha256":"d8994506e8d786f7579b262eef87d77ad2ae6a9938f3bd29c329f8e06e782391","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":64,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.2","title":"Thrusting actions","body":"Any thrusting actions with a weapon are prohibited. Threats of a thrusting action are also prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b66e09919729cecf191266007dd5da0dc963a9e438f0326ccb2cd867f494bbea","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":65,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.3","title":"Offensive actions at prohibited strike zones","body":"Any offensive actions aimed at any prohibited strike zones (See section 12 below) are prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["12"],"content_sha256":"730568cb565ffb6ab736923a995264760a67ac6fd08df2c7e97fce2def652688","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":66,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.4","title":"Actions with foot or shin at the knee","body":"Actions with the foot or shin aimed at the knee are prohibited. This includes actions that may cause the knee to hyperextend, such as push kicks to the thigh.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bdd2a1a56805d323c07108ff30e7071129601f687c1135fe76bd417d614bcc05","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":67,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.5","title":"Grappling and holding","body":"Grappling and holding with the hand on specific armor elements (aventail, edge of pauldrons, edge of the helmet), pushes on the bottom edge of the helmet, neck cranks, and subsequent neck twists are prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ebad01195a93f387d5e46c0e36c4bcf77c629161fc186e2efafafbd15649744a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":68,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.6","title":"Suffocation techniques","body":"Grips, clamps, suffocation techniques with direct pressure on the neck using any part of the body, equipment, or weapon are prohibited. A poorly fitted helmet does not count as a suffocating technique.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3af2ba155c4db337d42c3b28a45a5bde742afe0268d0d09fbb1c14d96d931ca2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":69,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.7","title":"Joint locks and hyperextension","body":"Arm lock techniques, leg lock techniques and any actions that may cause a limb to hyperextend are prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2f243cce25ae6a960f48d0a4e436f841b4867f51c7c63c5cc7302b78bf37d037","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":70,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.8","title":"Specific strikes","body":"Strikes with the head of a one-handed axe are prohibited if the grip of the hand on the shaft is less than 30cm away from the axe’s head.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.8","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5bad418b26eee2070ef7b7cb03bbaf02324f2a792d23ed2438137d316277ef7f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":71,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.9","title":"Armor tampering","body":"Deliberate attempts to remove any elements of the armor are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.9","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6b7b4ea932304fb1d125dae460a9fc74d04c24e15a052ed844524e3bfb7dc0ca","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":72,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.10","title":"Strikes to a disarmed opponent","body":"Strikes to an opponent who has lost their weapon are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.10","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"84b9084515fcabc21f3c37ddcf2dfe4e6b38f8ff6cfe6bac0bf125d0a77129a9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":73,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.11","title":"Strikes to a grounded opponent","body":"Foot and shin strikes to a grounded opponent are prohibited.\nKnee strikes to a grounded opponent’s legs or head are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.11","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"28510dc32cc2d677ab083007345ed4951f141e36aa4a3e419995cd621cfafd5d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":74,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.12","title":"Dangerous take downs","body":"Any takedown that forces an opponent to land on their head/neck and suplex (arch throws) variations are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.12","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"085ebf40e5c0bd61a4dbe650ef7e85ee52df6e2ea86e68d2f5c5868b21f64416","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":75,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.13","title":"Out-of-bounds actions","body":"Intentional pushing or throwing an opponent out of the designated fighting area (list) is prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.13","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e2b8a8baa47db4ddca50f5322e8801fdc13e3f4fc4b38bcc098115653025efb9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":76,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.14","title":"Fence interaction","body":"Grabbing the fence and resting with hands/elbows above the fence is prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.14","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ab8a7a6166cb42684eaa12269fce4aaff1c79d3d26d4b3c80597de9346b0c5d8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":77,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.15","title":"Eye protection","body":"Attacks that may penetrate the eye slits of the opponent's helmet are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.15","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3da3ab854ee4291c286626b6694062a7dea988d41fb8b178bf983649cac847ab","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":78,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.16","title":"Intentional passivity","body":"Intentional passivity and stalling of the action are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.16","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"84300c0852731b2133834b04875369a637fe4e63bca744c477fd61f932ad3c66","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":79,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.17","title":"Assistance after a break","body":"A competitor cannot purposefully push on their opponent to get up off the ground after a \"Break\" or \"Stop fight\" command.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.17","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a8c2c2232fc5989d49bf3f959587bbde6e8e0d2816ef8a418c1d2449a0ea3e1d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":80,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"11","title":"Other prohibited actions","body":"These rules contribute to maintaining the integrity, safety, and orderliness of the event. They cover aspects such as participants behavior, substance use, adherence to commands, and respect for officials and other attendees. The role of the knight marshal is highlighted in several instances, emphasizing their authority and responsibility in ensuring the proper conduct of the event.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9be680ebc896e3803ef470fdd8ec40c885159bcb77c63485cc641e9e9db5d444","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":81,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.1","title":"Leaving the list","body":"Intentional leaving of the list after the command “Start fight” and before the announcement of the results of the fight is prohibited. Permission to leave must be granted by the knight marshal.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b427588b2dfd29cee4ee03ede09d61fb8133e0a99aa386985fa699d4676a2b4d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":82,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.2","title":"Equipment and weapon approval","body":"Competitors are not allowed to use any part of the equipment or any weapon that hasn't been allowed by the technical marshal.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"479bb988a530a3044a7e3dc1eef83e813bd4d52169f82949ef553386d11edea2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":83,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.3","title":"Substance use","body":"Competitors are not allowed to be under the influence of alcohol or any psychoactive substances.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a9c911e3f8f27bacca5d368c5d24c77d8e5408e040ad7d85cb6357bbc3f8cec5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":84,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.4","title":"Stalling after commands","body":"Intentionally stalling for time after a “Break” or “Hold” command has been given is prohibited. The knight marshal will issue a warning, and if the competitor is not ready after the warning, a 5-second count will be initiated. If the count reaches 5 seconds, the fight will be stopped, and a TKO win will be awarded to the opposing competitor.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"90a3daed5161e14ada783a079e501aba9006f723a75b7168b6103eeebd3e2193","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":85,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.5","title":"Offensive actions against others participants","body":"Any offensive actions against marshals, corner men, spectators, or anyone else other than the current opponent are prohibited.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2c86702d3e4dc933998828a44433aca54faa0875f760dd1bc1593ca572a4970b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":86,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.6","title":"Event interference","body":"Any actions made by a competitor or their corner men that may impede the course of the event are prohibited.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"844b31352bb827d5b9dc20ae011be50e76d9c05c98828c63a9e13aee59000b0f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":87,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"12","title":"Prohibited strike zones","body":"These rules are designed to prioritize the safety of the participants by prohibiting strikes to vulnerable and potentially dangerous areas. Their overall intention is to prevent serious injuries and ensure a fair and safe competition.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4c9b2a336f776e1d79d4a09b44ef0fc88d57675bb2d6a8e26126dcd7b5a41af6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":88,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.1","title":"Back and front of the neck","body":"Strikes to the back and front of the neck are prohibited.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ba5b4d19d67dbc00da3a0d862ce3f42233a188c52db100966e34beed9fcc9d51","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":89,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.2","title":"Base of the skull","body":"Strikes to the base of the skull are prohibited.\nThe base of the skull is defined as the bottom third of the back of the helmet.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0ac383a5ab2ee6d4111ddd671247ec3713532cbfe465348ad6d3b0c1e8e67820","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":90,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.3","title":"Back of the knee","body":"Strikes to the back of the knee are prohibited.\nPlacing pressure to the back of the knee is prohibited.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fe6d30aad8e67c65b4e0d14636bd36943630ca300bb1a6af7effd36692fdc75f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":91,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.4","title":"Groin and crotch","body":"Strikes to the groin and crotch are prohibited.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b0967807713ead468ffecca5a927a47cdc2a1f0234a4d2655712796ab9d7e65f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":92,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.5","title":"Foot and ankle","body":"Strikes to the feet and ankles are prohibited. However, striking the foot is not considered a prohibited strike if the competitor raises their foot while the strike is already occurring.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8b10bd12f1d9be3f9cba59d1431feb1c364e4d7fcc5f5d2d6ae4ce0d4f40afa5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":93,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.6","title":"Unprotected body parts","body":"Any part of the opponent’s body that has lost its protection is considered a prohibited strike zone.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bbb308732796487926d50b26501bfc6a6a4ad01e5f9b8c76c44f714af30bdb1b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":94,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.7","title":"Illustration of prohibited strikes zones","body":"","page_from":21,"page_to":21,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a8e6c1314e0cdd5061f5ccbf82d33826bd9941f9dc31bf92e6822464b17289b8","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":95,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"13","title":"Penalties","body":"These penalties are designed to maintain the integrity of the event, enforce the rules, and ensure a fair and safe competition. The progression from verbal warnings to yellow cards and potential disqualification emphasizes the seriousness of rule violations. Only the Knight Marshal may issue these","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"997a8550099ede83a4b331caa1222142b33d1840d88936d0825c64bd1fcf0db0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":96,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.1","title":"Verbal warning","body":"A verbal warning is given to a competitor or a corner man for a minor rule violation that does not significantly impact the course of the fight.\nIt serves as an alert that more serious actions will be taken if the violation is repeated.\nVerbal warnings do not have to be recorded in the protocol.\n3 verbal warnings will result in escalation to a yellow card.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2163118158cc9b73ea83ff01133e9db2779ba3505677d1d2cb5f1d9dd6e37717","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":97,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.2","title":"Yellow card","body":"Given by the knight marshal to a competitor or a corner man for systematic violations of the rules or for a violation that had a serious impact on the fight.\nYellow cards are recorded in the protocol and considered in the final score of the fight.\nThe knight marshal should point their hand in the direction of the competitor while announcing \"Yellow card”.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3caec1c9c3b0976f2ddee8374597c275c561b88afeda7a6243af099d20c90f49","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":98,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.3","title":"Expulsion of a corner man","body":"The knight marshal has the authority to expel a corner man for systematic violations of the rules or for a violation that had a serious impact on the fight.\nThe decision is noted in the protocol but does not affect the score of the fight.\nIf a competitor had only one (1) corner man, another person should be appointed immediately to take their position.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4d768c83b60dc32e6949ad34699c6e343f0f0b19572d1a2e1ae6c566c50b8f8e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":99,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.4","title":"Red card (disqualification)","body":"A red card equals a disqualification and is automatically given to a competitor who receives a second yellow card.\nIt may also be given if action(s) by the competitor or their corner man disrupt the course of the fight to the extent that it cannot continue or properly start.\nRed cards are recorded in the protocol.\nThe marshal should point their hand in the direction of the competitor while announcing “Red card” or “Disqualification”.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"773f40aaf3900eea21db6e1cba1166816aef78e58cb55f9484f88967a18c7fe8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":100,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"14","title":"Special situations","body":"","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"773ddf8e456ee306693d5fb0ed1dfd2dc8e565c1f917573fda9a0f611d56dc48","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":101,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.1","title":"Weapon loss","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with the “Hold” command.\n● Both competitors cease fighting, remain in position.\n● The knight marshal rearms the competitor and resets both competitors.\n● The knight marshal gives the “Fight” command.\nImportant note:\nWhen a fighter loses a weapon 3 or more times in a single round, this will result in a one (1) point deduction to the fighter's round. (see section 15.3.2 below) If a competitor loses their weapon more than twice during a round, they are deducted one (1) point off their round score (see section 15.3.2 below).","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["15.3.2"],"content_sha256":"a318d69a3ec618f1f65e6c0ec05b6c541b4f47895ac73e26919a9b08734025e7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":102,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.2","title":"Weapon breakage","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with the “Break” command.\n● The competitor must replace the weapon with a new one that was accepted by the technical marshal during the preparation of the fight.\n● If a replacement is impossible, victory is given to the opponent by TKO armor/weapon failure.\n● If a replacement is done, the fight continues with no penalty.","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"988c7976d51620eb6ac99af66c91e1c68fd5ce000a783f68635434b38967a204","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":103,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.3","title":"Armor failure","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with the “Break” command.\n● If the competitor, with the help of their corner men, can fix their armor in 90 seconds or less, they are deducted one (1) point off their round score (see section 15.3.2 below).\n● If they are unable to fix their armor in 90 seconds or less, they may be granted 90 additional seconds. They are deducted one (1) additional point off their round score (see section 15.3.2 below).\n● If they are still unable to fix the armor within the additional 90 seconds, their opponent is awarded the victory by TKO armor/weapon failure.","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["90","15.3.2"],"content_sha256":"3322b4cc1b04b3c16cfbbf98751681dfcc441b8a775bb2cbec688974c04b71e4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":104,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.4","title":"Clinch","body":"A clinch is a standing position where fighters lock their upper bodies together with their arms between competitors during the fight.\nProcedure:\n● If the clinch is inactive for 10 seconds, the knight marshal stops the fight with the “Break” command.\n● Both competitors separate, and after the \"Fight\" command, they continue the fight.","page_from":24,"page_to":24,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0e4411d50e1e2587f902cab80d8cb18dda3cce377d164cf92fbd91f00dd7419c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":105,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.5","title":"Unintentional fall outside or under the list","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with a \"Hold\" command.\n● Both competitors return to the middle of the list in the same position as when the \"Hold\" command was given.\n● \"Fight\" command is given to resume the fight.","page_from":24,"page_to":24,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3bd235d41c05949a2cce6ee44e7dc316cc6b75651ae620f7cdaad2e385569bb1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":106,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.6","title":"Grounded position","body":"A grounded position is a situation when a competitor has more than just the soles of their feet touching the ground. This includes hands, knees, back or their buttocks. One or both competitors can be in a grounded position simultaneously. The action is permitted to continue indefinitely providing that the action is consistent.\nProcedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight after 10 seconds of inactivity with the \"Break\" command.\n● Both competitors take a standing position about 3 meters apart and wait for the knight marshal's command to resume the fight.\n● A fallen competitor may take any actions to protect themselves (excluding prohibited actions).","page_from":24,"page_to":24,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2a9dd7611482f8fb051f1c811cba118b87837ddc1703d05438e733c9b8dec3f1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":107,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.7","title":"Technical knockout (TKO)","body":"Procedure:\n● Determination by the knight marshal: The knight marshal, as the official overseeing the fight, is responsible for determining if a fighter is no longer able to intelligently defend themselves.\n● Verbal warning: If the knight marshal observes that a fighter is unable to intelligently defend themselves, they will issue a verbal warning to the fighter.\n● 5-Second count: Following the verbal warning, the knight marshal will initiate a 5-second count, during which the fighter must demonstrate the ability to intelligently defend themselves.\n\n● Continuous lack of defense: If, after the 5-second count, the fighter continues to be unable to intelligently defend themselves, the knight marshal will intervene.\n● “Stop fight” announcement: At this point, the knight marshal will call for the fight to be stopped.\n● Declaration of TKO: Following the stoppage of the fight, the knight marshal will officially declare a Technical Knockout (TKO) by announcing \"Knockout.\"\n\n● TKO: If a competitor receives a TKO due to a lack of defense, they will lose the Match in Division 1 or the round in Division 2. All TKO’s must be checked by Medic to verify they can continue to fight","page_from":24,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9d7d30a84c10d726925ac6ac554fa6f53cc4e4a3d8ee323093ca9b37581994e7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":108,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8","title":"Intelligent defending","body":"","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3dda9eade07955e14fa30daa22bf6c0a7531a34ddda6be8a68ec367e9188d680","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":109,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.1","title":"Movement and positioning","body":"● Employing footwork to maintain distance from the opponent.\n● Utilizing angles and lateral movement to create advantageous positions.\n● Controlling the center of the fighting space to dictate the pace and direction of the engagement.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"dcbff9428353d31f634978660c03e0f4923291c8444b335c7d47e89b6c5a79ac","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":110,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.2","title":"Technique","body":"● Blocking or parrying strikes with proper technique to minimize impact.\n● Executing defensive maneuvers such as slips, rolls, and evasions to avoid incoming attacks.\n● Understanding defensive principles specific to different martial arts or combat sports.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"48f96c05f02637388e562ec267833b3bc27ba31cb1607de3298ac54dab2fb23f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":111,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.3","title":"Counterattacking opportunities","body":"● Identifying openings in the opponent's defense to launch effective counterattacks.\n● Capitalizing on the opponent's mistakes or vulnerabilities to turn the tide of the fight.\n● Using feints and baiting techniques to provoke reactions and create offensive opportunities.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a98657fd8a0a74e2e0ffcfd7956d21b38fac6992c7fc6db3c4c1a0ced8467087","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":112,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.4","title":"Composure and adaptability","body":"● Staying calm and focused under pressure to make sound defensive decisions.\n● Analyzing the opponent's movements and adjusting defensive strategies accordingly.\n● Being adaptable to changing circumstances and adjusting tactics as the fight progresses.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"731cfd9d418fe920e0bf688262dc307f4d2f4667879b9fa6fa5cb3e977c48732","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":113,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.9","title":"Disqualification","body":"Disqualification occurs when a competitor is unable to continue fighting due to:\n● No available weapon or armor breakage that can not be repaired in the given time.\n● Disqualification also includes a fighter that has received a red card.\n\nImportant!\nShould a fighter be subject to a disqualification due to no available weapon or armor breakage, they will have until their next match to fix the issue.","page_from":25,"page_to":26,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.9","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"719204070633e24639d1fc045927cc1ae6b160f85aa2088559d8da4d0d25f9fe","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":114,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.10","title":"Knockout (KO)","body":"knockout occurs when a fighter is rendered unconscious and unable to continue fighting.\nThe knight marshal will announce “Stop Fight” then “Knockout”.\nImportant!\nShould a fighter lose a fight by KO, they will not be allowed to participate further in the tournament.","page_from":26,"page_to":26,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.10","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d63e110239d2d1cba996d2dd14a8f262715052ee916a9d61194ee21ce133bbf8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":115,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"15","title":"Scoring the fight","body":"","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"264d62ce1bfa92461f3410e2c92acca94b5af9c1e5c5cecb8310366bab7cac8e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":116,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.1","title":"Scoring system overview","body":"","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"55266ab230144035ad1977f027524a6713f2cdd3f94d8857f38762ea4ed687d5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":117,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.1.1","title":"Number of line marshals","body":"3 or 5 line marshals evaluate each bout from different locations around the list/fighting area.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.1.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bdaa7d7664f8f9334074f338ed756c48d6e6cad609a536b0b467c5fb8503bcd1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":118,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.1.2","title":"Scoring system","body":"The “10-Point Must System” is the standard for scoring bouts.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.1.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"18489a91bf3080b7fe5c231d372528655a6b7710083599c41a8d7d2b3957d398","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":119,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2","title":"Evaluation criteria (in order of priority)","body":"","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"62a15857a695c2cd6eef1a23592d4a35568b2ad88a3b36ceed4c156460aa0dcc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":120,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.1","title":"Effective striking","body":"● Clear, strong, and well-placed legal strikes to permitted zones.\n● All legal strikes with weapons, legs, arms, and shields account for one (1) strike point per clean landed blow.\n● Strikes with the head do not award any strike point.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3d635b3e672f704e575cc3fcb95211203de55e0d8113ab0dd2250c191389cf65","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":121,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.2","title":"Effective grappling","body":"● Successful legal takedowns, position reversals, and clinch control.\n● Consideration for takedowns from standing position to dominant position, reversal of position, and positional clinch work.\n● Takedowns with no subsequent strikes/ground action are recorded for posterity.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"509abd69a570b4f36ed4a855c762622b7ca3dd0b04addb2fcfdc5b88e70f0b1c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":122,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.3","title":"Effective list control","body":"● Dominating the opponent by dictating pace, location, and position.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d04c67cad4b280b1234d8a9c80ea9136f8dfa236093052cd3db7c99a4a7ebb73","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":123,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.4","title":"Effective aggression","body":"● Pushing forward with attacks, landing legal strikes, and making attempts to finish the fight.\n● No credit for chasing without effective results or impact.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ac5a8ecae2d3a414376825bc82e86202826d27c815021ec17f468be63ba2d573","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":124,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.5","title":"Effective defense","body":"● Avoiding being struck, taken down, or reversed while countering with offensive attacks.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"74f993164e51030a738e7ab55af401859a456c4a641f2b6853c61c0e38364bf4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":125,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3","title":"Scoring breakdown","body":"","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"be642ca2c8ea3d0ad0425475e72fbfe1f9346222662a68afaf7c488de8e46a71","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":126,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3.1","title":"Round scores","body":"Each marshal reports the score for each round to the secretary. The secretary adds these scores together and divides the total by the number of marshals to calculate the Round Score.\n● 10-10: A round with a strike point difference of 5 or less, and a winner cannot be determined by using the other evaluation criteria (noted as “Even”).\n● 10-9: A round with a strike point difference of 5 or less, and a winner can be determined by using the other evaluation criteria (noted as “Even”).\n● 10-9: Competitor out-strikes opponent by 6 to 10 strike points (noted as 'Slight').\n● 10-8: Competitor out-strikes opponent by 11 to 15 strike points (noted as 'Moderate').\n● 10-7: Competitor out-strikes opponent by 16 or more strike points (noted as 'Dominant').KO and TKO both result in this score","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3a6eb2952ef1ed2dd135793f43c4f93bf4c4acd8193577a0da7c0bc89ff29931","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":127,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3.2","title":"Point deductions","body":"Yellow cards, armor malfunction penalties and weapon loss penalties result in a single point deduction for each instance. .","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"56c01e5081bf5b8a89b376c3fcc385d057dcc81ec8c29ef23f7ad4d17dc14d56","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":128,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3.3","title":"Example scenario","body":"If competitor A and competitor B have an evenly fought round until competitor B incurs an armor failure (fixed within the required time), competitor A would be awarded 10 points, and competitor B would be awarded 9 points due to the armor failure.","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f54249f49ce4aaad3f85318d3f4849f3605c74b986e28623015dbe5b18f09afc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":129,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.4","title":"Fight outcome","body":"","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fa4dfe51dab5bc81185855e4d3cb07c3451e92980a905173a293982ee2fc5e12","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":130,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.4.1","title":"Total Fight Score: The Total Fight Score is determined by adding up all the Round","body":"Scores to declare the winner of the match.\n● Tournaments: The Total Fight Score is ranging between 14 and 20.\n● Matched Fights: The Total Fight Score is ranging between 21 and 30.","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.4.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d57f9bc39a050decfa9bb5f2cbc0e1c68baad6a8a7a6fb29125f6f6dcde07f90","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":131,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.4.2","title":"Win types","body":"● Unanimous decision: All line marshals scored the win for the same competitor.\n● Unanimous draw: All line marshals score the fight as a draw.\n● Majority decision: The majority of line marshals scored the win for one competitor, and the other line marshal(s) scored the fight as a draw.\n● Majority draw: The majority of line marshals scored the fight as a draw.\n● Split decision: The majority of line marshals scored the win for one competitor, and the other line marshal(s) scored the win for the other competitor.\n\n● Split draw: All line marshals score the fight differently but the score totals all result in a draw.\n● Technical Knockout (TKO)\n● Knockout (KO)\n\nExample scoresheet\n\n[Line Marshal | Blue Corner\n\n| ROUND 1 | | ROUND 2 | | ROUND 3\n\nRound Counting and Observations\n\nTotal Effective Strikes Total Effective Takedowns Total Loss of Weapon Total Armour Failures Total Point Deduction\n\nCriteria by Priority Red Blue Red Blue Red 1(1) Effective Striking —— —— —— Dominant (6-10) ee (16>) (6-10) eel (16>) (6-10) el (16>) 1(2) Effective Grappling Red Blue Red Blue Red\n\n[(3) Effective List Control Red —— Blue Red —— Blue Red —\n\n| Be | |\n\nWin Criteria Effective strike total > Effective Grappling > Effective List Control> Effective Aggression > Effective Defence\n\nEven Difference in Effective Strikes is 5 or less. Follow Criteria by Priority until a Winner can be determined. (10-9) If a Winner can be determined, Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 9. (10-10) If no Winner can be determined, Round is a Draw. A Drawn Round is Scored 10 for both Fighters.\n{Slight (10-9) Difference in Effective Strikes from 6 to 10. Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 9.\n{Moderate (10-8) Difference in Effective Strikes from 11 to 15. Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 8.\n\n|Dominant (10-7) Difference in Effective Strikes from 16 or more. Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 7.\n\nPoint Deductions Yellow Card Any yellow card given to a fighter will result in a 1 Point Deduction to that fighters Round.\n\n|Loss of weapon When a fighter loses a weapon 3 or more times in a single round, this will result in a 1 Point Deduction to that fighters Round.\n\n{Armour Failure For each 90 seconds granted for Armour Failure Repair, 1 Point will be Deduction to that fighters Round.","page_from":28,"page_to":30,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.4.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.4","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"OCR could not read some words with confidence: eel, {Moderate, |Dominant, |Loss, {Armour","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c2df1fde6c439e199d25ced7f86eae30437719a03a0a4f04523d73181ddc89e5","has_figures":true,"extraction":"mixed"},{"ordinal":132,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"16","title":"Appeal","body":"","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c86f8b577d3b6534903631a2504e11692a70b30de693f8d2a7d681f27c4d2917","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":133,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.1","title":"Submission of an appeal","body":"The competitor or their corner men can appeal a decision made by the marshals committee or the knight marshal.\nThe appeal is submitted in written form The number of appeals are determined by the organizers.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"025f7ba3915d40a52c6999cb1a9f3fcbbaa8464320d377c9c07c9bac5235c754","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":134,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.2","title":"Grounds for appeal","body":"An appeal can be filed for various reasons, including:\n● False implementation of point deduction, warning, card, or disqualification.\n● Unregistered clean blows to legal strike zones affecting the fight.\n● Unregistered rule violations by the opponent warranting point deduction.\n● Unregistered rule violations warranting yellow or red cards or severe rule violations.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"97f902f798266a44c4420ba5eb5e1af0261f11a09c8184970281ae9d582be023","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":135,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.3","title":"Submission timing","body":"The competitor can appeal directly at the end of the fight when the knight marshal requests objections, before the competitor has left the list.\nThe competitor’s corner men observing the fight must announce the intention to appeal to the knight marshal in person no later than 15 minutes after the fight.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e1bc3fca2ab6546e5d3600ce80b0cc8683e2296241eaf7375d5dc9c0f1447921","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":136,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.4","title":"Possible results of the appeal","body":"● A general rematch of the round.\n● Imposing or withdrawal of cards.\n● Imposing or withdrawal of point deduction.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d5d44a449124578738b1e1fbfcb04453643516c243a1e8683f09f0c5ea1b3fd4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":137,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.5","title":"Further appeal","body":"If the competitor or their corner men are dissatisfied with the knight marshal's decision, they can appeal to the Buhurt International Control and Disciplinary Committee, or the Head of the Buhurt International Marshals’ Committee.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8e16e6902df5e573d69d14e62acff7145ad8fb002d7688bd941380b2ece7ded7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":138,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"17","title":"League Ranking Scoring","body":"All competitors start with a score of 100. The minimum possible points is 0, and the maximum possible points is 250.","page_from":32,"page_to":32,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:17","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"73f4f90513286c7975b1cb200fbc44ac25549d0714020d2e104fe7de0f086cb0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":139,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"17.1","title":null,"body":"Tier System:\n● Tier 5: 130 points and below\n● Tier 4: 130 to 160 points\n● Tier 3: 160 to 190 points\n● Tier 2: 190 to 220 points\n● Tier 1: 220 to 250 points (the maximum possible number of League points)\n\nSteps for Scoring:\n\n1. Compare Total Fight Scores:\n● Calculate the difference between the Total Fight Scores of the two competitors.\n● In Tournaments, the difference can range from 0 to 6 points.\n● In Matched Fights, the difference can range from 0 to 9 points.\n2. Weight Modifier:\n● If a competitor does not make weight, the competitor who made weight receives:\n○ +1 in Tournaments.\n○ +2 in Matched Fights.\n3. Tier Modifier:\n● Compare the tiers of the two competitors.\n● In Tournaments, award +1 to the lower-tier competitor for each tier difference.\n● In Matched Fights, award +2 to the lower-tier competitor for each tier difference.\n4. Calculate the Final Score:\n● Add the Total Fight Score, Weight Modifier, and Tier Modifier.\n● Note: The winner of a fight cannot earn a negative score.\n5. Division 2 Adjustment:\n● If the fight is in Division 2, divide the League Points Score by 2.\n6. Update Overall League Score:\n● Add the resulting score into the competitor’s Overall League Score.\n\nRequired Participation:\n\n● One Season:\nIf a competitor does not compete within a season, they will automatically drop to the next lowest tier at the midpoint value of that tier (e.g., Tier 1 drops to Tier 2 at 205 points).\n● Two Seasons:\nIf a competitor does not compete for two seasons, their score will automatically reset to 100 points.","page_from":32,"page_to":32,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:17.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:17","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"53487ec4523d74978dcea44d3e59b3a5fd2e785e7c20ed65c01ebf3c576c4a19","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":140,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"18","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules March 2025 (2024.06 to 2025.03) Clarification: 2.1 Senior knight marshal Clarification: 2.2 Knight marshal Replaced: 5.2 will not be allowed to participate further in the tournament || will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review Replaced: 6.2 will not be allowed to participate further in the tournament || will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review Clarification: 1.3 (explaining the tier 1, 2 method) Replaced: 15.3.2 that round at the discretion of the knight marshal || each instance\n\nNovember 2024 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2024.11) Update date: December-2024 -Correction:\nTier 2: 190 220 to 2250 points | Tier 2: 190 to 220 points Tier 1: 2250 to 2580 points | Tier 1: 220 to 250 points\n- Added: Total fight score:\n- Removed: Total fight score: Each line marshal calculates the total fight score for each competitor by adding their round scores.\n- Clarification: A clinch is the a standing position where fighters lock their upper bodies together with their arms situation of stance between competitors during the fight.\n- clarification: 13.Penalties: Only the Knight Marshal may issue these\n- clarification: 10.14 Fence interaction: hands / elbows\n- add: 6.3 Appeal Submission: in their opinion, an action or actions taken by the opponent or any marshal contradicts the rules. See Section 16\n- Refactor: Protest to appeal\n- Removed: 4.1 Single fights\n- Added: 4.1 Matched Fights\n- Clarification: 1.3 Divisions: and will be rewarded more League points for this format\n- Clarification: Open Weight category + This will not generate a Weight Modifier if agreed upon in advance\n- Clarification: The competitor can appeal is submitted directly at the end of the fight when the knight marshal requests objections, before the competitor has left the list.\n- Clarification 15.3.1 | 10-7 added: KO and TKO both result in this score\n- Change 1.3:\nDivision 1 is for competitors with more than 2 years of competitive experience, or competitors with demonstrable international experience.\nDivision 2 is for competitors with less than 2 years of competitive experience and with no, or minimal, international competitive experience.\nDivision 1 is for more experienced competitors Division 2 is for less experienced competitors, structured to be more forgiving to newcomers to the ruleset.\n- Add: 14.7\n● Medical TKO: If a competitor receives a Medical TKO (medical staff determines the competitor cannot continue), they are disqualified from continuing in the tournament.\n\n● Non-Medical TKO: If a competitor receives a TKO due to a lack of defense, they will lose a Round in Division 1 or a Match in Division 2.\n- Add: 17 League Ranking Scoring\n\nUpdate date: June-2024\n- format: Grammar adjustments throughout the document Update date: March-2024\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.\nUpdate date: April-2024\n- removed 11.4 Passivity in a Fight (duplicated in rules 10.14 Intentional Passivity)\n- clarification\n- clarification 14.8 Disqualification (page29)\n- clarification 14.9 Knockout (KO) (page 29)","page_from":33,"page_to":34,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:18","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["16","10.14"],"content_sha256":"39ace7d6744f9354a581236e640125f6c4114a8e165f8722d046b0c7fb3f14d0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/outrance-rules","version":{"version":"26.1","title":"Outrance Rules and Regulations 26.1","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Title and footer \"Outrance Rules and Regulations\"; cover \"VER. 26.1\". Version labels: \"2024.12\" style until 2025, then \"26.1\" = January 2026 (Duel Regulations change log: \"January 2026 (2025.02 to 2026.1)\"; Infractions: \"January - 2026 (V. 26.1)\").","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1C7KTLpIkNhWAabDtFLX0b0R12mYVJifA/view","source_sha256":"a5904a25fc5c9aaf06f38e07dfdf08370f4bfcd169ebed05d1698462263739d5","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":33,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8 + OCR (tesseract 5.3.4 psm4 300dpi) on 2 page(s) without a text layer","content_sha256":"1cdd963869dc15b3c0e7bda6074d72cf37e51223daf2be5072128efd7278dc45","detected":{"version":"26.1","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":2,"edition_evidence":"Title and footer \"Outrance Rules and Regulations\"; cover \"VER. 26.1\". Version labels: \"2024.12\" style until 2025, then \"26.1\" = January 2026 (Duel Regulations change log: \"January 2026 (2025.02 to 2026.1)\"; Infractions: \"January - 2026 (V. 26.1)\").","source_files":[{"file":"Marshal/Archive/Outrance Rules 26.1.pdf","archive":"Marshal","sha256":"a5904a25fc5c9aaf06f38e07dfdf08370f4bfcd169ebed05d1698462263739d5","drive_file_id":"1C7KTLpIkNhWAabDtFLX0b0R12mYVJifA"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["4 provision(s) need review against the official document"],"pages":33,"source_lines":879,"assigned_lines":1116,"furniture_lines":151,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99591,"provisions":141,"numbered":140,"needs_review":4,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":33,"picture_text_lines":2,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"VER. 26.1\n\nRules and Regulations Outrance rules and regulations","page_from":1,"page_to":2,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"86998757867185a475b69996624e173490f5fa66c02c3d9da57d2ae427bcdb7d","has_figures":true,"extraction":"mixed"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General provisions","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b4f55b0721414150889a4410e85c6e0e88af141e828fa703c7c8c6661d2ce077","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Types of fights","body":"Outrance fights may be held in two ways:","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"19ac942cb2a7e28918b5338959b582e607ca1c8402f0ff171ad5b1cf59edbf60","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.1","title":null,"body":"Matched fights: one single fight between 2 competitors.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.1.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e268dc9008ec91154fa155d20c6b74c358fdfc6e36f155c52f2c3099fcc80a7f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.2","title":null,"body":"Tournament: a series of fights between multiple competitors.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.1.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3795db96cb2361dc4e282417a23884570b755156a268ac3ed22bd6756336077f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Weight categories","body":"Outrance fights are held in different categories based on the weight of participants.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"faaa29fe71d03af042f4159c017440d99b0c0dd5c7053538f653b20731cb1896","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.1","title":"For men","body":"● Lightweight: Up to a maximum of 75 kg.\n● Middleweight: Over 75 kg up to a maximum of 85 kg.\n● Light Heavyweight: Over 85 kg up to a maximum of 95 kg.\n● Heavyweight: Over 95 kg up to a maximum of 105 kg.\n● Super Heavyweight: Over 105 kg up to a maximum of 115 kg.\n● Ultra Heavyweight: Over 115 kg.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c5f764a10c7ca5d1f00613cba1cf278887e7050baff5694fba117c09142b8a50","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.2","title":"For women","body":"● Featherweight: Up to a maximum of 60 kg.\n● Lightweight: Over 60 kg up to a maximum of 70 kg.\n● Middleweight: Over 70 kg up to a maximum of 80 kg.\n● Light Heavyweight: over 80 kg up to a maximum of 90 kg.\n● Heavyweight: over 90 kg.\n\nMen Women\n\nFeatherweight <60kg\n\nLightweight   <75kg   60 - 70 kg\n\nMiddleweight   75 - 85 kg   70 - 80 kg\n\nLight Heavyweight   85 - 95 kg   80 - 90 kg\n\nHeavyweight   95 -105 kg   >90 kg\n\nSuper Heavyweight 105 -115 kg\n\nUltra Heavyweight >115kg","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"74fd53dc413f5ae6ac32a7fae3b1834d24636e731ddc212a06857683a721f016","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.3","title":"Open Weight category","body":"Should both participants agree, there may be a difference in the weight of competitors not based on the previously mentioned weight categories. This will not generate a Weight Modifier if agreed upon in advance.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24c0e9472ba6717c364f5a6b0d4290296aa5c3bd2a3b330eaa565f8f65f474b6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.4","title":"Weigh-in procedure","body":"The weigh-in may be done up to 24 before the event starts up until the day of competition to assign competitors to the proper category. If a competitor misses the weigh-in, they may have to forfeit their fight or the tournament. They may attempt a second weigh in before the competition begins.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.2.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ca333911ef5662a4ab1359dfe7f8f2687bac47359426e010e7afce3044bd6ebe","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"Divisions","body":"Division 1 is for more experienced competitors and will be rewarded more League points for this format (Defined as fighters with over 2 years competitive experience or fighters with demonstrable international experience).\nDivision 2 is for less experienced competitors, structured to be more forgiving to newcomers to the ruleset. (Defined as fighters with under 2 years competitive experience and no or minimal international competitive experience).\nDivision 2 fighters can elect to fight in Division 1 should they choose to.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["2"],"content_sha256":"28353849e6e67fff70ad63df67844da2b623561b4c1fd054a2180fca4104207b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4","title":"Criteria for participation","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"edd00c26c8fa62226bfbe13f60e726ef0f3a3e8a7b0ff0dda90d9b5b35edcdcc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4.1","title":"Legal age","body":"Competitors must be of legal age according to the laws of both their country and the country in which the competition is held.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5507f8e1e4a9801c69d3cf8c0f06f5512a804c7dcd1abb7eb76ad2705dd09475","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4.2","title":"Medical fitness","body":"Competitors must declare themselves medically fit to fight before the competition.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"de75ce1b68b7a6e112ceef2deab16d0f98d96032c83f49aff64df00177da6bfe","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4.3","title":"Medical support","body":"Each competition should have professional medical support provided by the organizer of the event.\nIn case of an injury, members of the medical support team may decide to withdraw the injured competitor from competition.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:1.4.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:1.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"07e80c2c6cb89011da06ab0170a49000008bde0aae1a72ff1bbe9f6a4765f89c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Marshals committee","body":"During an event, it is allowed to combine some of the marshals’ duties, for example the duties of the timekeeper may be combined with the secretary, and technical marshal with any other duties (knight marshal, line marshal, etc.).\nA marshals committee should consist of:","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e32308a38003194e2d5b0583dbf8556f50f08f376c7fc5fd65775c4fcfaa15d0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"One (1) Head marshal","body":"The senior knight marshal:\n● is responsible for the work of the marshals committee during the competition,\n● takes the lead in the consideration by the Marshals Committee of any appeal submitted by competitors,\n● has the final say in all matters related to the consideration of said appeals, and in the interpretation of the rules,\n● Is responsible for reviewing circumstances related to competitor stoppage, cornerman stoppage and TKO stoppage,\n● Where only one knight marshal is present, they can perform the senior knight marshal duties.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"981818fd9131a6b0a623817648e22b7389c644a0f2bc669952585202232e7ef3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"One (1) knight marshal","body":"The knight marshal:\n● is responsible for checking the readiness of competitors, marshals, and timekeeper before the fight,\n● gives the command to start, suspend and stop the fight,\n● controls the course of the fight by:\n○ counting time of clinches, ○ reacting to breakages of armor and weapon, losses of weapon, use of unauthorized techniques, ○ assessing knockout (KO) and technical knockout (TKO) of competitors,\n● has the right to give verbal warnings, yellow and red cards (disqualification), and to expel corner men,\n● checks the condition of the list between the rounds of a fight,\n● announces the winner according to the result of points counted by the line marshals.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3581ee207a6bb89670aff6f0cb6b855cc14c5b4dc3c985d5c6d6abc818c90b19","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Three (3) or five (5) line marshals","body":"The line marshals:\n● review objectively all the actions made by both competitors during the fight,\n● take note of loss of weapons and armor failure,\n\n● each keep scores independently. They are not allowed to contact other line marshals during the round and should be located on different sides of the list.","page_from":7,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e112f7df1ed687216952b75724ff922066bfdbdd1b680d4368cef9dc0a2fe495","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"One (1) timekeeper","body":"The timekeeper:\n● counts down the time of each round of the fight and of each break between rounds,\n● counts down the time allotted for repairment/replacement of broken equipment,\n● announces the end of the round and the end of the break between rounds with the command ”Time” and the sound of a gong or similar device.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e89a6ed87c8584615a5d813381d37eba90a33c08c1ecaffa85b41d664956f587","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.5","title":"One (1) secretary","body":"The secretary:\n● records the results of each round of the fight based on points counted by the line marshals,\n● makes notes in the fight protocol. All yellow and red cards should be marked in the protocol for further calculations,\n● takes notes if any medical conditions forbids a competitor to continue fighting,\n● calls competitors to the list according to the order of the fights, in case there's no announcer/herald of the event.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"97071dc977933bfe41cc002e8306a0a250ead8ff900ef8a2a2e7a27870e633e5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.6","title":"One (1) technical marshal","body":"The technical marshal:\n● checks the safety of the offensive and defensive equipment of each competitor,\n● inspects the general appearance and historical accuracy of armor and weapon,\n● have the right to demand the replacement of a selected element of equipment if it does not meet requirements of safety, appearance, or historical accuracy,\n● checks the equipment before each fight, and after a fight if a competitor requests it.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"21bb961f594d735d778559542c072f94cee7dcccb64060e0d341d7a4201cc210","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.7","title":"One (1) video supervisor","body":"The video supervisor:\n● checks and reviews all appeals given to the knight marshal,\n● discusses and makes decisions on all appeals with the knight/head marshal.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:2.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2fa08ed8404251f85f8da7f69a208c6a4c7e0b72f9d33ec7def735fa7d19f82c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"General commands","body":"Commands reserved for the knight marshal","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f71b1f955f02c7cdc6fe6712829a77d5c1c54f33022bf14edfda1228b761fb19","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"“Fight”","body":"Purpose: Initializes the fight at the beginning of the round or after any suspension of the fight.\nUsage: Start or resume the fight.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9e45b65ec70d9a916631eb6dccfb76a3a503ad748f0f76a61d91a2069baf09f7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"“Stop fight”","body":"Purpose: Stops the fight at the end of the round or when the fight is finished due to KO (Knockout) or TKO (Technical Knockout).\nUsage: Conclude the fight.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3b9dc97224ea393412aa5865b5223dbea0b74721fa4f85450c7b71f591c00e77","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"“Break”","body":"Purpose: Pauses the fight and separates both competitors.\nUsage: Temporarily stops the fight, creating a break between the competitors.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"924bd548f9de9c4dfaa081266e7ab56494fc6a967a647cfebf50b722a7b800ed","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"“Hold”","body":"Purpose: Pauses the fight but holds competitors' positions for a re-arm of the weapon or to move both competitors to the middle of the list when needed.\nUsage: Temporarily halts the action, keeping the competitors in their current positions for specific adjustments.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"08d830c80ec51e119c6bc47a84459ef8548b23b082baf185fb40896100a81879","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"“Breakdown of weapon/armor”","body":"Purpose: Announces the breakdown of part of the equipment.\nUsage: After the “Break” command has been given, indicates a specific issue with a competitor's weapon or armor that requires attention.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"41a4cfe376a7997a01b3ee393462b4407646e08d345d499030c05de71d080b6b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.6","title":"“Loss of weapon”","body":"Purpose: Used when one of the competitors loses their weapon.\nUsage: After the “Hold” command has been given, indicates that a competitor has lost their weapon during the paused state.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"27798fe49e21aefc8c78c8d2e5b4660f0e63c4ef763d61056dde570c3ae88f3d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.7","title":"“Knockout”","body":"Purpose: Used when one of the competitors is subject to a KO or TKO and after the “Stop fight” command has been given.\nUsage: Declares the end of the fight due to a knockout or technical knockout.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0fa9f68bd5d618e969740a3fdafe0dbf1f91d159b7998976c0de470d878df8e6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.8","title":"“Time”","body":"Purpose: Announces the flow of time during the fight.\nUsage:\n● To signify the end of a round or the end of a break between rounds.\n● If there was a breakdown of equipment, and the competitor has been granted time to repair it.\n● This command keeps track of the time progression during the fight.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:3.8","parent_key":"outrance-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ba665144d3d651cc7b513268368310c9b24a07c18a66232fc68a92c0939f92c2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Fight procedures","body":"A fight against an opponent consists of multiple rounds. The time duration of rounds and breaks and the number of rounds in a fight depends on the tournament type and Division. Below are the number of rounds and the round time durations.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bd0c91ac9ce102cdc85aa144fb1b8be011d086cb3be95ebb8246a3d59b6dc3a8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Matched fights","body":"Matched fights are competitive “Matches” where opponents are paired based on factors like skill, weight, experience, or age to ensure fairness and balance in the contest.\n\nDivision 1:\n● 3 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds)\n● 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds) Division 2:\n● 3 rounds of 1 minute and 30 seconds (90 seconds)\n● 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds)","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:4.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1e1978b16670966b94b11719f42981d609435f9dd65983006402a48ef635ed88","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Tournament fights","body":"Division 1:\n● 2 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds)\n● 1 break of 45 seconds Division 2:\n● 2 rounds of 1 minute and 30 seconds (90 seconds)\n● 1 break of 45 seconds\n● If a tiebreaker round is needed. Use the same time as above\n\nMatched fights Tournament fights\n\nDivision 1 3 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds) 2 rounds of 2 minutes (120 seconds) 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds) 1 break of 45 seconds\n\nDivision 2 3 rounds of 1m30s (90 seconds) 2 rounds of 1m30s (90 seconds) 2 breaks of 1 minute (60 seconds) 1 break of 45 seconds\n\nImportant!\nFor tournament fights, if after two rounds the fight is a draw, a 3rd round will be fought.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:4.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:4","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0269c5fec00effe767820408a627010bdbbe0a079e06e0ca3d366e020411a100","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Competitors","body":"","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e3207a0ba88189b190d7e840fa8cd17cecedf7325a32cac518c1d7a2fa68a2f0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"Knowledge and respect of the rules","body":"All competitors are obligated to know the rules and regulations and to strictly obey them.\nThey shall obey commands given by the knight marshal.\nThey shall defend themselves at all times unless under the direct instruction of the knight marshal to “Stop Fight”, “Break” or “Hold”.\nThey shall be polite to other participants, marshals, and spectators.\nSwearing, rudeness, and other impolite actions may be penalized by the knight marshal with a verbal warning, yellow card, or even disqualification if they are persistent.\nIn the case above, actions taken outside the list, the knight marshal may demand penalizing them by the event organizer and/or League.\nAll competitors shall use a set of armor, weapon, and clothes that fulfill all technical safety requirements.\nThey shall come to the list within one (1) minute after being called by the herald/secretary/announcer of the event.\nThey should have a set of spare weapons and elements of armor, along with the necessary repair kit that allows making urgent repairs.\nEach competitor should have at least one (1) corner man. A competitor has a maximum of two\n(2) corner men.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"22b49d81ab498de451b093aec260a29aeeade9a62ab6f5986e45758c1f3c2b09","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"Competitor stoppage","body":"A competitor may stop the fight to yield during a round. They signal the knight marshal by throwing their weapon to the surface of the list and/or shouting “Stop fighting”.\nA competitor may forfeit before the fight has started because of:\n● Disqualification armor/weapon failure: The competitor is unable to continue the fight because of their damaged armor/weapon.\n● Medical retirement: The competitor is unable to continue the fight for a medical reason (e.g., injury).\nImportant!\nA competitor that yields or forfeits will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8fdbfac8b7e1136f102260d1d95095f454251b366e45712958b125ea0bffae81","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Appeal submission","body":"The competitor may submit an appeal to the marshals committee if, in their opinion, an action or actions taken by the opponent or any marshal contradicts the rules.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:5.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"11c495ba9d4d8293f9c9bc8af96b803086089dd39bfe8cc545090669f045972d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"6","title":"Corner support","body":"","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7ad0120d16aa8ae47c5fc116019e402797e46689352d9f7cdd4b6efd7b951c6e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.1","title":"Knowledge and respect of rules","body":"All corner men are obligated to know the rules and regulations and to strictly obey them.\nThey shall obey commands given by the knight marshal.\nThey shall help their competitor to the limits of the list and aid them in preparations before the fight.\nThey shall be ready during the fight to make repairs/exchanges of damaged equipment or weapons according to the Marshal's demands.\nThey shall only enter the list in the time between rounds or at the demand of the knight marshal to aid the competitor in repairing/exchanging damaged equipment.\nThey shall be polite to other participants, marshals, and spectators.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f6c8e5bf4b24e3ae0ad0d9450156977d7c8ef708c2299a30e18365ca06bcc610","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.2","title":"Right to demand stoppage","body":"A corner man has the right to demand to stop the fight. They signal the above demand by throwing a white towel/flag onto the surface of the list.\nThey have the right to demand to stop the fight in the following cases:\n● They recognize and accept the defeat of their competitor (TKO).\n● Their competitor is unable to continue fighting caused by the breakdown or loss of the element of their equipment (TKO armor/weapons failure).\n● The competitor is unable to continue the fight due to an injury or other medical causes (Medical Retirement).\nImportant !\nIf one of their corner men demand to stop the fight, the competitor will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review of corner men stoppage.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"382ff724c7652b61a080c251d04bcdba49486b5e593236374f086574a4505f20","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.3","title":"Appeal submission","body":"The corner man has the right to submit an appeal in the name of their competitor (if they cannot do it by themselves) if, in their opinion, an action or actions taken by the opponent or any marshal contradicts the rules. See Section 16","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:6.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["16"],"content_sha256":"e8ebf367dfcfd33df7b92ca4f8df978f36e460aa36ed5ff4fe5037dd11909c25","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"7","title":"List requirements","body":"","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e6051cb2c8ed6ec153e10cdbe0fb713927f4be536f4c587c32a17b21800a3e0b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.1","title":"Size","body":"The list can be made of any suitable rigid structure.\nWidth and Length: 5 meters minimum. 10 meters maximum","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75c40a09df78e340edf14f842e01454d64eaf7de7dc8a7aca772817aba609d4a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.2","title":"List fence","body":"Height: between 0.9 meter (minimum) and 1.3 meters (maximum).\nIt should prevent competitors from coming out of the list’s limits.\nIt should be visible.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"05df3bc9d71ba6a710b3e1e7b9b7baa91f4b107c2bfa8b31f2c3b7c6b393cd34","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.3","title":"List boundaries","body":"Boundaries of the lists should be properly seated on the ground.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7b390e7aed015fd92b457b0178a979765f4f0f6e0ebca4d5ef9d6fab02b203ba","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.4","title":"Surface quality","body":"The surface of lists should be dense and plain.\nIt should prevent competitors from slipping.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"20b53862e65b488b5c1b43350b188cb6185ef179c3985a6abc80b039dbdb2a51","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.5","title":"Lighting","body":"The light source should be located above the list.\nPositioned at a height that prevents competitors from being blinded by it.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"475587dcf937a30a9dad124fc0d75fe53f0f417f38142038e7c95afa5404a2ce","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.6","title":"Signalization tools","body":"It is recommended to place a white towel in the competitors’ corners for the corner men to use if they want to demand the stoppage of the fight.\nIt is recommended to make a clear and visible mark for the starting corner of each competitor.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"618d6b5de589c3a03dae7beed0958ec661eb7d9e2ce2792882fbb9b45224c320","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"7.7","title":"Safety zone","body":"The organizer must provide a 2m-wide safety zone by placing a barrier around every side of the list.\nOnly the marshals committee, the corner men, and accredited photo/videographers are permitted into the safety zone.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:7.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:7","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"edabb1365adfec42fc8ed7444841faec2ec956ba0ac1c454c90401783243d9e3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"8","title":"Authorized Equipment","body":"","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"496113a9bf833af881f77398b1f661869429b298a41f0628eb03be0b3182b7fb","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.1","title":"General requirements","body":"Technical and Authentic Compliance: all equipment must meet Buhurt International technical and authentic requirements.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c2a33aa57bffd4dd2212fa3416e3f2904006d88a8867af42924d3db0b277cb7b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":54,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.2","title":"Specifics on weapons and shields","body":"All Buhurt International weapons and shields are permitted.\nAny combination of these weapons is allowed.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b5d16a12999435d5aaacdcf80f49c4f65b99af51a8e6fed84710beb965f00cc3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":55,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.3","title":"Changes of equipment","body":"Participants are allowed to change elements of their equipment (armor or weapon) during intervals or due to breakage.\nThe supervision of the technical marshal is required for any change of equipment.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9547ab66402d5b6c8277ec3c1aed95f501f5c8d34553d5ef515b3b16cd27a1a7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":56,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"8.4","title":"Marshal authority","body":"The knight marshal and the technical marshal have the authority to demand changes to any element of armor or weapon for safety, aesthetic, or historical accuracy reasons.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:8.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"669e5d812acc64ba965a196e018973f027a1c33448ee85091a9548f29c4574e2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":57,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"9","title":"Authorized fighting techniques","body":"These rules aim to define a set of permitted and prohibited actions to ensure the safety of participants while engaging in combat. The guidelines cover striking, grabbing, and various techniques to maintain a fair and controlled environment during the event.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1861a2154f2bbcf34e37cc997c6643f96ef5b019a8e2929c7c33df875eddc258","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":58,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.1","title":"Permitted strikes","body":"Strikes are permitted with any part of the weapon, the shield, and with various body parts (arms, legs and head), whether standing or on the ground.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"463db0f2c4d6dc5f420f3e37e115cf0fdc213c676848695c010941c52f145953","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":59,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.2","title":"Permitted strike zones","body":"Strikes are allowed to any area not mentioned as a prohibited strike zone (See section 12 below).","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["12"],"content_sha256":"afc6275d61f3b495ee306879ae2f24a0208bf60c39f1b100a77c25d335ac68ce","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":60,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.3","title":"Weapon-grabbing","body":"Competitors are allowed to grab their own weapon and weapon blade with their hands.\nCompetitors are allowed to grab their opponent’s weapon (except by the blade) and shield with a free hand.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6e569761abb23e15a2f3c8ac06ebaee7357ee44260f7fd4f1fe5187ea9b63e28","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":61,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"9.4","title":"Techniques and moves","body":"Back heels, wrestling throws, and clinches are allowed.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:9.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:9","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0a2aaeee61085e518170add53a4f62b09ac68e73802b845bf174a1a03916c7b0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":62,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"10","title":"Prohibited fighting techniques","body":"These rules aim to ensure the safety, fairness, and adherence to a set of standards during the combat activities in the specified event.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e038657ba34ff935e5dd7db58723d75750050d961d2b268d63075fe5abc85ed5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":63,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.1","title":"Unlisted techniques","body":"Any actions not listed in section 9 of the rules are prohibited. Only authorized techniques are permitted.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["9"],"content_sha256":"d8994506e8d786f7579b262eef87d77ad2ae6a9938f3bd29c329f8e06e782391","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":64,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.2","title":"Thrusting actions","body":"Any thrusting actions with a weapon are prohibited. Threats of a thrusting action are also prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b66e09919729cecf191266007dd5da0dc963a9e438f0326ccb2cd867f494bbea","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":65,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.3","title":"Offensive actions at prohibited strike zones","body":"Any offensive actions aimed at any prohibited strike zones (See section 12 below) are prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["12"],"content_sha256":"730568cb565ffb6ab736923a995264760a67ac6fd08df2c7e97fce2def652688","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":66,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.4","title":"Actions with foot or shin at the knee","body":"Actions with the foot or shin aimed at the knee are prohibited. This includes actions that may cause the knee to hyperextend, such as push kicks to the thigh.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bdd2a1a56805d323c07108ff30e7071129601f687c1135fe76bd417d614bcc05","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":67,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.5","title":"Grappling and holding","body":"Grappling and holding with the hand on specific armor elements (aventail, edge of pauldrons, edge of the helmet), pushes on the bottom edge of the helmet, neck cranks, and subsequent neck twists are prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ebad01195a93f387d5e46c0e36c4bcf77c629161fc186e2efafafbd15649744a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":68,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.6","title":"Suffocation techniques","body":"Grips, clamps, suffocation techniques with direct pressure on the neck using any part of the body, equipment, or weapon are prohibited. A poorly fitted helmet does not count as a suffocating technique.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3af2ba155c4db337d42c3b28a45a5bde742afe0268d0d09fbb1c14d96d931ca2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":69,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.7","title":"Joint locks and hyperextension","body":"Arm lock techniques, leg lock techniques and any actions that may cause a limb to hyperextend are prohibited.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2f243cce25ae6a960f48d0a4e436f841b4867f51c7c63c5cc7302b78bf37d037","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":70,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.8","title":"Specific strikes","body":"Strikes with the head of a one-handed axe are prohibited if the grip of the hand on the shaft is less than 30cm away from the axe’s head.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.8","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5bad418b26eee2070ef7b7cb03bbaf02324f2a792d23ed2438137d316277ef7f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":71,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.9","title":"Armor tampering","body":"Deliberate attempts to remove any elements of the armor are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.9","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6b7b4ea932304fb1d125dae460a9fc74d04c24e15a052ed844524e3bfb7dc0ca","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":72,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.10","title":"Strikes to a disarmed opponent","body":"Strikes to an opponent who has lost their weapon are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.10","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"84b9084515fcabc21f3c37ddcf2dfe4e6b38f8ff6cfe6bac0bf125d0a77129a9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":73,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.11","title":"Strikes to a grounded opponent","body":"Foot and shin strikes to a grounded opponent are prohibited.\nKnee strikes to a grounded opponent’s legs or head are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.11","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"28510dc32cc2d677ab083007345ed4951f141e36aa4a3e419995cd621cfafd5d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":74,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.12","title":"Dangerous take downs","body":"Any takedown that forces an opponent to land on their head/neck and suplex (arch throws) variations are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.12","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"085ebf40e5c0bd61a4dbe650ef7e85ee52df6e2ea86e68d2f5c5868b21f64416","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":75,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.13","title":"Out-of-bounds actions","body":"Intentional pushing or throwing an opponent out of the designated fighting area (list) is prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.13","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e2b8a8baa47db4ddca50f5322e8801fdc13e3f4fc4b38bcc098115653025efb9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":76,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.14","title":"Fence interaction","body":"Grabbing the fence and resting with hands/elbows above the fence is prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.14","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ab8a7a6166cb42684eaa12269fce4aaff1c79d3d26d4b3c80597de9346b0c5d8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":77,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.15","title":"Eye protection","body":"Attacks that may penetrate the eye slits of the opponent's helmet are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.15","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3da3ab854ee4291c286626b6694062a7dea988d41fb8b178bf983649cac847ab","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":78,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.16","title":"Intentional passivity","body":"Intentional passivity and stalling of the action are prohibited.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.16","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"84300c0852731b2133834b04875369a637fe4e63bca744c477fd61f932ad3c66","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":79,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"10.17","title":"Assistance after a break","body":"A competitor cannot purposefully push on their opponent to get up off the ground after a \"Break\" or \"Stop fight\" command.","page_from":18,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:10.17","parent_key":"outrance-rules:10","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a8c2c2232fc5989d49bf3f959587bbde6e8e0d2816ef8a418c1d2449a0ea3e1d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":80,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"11","title":"Other prohibited actions","body":"These rules contribute to maintaining the integrity, safety, and orderliness of the event. They cover aspects such as participants behavior, substance use, adherence to commands, and respect for officials and other attendees. The role of the knight marshal is highlighted in several instances, emphasizing their authority and responsibility in ensuring the proper conduct of the event.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9be680ebc896e3803ef470fdd8ec40c885159bcb77c63485cc641e9e9db5d444","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":81,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.1","title":"Leaving the list","body":"Intentional leaving of the list after the command “Start fight” and before the announcement of the results of the fight is prohibited. Permission to leave must be granted by the knight marshal.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b427588b2dfd29cee4ee03ede09d61fb8133e0a99aa386985fa699d4676a2b4d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":82,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.2","title":"Equipment and weapon approval","body":"Competitors are not allowed to use any part of the equipment or any weapon that hasn't been allowed by the technical marshal.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"479bb988a530a3044a7e3dc1eef83e813bd4d52169f82949ef553386d11edea2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":83,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.3","title":"Substance use","body":"Competitors are not allowed to be under the influence of alcohol or any psychoactive substances.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a9c911e3f8f27bacca5d368c5d24c77d8e5408e040ad7d85cb6357bbc3f8cec5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":84,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.4","title":"Stalling after commands","body":"Intentionally stalling for time after a “Break” or “Hold” command has been given is prohibited. The knight marshal will issue a warning, and if the competitor is not ready after the warning, a 5-second count will be initiated. If the count reaches 5 seconds, the fight will be stopped, and a TKO win will be awarded to the opposing competitor.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"90a3daed5161e14ada783a079e501aba9006f723a75b7168b6103eeebd3e2193","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":85,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.5","title":"Offensive actions against others participants","body":"Any offensive actions against marshals, corner men, spectators, or anyone else other than the current opponent are prohibited.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2c86702d3e4dc933998828a44433aca54faa0875f760dd1bc1593ca572a4970b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":86,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"11.6","title":"Event interference","body":"Any actions made by a competitor or their corner men that may impede the course of the event are prohibited.","page_from":19,"page_to":19,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:11.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:11","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"844b31352bb827d5b9dc20ae011be50e76d9c05c98828c63a9e13aee59000b0f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":87,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"12","title":"Prohibited strike zones","body":"These rules are designed to prioritize the safety of the participants by prohibiting strikes to vulnerable and potentially dangerous areas. Their overall intention is to prevent serious injuries and ensure a fair and safe competition.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4c9b2a336f776e1d79d4a09b44ef0fc88d57675bb2d6a8e26126dcd7b5a41af6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":88,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.1","title":"Back and front of the neck","body":"Strikes to the back and front of the neck are prohibited.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ba5b4d19d67dbc00da3a0d862ce3f42233a188c52db100966e34beed9fcc9d51","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":89,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.2","title":"Base of the skull","body":"Strikes to the base of the skull are prohibited.\nThe base of the skull is defined as the bottom third of the back of the helmet.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0ac383a5ab2ee6d4111ddd671247ec3713532cbfe465348ad6d3b0c1e8e67820","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":90,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.3","title":"Back of the knee","body":"Strikes to the back of the knee are prohibited.\nPlacing pressure to the back of the knee is prohibited.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fe6d30aad8e67c65b4e0d14636bd36943630ca300bb1a6af7effd36692fdc75f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":91,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.4","title":"Groin and crotch","body":"Strikes to the groin and crotch are prohibited.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b0967807713ead468ffecca5a927a47cdc2a1f0234a4d2655712796ab9d7e65f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":92,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.5","title":"Foot and ankle","body":"Strikes to the feet and ankles are prohibited. However, striking the foot is not considered a prohibited strike if the competitor raises their foot while the strike is already occurring.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8b10bd12f1d9be3f9cba59d1431feb1c364e4d7fcc5f5d2d6ae4ce0d4f40afa5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":93,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.6","title":"Unprotected body parts","body":"Any part of the opponent’s body that has lost its protection is considered a prohibited strike zone.","page_from":20,"page_to":20,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bbb308732796487926d50b26501bfc6a6a4ad01e5f9b8c76c44f714af30bdb1b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":94,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"12.7","title":"Illustration of prohibited strikes zones","body":"","page_from":21,"page_to":21,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:12.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:12","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a8e6c1314e0cdd5061f5ccbf82d33826bd9941f9dc31bf92e6822464b17289b8","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":95,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"13","title":"Penalties","body":"These penalties are designed to maintain the integrity of the event, enforce the rules, and ensure a fair and safe competition. The progression from verbal warnings to yellow cards and potential disqualification emphasizes the seriousness of rule violations. Only the Knight Marshal may issue these","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"997a8550099ede83a4b331caa1222142b33d1840d88936d0825c64bd1fcf0db0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":96,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.1","title":"Verbal warning","body":"A verbal warning is given to a competitor or a corner man for a minor rule violation that does not significantly impact the course of the fight.\nIt serves as an alert that more serious actions will be taken if the violation is repeated.\nVerbal warnings do not have to be recorded in the protocol.\n3 verbal warnings will result in escalation to a yellow card.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2163118158cc9b73ea83ff01133e9db2779ba3505677d1d2cb5f1d9dd6e37717","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":97,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.2","title":"Yellow card","body":"Given by the knight marshal to a competitor or a corner man for systematic violations of the rules or for a violation that had a serious impact on the fight.\nYellow cards are recorded in the protocol and considered in the final score of the fight.\nThe knight marshal should point their hand in the direction of the competitor while announcing \"Yellow card”.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3caec1c9c3b0976f2ddee8374597c275c561b88afeda7a6243af099d20c90f49","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":98,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.3","title":"Expulsion of a corner man","body":"The knight marshal has the authority to expel a corner man for systematic violations of the rules or for a violation that had a serious impact on the fight.\nThe decision is noted in the protocol but does not affect the score of the fight.\nIf a competitor had only one (1) corner man, another person should be appointed immediately to take their position.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4d768c83b60dc32e6949ad34699c6e343f0f0b19572d1a2e1ae6c566c50b8f8e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":99,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"13.4","title":"Red card (disqualification)","body":"A red card equals a disqualification and is automatically given to a competitor who receives a second yellow card.\nIt may also be given if action(s) by the competitor or their corner man disrupt the course of the fight to the extent that it cannot continue or properly start.\nRed cards are recorded in the protocol.\nThe marshal should point their hand in the direction of the competitor while announcing “Red card” or “Disqualification”.","page_from":22,"page_to":22,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:13.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:13","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"773f40aaf3900eea21db6e1cba1166816aef78e58cb55f9484f88967a18c7fe8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":100,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"14","title":"Special situations","body":"","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"773ddf8e456ee306693d5fb0ed1dfd2dc8e565c1f917573fda9a0f611d56dc48","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":101,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.1","title":"Weapon loss","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with the “Hold” command.\n● Both competitors cease fighting, remain in position.\n● The knight marshal rearms the competitor and resets both competitors.\n● The knight marshal gives the “Fight” command.\nImportant note:\nWhen a fighter loses a weapon 3 or more times in a single round, this will result in a one (1) point deduction to the fighter's round. (see section 15.3.2 below) If a competitor loses their weapon more than twice during a round, they are deducted one (1) point off their round score (see section 15.3.2 below).","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["15.3.2"],"content_sha256":"a318d69a3ec618f1f65e6c0ec05b6c541b4f47895ac73e26919a9b08734025e7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":102,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.2","title":"Weapon breakage","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with the “Break” command.\n● The competitor must replace the weapon with a new one that was accepted by the technical marshal during the preparation of the fight.\n● If a replacement is impossible, victory is given to the opponent by TKO armor/weapon failure.\n● If a replacement is done, the fight continues with no penalty.","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"988c7976d51620eb6ac99af66c91e1c68fd5ce000a783f68635434b38967a204","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":103,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.3","title":"Armor failure","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with the “Break” command.\n● If the competitor, with the help of their corner men, can fix their armor in 90 seconds or less, they are deducted one (1) point off their round score (see section 15.3.2 below).\n● If they are unable to fix their armor in 90 seconds or less, they may be granted 90 additional seconds. They are deducted one (1) additional point off their round score (see section 15.3.2 below).\n● If they are still unable to fix the armor within the additional 90 seconds, their opponent is awarded the victory by TKO armor/weapon failure.","page_from":23,"page_to":23,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["90","15.3.2"],"content_sha256":"3322b4cc1b04b3c16cfbbf98751681dfcc441b8a775bb2cbec688974c04b71e4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":104,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.4","title":"Clinch","body":"A clinch is a standing position where fighters lock their upper bodies together with their arms between competitors during the fight.\nProcedure:\n● If the clinch is inactive for 10 seconds, the knight marshal stops the fight with the “Break” command.\n● Both competitors separate, and after the \"Fight\" command, they continue the fight.","page_from":24,"page_to":24,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0e4411d50e1e2587f902cab80d8cb18dda3cce377d164cf92fbd91f00dd7419c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":105,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.5","title":"Unintentional fall outside or under the list","body":"Procedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight with a \"Hold\" command.\n● Both competitors return to the middle of the list in the same position as when the \"Hold\" command was given.\n● \"Fight\" command is given to resume the fight.","page_from":24,"page_to":24,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3bd235d41c05949a2cce6ee44e7dc316cc6b75651ae620f7cdaad2e385569bb1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":106,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.6","title":"Grounded position","body":"A grounded position is a situation when a competitor has more than just the soles of their feet touching the ground. This includes hands, knees, back or their buttocks. One or both competitors can be in a grounded position simultaneously. The action is permitted to continue for 30 seconds providing that the action is consistent.\nProcedure:\n● The knight marshal stops the fight after 10 seconds of inactivity with the \"Break\" command.\n● Both competitors take a standing position about 3 meters apart and wait for the knight marshal's command to resume the fight.\n● A fallen competitor may take any actions to protect themselves (excluding prohibited actions).","page_from":24,"page_to":24,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.6","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e8a06106eab90678ca71b320db273cb2f26646ca13647d7e8c25069f3b930f15","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":107,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.7","title":"Technical knockout (TKO)","body":"Procedure:\n● Determination by the knight marshal: The knight marshal, as the official overseeing the fight, is responsible for determining if a fighter is no longer able to intelligently defend themselves.\n● Verbal warning: If the knight marshal observes that a fighter is unable to intelligently defend themselves, they will issue a verbal warning to the fighter.\n● 5-Second count: Following the verbal warning, the knight marshal will initiate a 5-second count, during which the fighter must demonstrate the ability to intelligently defend themselves.\n\n● Continuous lack of defense: If, after the 5-second count, the fighter continues to be unable to intelligently defend themselves, the knight marshal will intervene.\n● “Stop fight” announcement: At this point, the knight marshal will call for the fight to be stopped.\n● Declaration of TKO: Following the stoppage of the fight, the knight marshal will officially declare a Technical Knockout (TKO) by announcing \"Knockout.\"\n\n● TKO: If a competitor receives a TKO due to a lack of defense, they will lose the Match in Division 1 or the round in Division 2. All TKO’s must be checked by Medic to verify they can continue to fight","page_from":24,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.7","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9d7d30a84c10d726925ac6ac554fa6f53cc4e4a3d8ee323093ca9b37581994e7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":108,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8","title":"Intelligent defending","body":"","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3dda9eade07955e14fa30daa22bf6c0a7531a34ddda6be8a68ec367e9188d680","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":109,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.1","title":"Movement and positioning","body":"● Employing footwork to maintain distance from the opponent.\n● Utilizing angles and lateral movement to create advantageous positions.\n● Controlling the center of the fighting space to dictate the pace and direction of the engagement.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"dcbff9428353d31f634978660c03e0f4923291c8444b335c7d47e89b6c5a79ac","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":110,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.2","title":"Technique","body":"● Blocking or parrying strikes with proper technique to minimize impact.\n● Executing defensive maneuvers such as slips, rolls, and evasions to avoid incoming attacks.\n● Understanding defensive principles specific to different martial arts or combat sports.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"48f96c05f02637388e562ec267833b3bc27ba31cb1607de3298ac54dab2fb23f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":111,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.3","title":"Counterattacking opportunities","body":"● Identifying openings in the opponent's defense to launch effective counterattacks.\n● Capitalizing on the opponent's mistakes or vulnerabilities to turn the tide of the fight.\n● Using feints and baiting techniques to provoke reactions and create offensive opportunities.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a98657fd8a0a74e2e0ffcfd7956d21b38fac6992c7fc6db3c4c1a0ced8467087","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":112,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"14.8.4","title":"Composure and adaptability","body":"● Staying calm and focused under pressure to make sound defensive decisions.\n● Analyzing the opponent's movements and adjusting defensive strategies accordingly.\n● Being adaptable to changing circumstances and adjusting tactics as the fight progresses.","page_from":25,"page_to":25,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.8.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14.8","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"731cfd9d418fe920e0bf688262dc307f4d2f4667879b9fa6fa5cb3e977c48732","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":113,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.9","title":"Disqualification","body":"Disqualification occurs when a competitor is unable to continue fighting due to:\n● No available weapon or armor breakage that can not be repaired in the given time.\n● Disqualification also includes a fighter that has received a red card.\n\nImportant!\nShould a fighter be subject to a disqualification due to no available weapon or armor breakage, they will have until their next match to fix the issue or be completely disqualified from the Tournament","page_from":25,"page_to":26,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.9","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d831cb858b40e64beee6ea0a821c0ec9652dac2aa6525332d7c426a2c114f7e1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":114,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"14.10","title":"Knockout (KO)","body":"knockout occurs when a fighter is rendered unconscious and unable to continue fighting.\nThe knight marshal will announce “Stop Fight” then “Knockout”.\nImportant!\nShould a fighter lose a fight by KO, they will not be allowed to participate further in the tournament.","page_from":26,"page_to":26,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:14.10","parent_key":"outrance-rules:14","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d63e110239d2d1cba996d2dd14a8f262715052ee916a9d61194ee21ce133bbf8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":115,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"15","title":"Scoring the fight","body":"","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"264d62ce1bfa92461f3410e2c92acca94b5af9c1e5c5cecb8310366bab7cac8e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":116,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.1","title":"Scoring system overview","body":"","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"55266ab230144035ad1977f027524a6713f2cdd3f94d8857f38762ea4ed687d5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":117,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.1.1","title":"Number of line marshals","body":"3 or 5 line marshals evaluate each bout from different locations around the list/fighting area.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.1.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bdaa7d7664f8f9334074f338ed756c48d6e6cad609a536b0b467c5fb8503bcd1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":118,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.1.2","title":"Scoring system","body":"The “10-Point Must System” is the standard for scoring bouts.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.1.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"18489a91bf3080b7fe5c231d372528655a6b7710083599c41a8d7d2b3957d398","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":119,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2","title":"Evaluation criteria (in order of priority)","body":"","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"62a15857a695c2cd6eef1a23592d4a35568b2ad88a3b36ceed4c156460aa0dcc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":120,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.1","title":"Effective striking","body":"● Clear, strong, and well-placed legal strikes to permitted zones.\n● All legal strikes with weapons, legs, arms, and shields account for one (1) strike point per clean landed blow.\n● Strikes with the head do not award any strike point.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3d635b3e672f704e575cc3fcb95211203de55e0d8113ab0dd2250c191389cf65","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":121,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.2","title":"Effective grappling","body":"● Successful legal takedowns, position reversals, and clinch control.\n● Consideration for takedowns from standing position to dominant position, reversal of position, and positional clinch work.\n● Takedowns with no subsequent strikes/ground action are recorded for posterity.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"509abd69a570b4f36ed4a855c762622b7ca3dd0b04addb2fcfdc5b88e70f0b1c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":122,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.3","title":"Effective list control","body":"● Dominating the opponent by dictating pace, location, and position.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d04c67cad4b280b1234d8a9c80ea9136f8dfa236093052cd3db7c99a4a7ebb73","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":123,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.4","title":"Effective aggression","body":"● Pushing forward with attacks, landing legal strikes, and making attempts to finish the fight.\n● No credit for chasing without effective results or impact.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ac5a8ecae2d3a414376825bc82e86202826d27c815021ec17f468be63ba2d573","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":124,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.2.5","title":"Effective defense","body":"● Avoiding being struck, taken down, or reversed while countering with offensive attacks.","page_from":27,"page_to":27,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.2.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"74f993164e51030a738e7ab55af401859a456c4a641f2b6853c61c0e38364bf4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":125,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3","title":"Scoring breakdown","body":"","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"be642ca2c8ea3d0ad0425475e72fbfe1f9346222662a68afaf7c488de8e46a71","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":126,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3.1","title":"Round scores","body":"Each marshal reports the score for each round to the secretary. The secretary adds these scores together and divides the total by the number of marshals to calculate the Round Score.\n● 10-10: A round with a strike point difference of 5 or less, and a winner cannot be determined by using the other evaluation criteria (noted as “Even”).\n● 10-9: A round with a strike point difference of 5 or less, and a winner can be determined by using the other evaluation criteria (noted as “Even”).\n● 10-9: Competitor out-strikes opponent by 6 to 10 strike points (noted as 'Slight').\n● 10-8: Competitor out-strikes opponent by 11 to 15 strike points (noted as 'Moderate').\n● 10-7: Competitor out-strikes opponent by 16 or more strike points (noted as 'Dominant').KO and TKO both result in this score","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3a6eb2952ef1ed2dd135793f43c4f93bf4c4acd8193577a0da7c0bc89ff29931","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":127,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3.2","title":"Point deductions","body":"Yellow cards, armor malfunction penalties and weapon loss penalties result in a single point deduction for each instance. .","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"56c01e5081bf5b8a89b376c3fcc385d057dcc81ec8c29ef23f7ad4d17dc14d56","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":128,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.3.3","title":"Example scenario","body":"If competitor A and competitor B have an evenly fought round until competitor B incurs an armor failure (fixed within the required time), competitor A would be awarded 10 points, and competitor B would be awarded 9 points due to the armor failure.","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.3.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f54249f49ce4aaad3f85318d3f4849f3605c74b986e28623015dbe5b18f09afc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":129,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"15.4","title":"Fight outcome","body":"","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fa4dfe51dab5bc81185855e4d3cb07c3451e92980a905173a293982ee2fc5e12","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":130,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.4.1","title":"Total Fight Score: The Total Fight Score is determined by adding up all the Round","body":"Scores to declare the winner of the match.\n● Tournaments: The Total Fight Score is ranging between 14 and 20.\n● Matched Fights: The Total Fight Score is ranging between 21 and 30.","page_from":28,"page_to":28,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.4.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d57f9bc39a050decfa9bb5f2cbc0e1c68baad6a8a7a6fb29125f6f6dcde07f90","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":131,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"15.4.2","title":"Win types","body":"● Unanimous decision: All line marshals scored the win for the same competitor.\n● Unanimous draw: All line marshals score the fight as a draw.\n● Majority decision: The majority of line marshals scored the win for one competitor, and the other line marshal(s) scored the fight as a draw.\n● Majority draw: The majority of line marshals scored the fight as a draw.\n● Split decision: The majority of line marshals scored the win for one competitor, and the other line marshal(s) scored the win for the other competitor.\n\n● Split draw: All line marshals score the fight differently but the score totals all result in a draw.\n● Technical Knockout (TKO)\n● Knockout (KO)\n\nExample scoresheet\n\n[Line Marshal | Blue Corner\n\n| ROUND 1 | | ROUND 2 | | ROUND 3\n\nRound Counting and Observations\n\nTotal Effective Strikes Total Effective Takedowns Total Loss of Weapon Total Armour Failures Total Point Deduction\n\nCriteria by Priority Red Blue Red Blue Red 1(1) Effective Striking —— —— —— Dominant (6-10) ee (16>) (6-10) eel (16>) (6-10) el (16>) 1(2) Effective Grappling Red Blue Red Blue Red\n\n[(3) Effective List Control Red —— Blue Red —— Blue Red —\n\n| Be | |\n\nWin Criteria Effective strike total > Effective Grappling > Effective List Control> Effective Aggression > Effective Defence\n\nEven Difference in Effective Strikes is 5 or less. Follow Criteria by Priority until a Winner can be determined. (10-9) If a Winner can be determined, Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 9. (10-10) If no Winner can be determined, Round is a Draw. A Drawn Round is Scored 10 for both Fighters.\n{Slight (10-9) Difference in Effective Strikes from 6 to 10. Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 9.\n{Moderate (10-8) Difference in Effective Strikes from 11 to 15. Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 8.\n\n|Dominant (10-7) Difference in Effective Strikes from 16 or more. Round to be Scored, Winner 10, Opponent 7.\n\nPoint Deductions Yellow Card Any yellow card given to a fighter will result in a 1 Point Deduction to that fighters Round.\n\n|Loss of weapon When a fighter loses a weapon 3 or more times in a single round, this will result in a 1 Point Deduction to that fighters Round.\n\n{Armour Failure For each 90 seconds granted for Armour Failure Repair, 1 Point will be Deduction to that fighters Round.","page_from":28,"page_to":30,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:15.4.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:15.4","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"OCR could not read some words with confidence: eel, {Moderate, |Dominant, |Loss, {Armour","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c2df1fde6c439e199d25ced7f86eae30437719a03a0a4f04523d73181ddc89e5","has_figures":true,"extraction":"mixed"},{"ordinal":132,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"16","title":"Appeal","body":"","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c86f8b577d3b6534903631a2504e11692a70b30de693f8d2a7d681f27c4d2917","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":133,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.1","title":"Submission of an appeal","body":"The competitor or their corner men can appeal a decision made by the marshals committee or the knight marshal.\nThe appeal is submitted in written form The number of appeals are determined by the organizers.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"025f7ba3915d40a52c6999cb1a9f3fcbbaa8464320d377c9c07c9bac5235c754","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":134,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.2","title":"Grounds for appeal","body":"An appeal can be filed for various reasons, including:\n● False implementation of point deduction, warning, card, or disqualification.\n● Unregistered clean blows to legal strike zones affecting the fight.\n● Unregistered rule violations by the opponent warranting point deduction.\n● Unregistered rule violations warranting yellow or red cards or severe rule violations.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"97f902f798266a44c4420ba5eb5e1af0261f11a09c8184970281ae9d582be023","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":135,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.3","title":"Submission timing","body":"The competitor can appeal directly at the end of the fight when the knight marshal requests objections, before the competitor has left the list.\nThe competitor’s corner men observing the fight must announce the intention to appeal to the knight marshal in person no later than 15 minutes after the fight.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.3","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e1bc3fca2ab6546e5d3600ce80b0cc8683e2296241eaf7375d5dc9c0f1447921","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":136,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.4","title":"Possible results of the appeal","body":"● A general rematch of the round.\n● Imposing or withdrawal of cards.\n● Imposing or withdrawal of point deduction.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.4","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d5d44a449124578738b1e1fbfcb04453643516c243a1e8683f09f0c5ea1b3fd4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":137,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"16.5","title":"Further appeal","body":"If the competitor or their corner men are dissatisfied with the knight marshal's decision, they can appeal to the Buhurt International Control and Disciplinary Committee, or the Head of the Buhurt International Marshals’ Committee.","page_from":31,"page_to":31,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:16.5","parent_key":"outrance-rules:16","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8e16e6902df5e573d69d14e62acff7145ad8fb002d7688bd941380b2ece7ded7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":138,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"17","title":"League Ranking Scoring","body":"All competitors will be tracked via win/loss record.","page_from":32,"page_to":32,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:17","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8d6ddb0e5f12c9fba8cd3d5f88eaad7beeb45fa7d0ed0910a25b39fb2f2cc959","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":139,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"17.1","title":null,"body":"Competitors will be compared via their win/loss within their active weight category.","page_from":32,"page_to":32,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:17.1","parent_key":"outrance-rules:17","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1de4fc45573c2d73366b4ba1021078676695ae3da7b5c71d8c21e9d5b0981fcd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":140,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"17.2","title":null,"body":"If a competitor does not compete for 1 year their ranking will be shifted to “retired” status. If they do not compete for 2 years their ranking and record will be deleted from the standings.","page_from":32,"page_to":32,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:17.2","parent_key":"outrance-rules:17","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1e544b4a75fff41b4a4bf058b5bd4f9a8a9d1ba6f8410e9e580ded7d706b3564","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":141,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"18","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules January 2026 (2025.03 to 2026.1) Replaced: 1.2.4 The weigh-in may be done up to 24 before the event starts up until the day of competition to assign competitors to the proper category. If a competitor misses the weigh-in, they may have to forfeit their fight or the tournament. They may attempt a second weigh in before the competition begins.\nAdd: 4.2 If a tiebreaker round is needed. Use the same time as above Add: 14.6 30 seconds Remove: 14.6 indefinitely Remove: 17 Add: 17\n\nMarch 2025 (2024.06 to 2025.03) Clarification: 2.1 Senior knight marshal Clarification: 2.2 Knight marshal Replaced: 5.2 will not be allowed to participate further in the tournament || will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review Replaced: 6.2 will not be allowed to participate further in the tournament || will need to be assessed to verify their ability to continue. This may include medical review and senior knight marshal review Clarification: 1.3 (explaining the tier 1, 2 method) Replaced: 15.3.2 that round at the discretion of the knight marshal || each instance\n\nNovember 2024 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2024.11) Update date: December-2024 -Correction:\nTier 2: 190 220 to 2250 points | Tier 2: 190 to 220 points Tier 1: 2250 to 2580 points | Tier 1: 220 to 250 points\n- Added: Total fight score:\n- Removed: Total fight score: Each line marshal calculates the total fight score for each competitor by adding their round scores.\n\n- Clarification: A clinch is the a standing position where fighters lock their upper bodies together with their arms situation of stance between competitors during the fight.\n- clarification: 13.Penalties: Only the Knight Marshal may issue these\n- clarification: 10.14 Fence interaction: hands / elbows\n- add: 6.3 Appeal Submission: in their opinion, an action or actions taken by the opponent or any marshal contradicts the rules. See Section 16\n- Refactor: Protest to appeal\n- Removed: 4.1 Single fights\n- Added: 4.1 Matched Fights\n- Clarification: 1.3 Divisions: and will be rewarded more League points for this format\n- Clarification: Open Weight category + This will not generate a Weight Modifier if agreed upon in advance\n- Clarification: The competitor can appeal is submitted directly at the end of the fight when the knight marshal requests objections, before the competitor has left the list.\n- Clarification 15.3.1 | 10-7 added: KO and TKO both result in this score\n- Change 1.3:\nDivision 1 is for competitors with more than 2 years of competitive experience, or competitors with demonstrable international experience.\nDivision 2 is for competitors with less than 2 years of competitive experience and with no, or minimal, international competitive experience.\nDivision 1 is for more experienced competitors Division 2 is for less experienced competitors, structured to be more forgiving to newcomers to the ruleset.\n- Add: 14.7\n● Medical TKO: If a competitor receives a Medical TKO (medical staff determines the competitor cannot continue), they are disqualified from continuing in the tournament.\n● Non-Medical TKO: If a competitor receives a TKO due to a lack of defense, they will lose a Round in Division 1 or a Match in Division 2.\n- Add: 17 League Ranking Scoring\n\nUpdate date: June-2024\n- format: Grammar adjustments throughout the document Update date: March-2024\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.\nUpdate date: April-2024\n- removed 11.4 Passivity in a Fight (duplicated in rules 10.14 Intentional Passivity)\n- clarification\n- clarification 14.8 Disqualification (page29)\n- clarification 14.9 Knockout (KO) (page 29)","page_from":32,"page_to":33,"stable_key":"outrance-rules:18","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["16","10.14"],"content_sha256":"6b48811eefdd7fc7148a32c0c0f02f809ab6249278835f2e85f0580d3dfdba06","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/weapon-shield-chart","version":{"version":"2024.12.13","title":"Weapons/Shield Chart 2024.12.13","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"\"Weapons/Shield Chart\" (Google Sheets): weapons sheet \"TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED WEAPONS V2024.12.13\"; its SHIELDS sheet (page 2) is printed \"V2025.03\"; change log has only the undated \"Older vers.\" entries. Labelled by the first sheet as printed; the mixed sheet versions are recorded. Older than 26.1.","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FZNlPCWImDn_qUsmSOfDnSr2umzMEh5G/view","source_sha256":"22927e949dfc460d413de01219977c116dd586b6540c156e8d088788fab508d5","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":3,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"22b601fa0a626308309c9745322c456bdf284cfa4b36f70cdcb79ec786bb9323","detected":{"version":"2024.12.13","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":1,"edition_evidence":"\"Weapons/Shield Chart\" (Google Sheets): weapons sheet \"TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED WEAPONS V2024.12.13\"; its SHIELDS sheet (page 2) is printed \"V2025.03\"; change log has only the undated \"Older vers.\" entries. Labelled by the first sheet as printed; the mixed sheet versions are recorded. Older than 26.1.","source_files":[{"file":"Marshal/Archive/Weapons_Shield Chart 2024.12.13.pdf","archive":"Marshal","sha256":"22927e949dfc460d413de01219977c116dd586b6540c156e8d088788fab508d5","drive_file_id":"1FZNlPCWImDn_qUsmSOfDnSr2umzMEh5G"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["1 provision(s) need review against the official document"],"pages":3,"source_lines":52,"assigned_lines":85,"furniture_lines":2,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":1,"provisions":1,"numbered":0,"needs_review":1,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED WEAPONS V2024.12.13\n\nBladed Weapons (Swords, Sabers, Falchions etc)   Weight   Length   Length of the Blade   Length of the Handle   Special Restrictions\n\nType 1 Bladed (arming swords, falchions, sabers)   1.1 - 1.7   72 - 100   60 - 80   12 - 20\n\nType 2 Bladed (longsword)   1.7 - 2.3   100 - 140   70 - 100   20 - 50   The Hilt should not extend more then 35mm over the Bearers hand.\n\nType 3 Bladed   2.3 - 3.0   120 - 160   90 - 130   30 - 50\n\nHafted Weapons(Polearm,Poleaxe,2-handed axe)   Weight   Length   Length of Striking Edge   Special Restrictions\n\nType 1 Hafted (Mace)   0.7 -1.3   50-70   >5\n\nType 2 Hafted (Axe) 0.7 - 1.3 50 - 90 >7 Type 1 Hafted (Maces) must have 6 or more flanges or be a ball. All Hafted weapons with sharp corners (Less than 90 degrees) and corners that can be considered dangerous are not permitted. Any point on the Striking Edge of the weapon Must have an angle more than 90\nType 3 Hafted (Longaxe)   1.3 - 2.5   90 - 130   >9   degrees.\n\nType 4 Hafted (Polearm)   2.2 - 3.2   130 - 220   >12\n\nOutrance Bladed Weapons (Swords, Sabers, Falchions etc)   Calculation   Special Restrictions\n\nMens Balance Point of 15cm or more Outrance swords must also meet the Bladed Weapons Technical Requirements.\nBalance points are measured from the edge of the grip zone and includes the crossguard.\nWomens Balance Point of 10cm or more\n\nOther Restrictions for all Weapon Types\n\nThe permissible upwards error for all weapons is 100g.\nHeavier weapons or thrust weapons are not allowed under any circumstance.\nThe edge of all blades must be rebated and have a thickness of 2mm or more. This applies to striking and non-striking edges of all weapons.\nThe Radius of all edges must be more than 10mm.\nOnly Weapons which have chronological validity of a specific historical period as confirmed by the Authenticity Committee are allowed.\n\nTECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED SHIELDS V2025.03\n\nDuels Shields and Bucklers   Lenght   Width   Diameter   Weight\n\nMin Max Min Max Min Max Max\n\nHeater shield   40   75   30   65\n\nPunch shield   55   75   30   50\n\nRound shield for sword and shield   25   70   5\n\nRound shield for sword and buckler   25   35\n\nBuckler   20   35\n\nBuhurt Bucklers and Shields   Lenght   Width   Diameter   Weight\n\nHeater shield   40   75   30   65\n\nPunch shield 55 75 30 50 5\nRound shield   25   70\n\nBuckler   20   40\n\nOther Restrictions for all Weapon Types All shapes must be conform with the Shields and Buckler rule document The Radius of striking edge must be more than 7 cm.\nOnly Shields which have chronological validity of a specific historical period as confirmed by the Authenticity Committee are allowed.\n\nChangelog -add Shields sheet has been added\n- change The permissible upwards error (Has been changed to 100gram for all weapons)\n- change minium size of round shields was removed -add Round shields for Duels\n- format Changed the layout of shields","page_from":1,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"weapon-shield-chart:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fb5599de9dc73b826dde182ffa26f1daa6cde51e3a6d029adfee9fe279d3e9e1","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/weapon-shield-chart","version":{"version":"26.1","title":"Weapons/Shield Chart 26.1","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"\"Weapons/Shield Chart\": \"VER. 26.1\" on the weapons sheet; change log \"VER 26.1\" above \"Older vers.\".","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gmxi1-oetscRY5TZtU98KkOKS-iTLfJ6/view","source_sha256":"44b9ec5e2e644c3c957d4d7fc3b61ede9b35cd28608e99f67ab9590b6ed1726f","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":3,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"b12d8a0aadd5e0ca23184f0ee44a1aafe2dee9d7a251740c093475f7d72fa2d5","detected":{"version":"26.1","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":2,"edition_evidence":"\"Weapons/Shield Chart\": \"VER. 26.1\" on the weapons sheet; change log \"VER 26.1\" above \"Older vers.\".","source_files":[{"file":"Marshal/Archive/Weapons_Shield Chart 26.1.pdf","archive":"Marshal","sha256":"44b9ec5e2e644c3c957d4d7fc3b61ede9b35cd28608e99f67ab9590b6ed1726f","drive_file_id":"1gmxi1-oetscRY5TZtU98KkOKS-iTLfJ6"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["1 provision(s) need review against the official document"],"pages":3,"source_lines":56,"assigned_lines":84,"furniture_lines":2,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":1,"provisions":1,"numbered":0,"needs_review":1,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED WEAPONS\n\nAll weights and sizes are in metric (kg,cm)\n\nBladed Weapons (Swords, Sabers, Falchions etc)   Weight   Length   Length of the Blade   Length of the Handle   Special Restrictions\n\nType 1 Bladed (arming swords, falchions, sabers)   1.1 - 1.7   72 - 100   60 - 80   12 - 20\n\nType 2 Bladed (longsword)   1.7 - 2.3   100 - 140   70 - 100   20 - 50   The Hilt should not extend more then 35mm over the Bearers hand.\n\nType 3 Bladed   2.3 - 3.0   120 - 160   90 - 130   30 - 50\n\nHafted Weapons(Polearm,Poleaxe,2-handed axe)   Weight   Length   Length of Striking Edge   Special Restrictions\n\nType 1 Hafted (Mace)   0.7 -1.3   50-70   >5\n\nType 2 Hafted (Axe) 0.7 - 1.3 50 - 90 >7 Type 1 Hafted (Maces) must have 6 or more flanges or be a ball. All Hafted weapons with sharp corners (Less than 90 degrees) and corners that can be considered dangerous are not permitted. Any point on the Striking Edge of the weapon Must have an angle more than 90\nType 3 Hafted (Longaxe)   1.3 - 2.5   90 - 130   >9   degrees.\n\nType 4 Hafted (Polearm)   2.2 - 3.2   130 - 220   >12\n\nOutrance Bladed Weapons (Swords, Sabers, Falchions etc)   Calculation   Special Restrictions\n\nMens Balance Point of 15cm or more Outrance swords must also meet the Bladed Weapons Technical Requirements.\nBalance points are measured from the edge of the grip zone and includes the crossguard.\nWomens Balance Point of 10cm or more\n\nOther Restrictions for all Weapon Types\n\nThe permissible upwards error for all weapons is 100g.\nHeavier weapons or thrust weapons are not allowed under any circumstance.\nThe edge of all blades must be rebated and have a thickness of 2mm or more. This applies to striking and non-striking edges of all weapons.\nThe Radius of all edges must be more than 10mm.\nOnly Weapons which have chronological validity of a specific historical period as confirmed by the Authenticity Committee are allowed.\n\nTECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED SHIELDS\n\nAll weights and sizes are in metric (kg and cm)\n\nHeather and Punch Shields   Lenght   Width   Weight\n\nHeater shield 55 - 75 30 - 65 ≤5\nPunch shield   55 - 75   30 - 50\n\nRound Shields and Bucklers   Diameter   Weight\n\nRound shield 25 - 70 Buhurt ≤5 Buckler 20 - 70\n\nRound Shield 25 - 35 Duel ≤5 Buckler 20 - 35\n\nOther Restrictions for all Weapon Types All shapes must be conform with the Shields and Buckler rule document.\nThe Radius of striking edge must be more than 7 cm.\nOnly Shields which have chronological validity of a specific historical period as confirmed by the Authenticity Committee are allowed.\n\nChangelog VER 26.1\n- format Changed the layout of shields.\n- change Correction of the minimum lenght of Heather shield to match \"Shields and Bucklers\" document.\n- change Modification of the maximum diameter for Round shield and Bucklers in duels.\n- change Precision for Weight: \"≤ 5\".\n\nOlder vers.\n-add Shields sheet has been added\n- change The permissible upwards error (Has been changed to 100gram for all weapons)\n- change minium size of round shields was removed -add Round shields for Duels\n- format Changed the layout of shields","page_from":1,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"weapon-shield-chart:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"904729d07726c3ab0e3521c1feedeea34412386b8ab90e1a0979a63a41bb47f5","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/weapon-shield-chart","version":{"version":"26.2","title":"Weapons/Shield Chart 26.2","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"\"Weapons/Shield Chart\": \"VER. 26.2\"; change log \"VER 26.2\" above \"VER 26.1\". The current 26.2.1 change log continues \"VER 26.2.1\" above \"VER 26.2\".","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19_a5eCLtWKSESV7pzPZsUuER5n2Lu1FN/view","source_sha256":"6342d58e1f352c97104dcfaa3a8af740720efd35c7e3a5780449d2f2e7b5cd73","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":3,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"77b842ea638c6d0e07db6dc4e86053b80f9dbf3b14f597366045d98ec4ac105b","detected":{"version":"26.2","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":3,"edition_evidence":"\"Weapons/Shield Chart\": \"VER. 26.2\"; change log \"VER 26.2\" above \"VER 26.1\". The current 26.2.1 change log continues \"VER 26.2.1\" above \"VER 26.2\".","source_files":[{"file":"Marshal/Archive/Weapons_Shield Chart V26.2.pdf","archive":"Marshal","sha256":"6342d58e1f352c97104dcfaa3a8af740720efd35c7e3a5780449d2f2e7b5cd73","drive_file_id":"19_a5eCLtWKSESV7pzPZsUuER5n2Lu1FN"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["1 provision(s) need review against the official document"],"pages":3,"source_lines":58,"assigned_lines":83,"furniture_lines":4,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":1,"provisions":1,"numbered":0,"needs_review":1,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED WEAPONS\n\nBladed Weapons (Sword, Saber, Falchion, etc)   Weight   Length   Length of the Blade   Length of the Handle   Special Restrictions\n\nType 1 Bladed (Arming sword, Falchion, Saber)   1.1 - 1.7   72 - 100   60 - 80   12 - 20\n\nType 2 Bladed (Longsword)   1.7 - 2.3   100 - 140   70 - 100   20 - 50   The Hilt should not extend more then 35mm over the Bearer's hand.\n\nType 3 Bladed   2.3 - 3.0   120 - 160   90 - 130   30 - 50\n\nHafted Weapons (Polearm, Poleaxe, 2-handed axe, etc)   Weight   Length   Length of Striking Edge   Special Restrictions\n\nType 1 Hafted (Mace)   0.7 -1.3   50-70   >5\n\nType 2 Hafted (Axe) 0.7 - 1.3 50 - 90 >7 Type 1 Hafted (Maces) must have 6 or more flanges or be a ball. All Hafted weapons with sharp corners (Less than 90 degrees) and corners that can be considered dangerous are not permitted. Any point on the Striking Edge of the weapon Must have an angle more than 90\nType 3 Hafted (Longaxe)   1.3 - 2.5   90 - 130   >9   degrees.\n\nType 4 Hafted (Polearm)   2.2 - 3.2   130 - 220   > 12\n\nOutrance Bladed Weapons (Sword, Saber, Falchion, etc)   Calculation   Special Restrictions\n\nMen Balance Point of 15cm or more Outrance swords must also meet the Bladed Weapons Technical Requirements.\nBalance points are measured from the edge of the grip zone and includes the crossguard.\nWomen Balance Point of 10cm or more\n\nOther Restrictions for all Weapon Types\n\nThe permissible upwards error for all weapons is 100g.\nHeavier weapons or thrust weapons are not allowed under any circumstance.\nThe edge of all blades must be rebated and have a thickness of 2mm or more. This applies to striking and non-striking edges of all weapons.\nThe Radius of all edges must be more than 10mm.\nOnly Weapons which have chronological validity of a specific historical period as confirmed by the Authenticity Committee are allowed.\n\nTECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR PERMITTED SHIELDS\n\nHeather and Punch Shields   Lenght   Width   Weight\n\nHeater shield 55 - 75 30 - 65 ≤5\nPunch shield   55 - 75   30 - 50\n\nRound Shields and Bucklers   Diameter   Weight\n\nRound shield 25 - 70 Buhurt ≤5 Buckler 20 - 40\n\nRound Shield 25 - 35 Duel ≤5 Buckler 20 - 35\n\nOther Restrictions for all Shield and Buckler Types All shapes must be conform with the \"Shields and Bucklers\" rule document.\nThe Radius of striking edge must be more than 7 cm.\nOnly Shields which have chronological validity of a specific historical period as confirmed by the Authenticity Committee are allowed.\n\nChangelog VER 26.2\n- change Correction of the maximum diameter of Buckler for Buhurt to match \"Shields and Bucklers\" document.\nVER 26.1\n- format Changed the layout of shields.\n- change Correction of the minimum lenght of Heather shield to match \"Shields and Bucklers\" document.\n- change Modification of the maximum diameter for Round shield and Bucklers in duels.\n- change Precision for Weight: \"≤ 5\".\n\nOlder vers.\n-add Shields sheet has been added\n- change The permissible upwards error (Has been changed to 100gram for all weapons)\n- change minium size of round shields was removed -add Round shields for Duels\n- format Changed the layout of shields","page_from":1,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"weapon-shield-chart:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"723e33544ef0a3cce455dad690be6066d7b13ffcac4be6a52b0bfe1f95931a5b","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"tournament/buhurt-regulations","version":{"version":"2025.03","title":"Buhurt Regulations 2025.03","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Title \"Buhurt Regulations\"; cover \"VER. 2025.03\"; change log \"February-2025 (V2025.03)\" (and a \"December-2025\" document-created entry, as printed). Older than 26.1.","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kV8PHbC3elrC2N-ge55tMQ-q67Q4hCsI/view","source_sha256":"253663c21e363c1b1fe9cb3fa7122fcee776d1c94544ad9afef0453944e229f2","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":17,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8 + OCR (tesseract 5.3.4 psm4 300dpi) on 1 page(s) without a text layer","content_sha256":"095c3109e502ca21692f76bf90b1dd9045cc54bd825935a25d645fe5c33a3c15","detected":{"version":"2025.03","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":1,"edition_evidence":"Title \"Buhurt Regulations\"; cover \"VER. 2025.03\"; change log \"February-2025 (V2025.03)\" (and a \"December-2025\" document-created entry, as printed). Older than 26.1.","source_files":[{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Buhurt Regulations 2025.03.pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"253663c21e363c1b1fe9cb3fa7122fcee776d1c94544ad9afef0453944e229f2","drive_file_id":"1kV8PHbC3elrC2N-ge55tMQ-q67Q4hCsI"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["1 line(s) looked like a numbered heading but did not fit the sequence"],"pages":17,"source_lines":475,"assigned_lines":512,"furniture_lines":73,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99548,"provisions":74,"numbered":73,"needs_review":0,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":1,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":4,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"BUHURT\n\nVER. 2025.03\n\nBuhurt Regulations","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cc77f205ebd896f6a05aa4c7082f8111e6617123a25711d7d6f9e2eeef703b7e","has_figures":true,"extraction":"ocr"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General Regulations","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1c34870f9a45b95d70c2072f2b34fc7cf98feddc39bf0ef0064f9f14be3f722b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Weight Limit","body":"There are no weight categories in group battles.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7e9174cf2c0ca77c5fe747960bf5ecd6817e29242e2d6e1864dbe34dd7244ed8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"The Marshals Team Includes","body":"● Knight Marshal\n● Field Marshals (should be no less than 2 field marshals and 1 knight marshal in the list)\n● Line Marshals\n● Video Supervisors (recommended)\n● Secretary (a timekeeper)\n● Authenticity Committee Representative (AC Rep)","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"962d693da336e5305840b3ed2278811e8dc1c7850d60f8c05e5acd3cef06fbad","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"List Requirements","body":"Fights of the Buhurt International group battles category are conducted in the list with a hard surface and a rail. Depending on the type of the tournament, the size of the list may vary, provided it was agreed with Buhurt International and documented in the tournament Regulations.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fdda44ccb68d35d47f545a862fd5a26665bfbd9665b978265f1265643aec9a03","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.1","title":"Dimensions","body":"● 3v3: Length: 7 to 20 m | Width: 5 to 15 m\n● 5v5: Length: 9 to 20 m | Width: 7 to 15 m\n● 12v12: Length: 15 to 20 m | Width: 7 to 15 m\n● 30v30: Length: 25 to 30 m | Width: 12.5 to 20 m","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4399e5384c1932951d16e4cf97fe1862758ab2f799be3b08081a6fc8d3d294f3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.2","title":"List Height","body":"The height of the rail is 0.9 to 1.3 m.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"10043027de442b95f18c2d9e4a590a7c8deb07ff819c2a4e829e416086383338","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.3","title":"Safe Zone","body":"An organizer must provide a fenced, 2m wide safety zone around every side of the list.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"484a486c00bca64cc4347b5e5290dd971d180c692e11e0051216ca0e4a995f9a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.4","title":"Table top size","body":"The table top width should be between 50 - 70 cm","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"649ee4f266a34bf7a5a7ee95fa9b5ae6a8ee22ba43bfb49cd441caf755c9dace","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4","title":"Roles Allowed in the Safe Zone","body":"● Marshals\n● Team support (Handing over reserve weapons) in designated areas within the safe zone\n● Team manager (Captain, Coach)\n● Secretaries\n● Technical staff (List maintenance)\n● Media (Only approved media staff)","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bbcef2df38d5e9c31ae614d1f5ddd5ad936aafdc204644614f64eae94e34f5dc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.5","title":"Penalty","body":"● Accessing the safe zone without a designated role above may result in a penalty (yellow card) for the individual or team.\n● Of the above roles, only marshal teams are allowed to rest their hands on top of the list this may result in a penalty","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d26c1b8b392601b5275a9e039c43b7c2af327bcec149777e45c6bd52df65597d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Team Structure","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"57755761a29be93b3dedeb802f5c31bdaa23a5f54974c05dd786de5d71ffc648","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"Composition","body":"Teams participating in group battles consist of the following members\n● Team Manager (captain, coach)\n● Team Support\n● Competitors","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2dada9b1458e565b4a733f4f0f752a7acc77e3773135ed37bea212fc6c711289","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Competitors","body":"● Competitors cannot be on multiple teams in a single category at a tournament.\n● Once the tournament has started, team rosters are locked in and can not be changed.\n● Teams may replace competitors from their tournament roster in any frequency and number between the rounds or matches.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7da3a4aabb308d29627f701a246597abc17948529f987e711ed240a6c25192ef","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Number of Reserve Competitors and Support in the Safety Zone","body":"Competitors can have a team manager or support role.\n● 3v3 Team: 5 competitors,1 team manager, 1 support\n● 5v5 Team: 8 competitors, 1 team manager, 1 support\n● 12v12 Team: 20 competitors, 1 team manager, 2 supports\n● 30v30 Team: 50 competitors, 1 team manager, 3 supports\n\nDuring the Matches the competitors are not allowed in the safety zone. They will get penalised following article 1.5.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["1.5"],"content_sha256":"b523bf728a641e680bf2f0e749b2a7e1a3f8da3a6a81e99d73a9c5c287913994","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"Alternative composition","body":"Organizers decide on the team composition for other types of group battles.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"65e0caab42399081f47226495652b9503d8324bc7d3fce9428dcddf61019cab9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"Match Structure","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3d2bda23040fd0a72ae2e031665c7a2ef6effc2ae0aa7ce3a44a981ac8bbddfd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Match Duration","body":"● A match consists of 2 rounds, each lasting 5 minutes of effective fighting time.\n● If the command \"Stop Fight\" is called the timer must be paused.\n● If the winner cannot be determined after two rounds, additional rounds are fought.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1b8ca88d10d5dc8ca219cb9ff1e175f27b2a326318f557e7afbbb28acb80de4c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Match and Round Win Criteria","body":"● A match is won when a team secures victory in two rounds before the opposing team.\n● A round is stopped when a team is outnumbered by a ratio of 3 to 1, with a round victory going to the outnumbering team.\nExamples:\n● 12v12:\n1 vs. 3 = stop fight 4 vs. 12 = stop fight 3 vs. 11 = stop fight 4 vs. 11 = continue fight\n● 5v5:\n2 vs. 5 = continue fight 2 vs. 4 = continue fight 1 vs. 4 = stop fight 1 vs. 3 = stop fight","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"505b335865e6841ea1ddd27c463d19a95e77b1e057baa0761dfe9478ca834ae0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"Group Stage","body":"● Time Limit for Each Match: 10 minutes\n● Time Limit for Each Round: 5 minutes\n● If the time limit is reached, the team with the most active (not grounded) competitors wins.\n● If the match ends in a draw (provided the number of round victories was a draw), record the match as a draw.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8a40dbbe038cb12c17610a212238e966fcff64363c0907901ac7ac98ae05552f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"Round Robin, Elimination Brackets, Semi-finals, and Finals","body":"● A match cannot end in a draw.\n● The time limit for the match is unlimited.\n● The time limit for each round is 5 minutes.\n● If the time limit is reached, the team with the most active (not grounded) competitors wins.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0ca48a87b5e5f7ba609886f2756f137de03093f1770c4447e79497c2cef8fc96","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.1","title":"Resolving a Draw","body":"Initial Rounds\n● If no team wins two rounds after the set rounds, a third round is fought.\n\nThird Round\n● During the third round:\n● If both teams have only one competitor left standing, the fight stops upon a 'Break' command.\n● The timer is paused.\n● Competitors are led to the middle of the list.\n● If the third round ends in a draw, a fourth round is fought.\n\nFourth Round\n● During the fourth round:\n● If both teams have only one competitor left standing, the fight stops upon a 'Break' command.\n● The timer is paused.\n● Competitors are led to the middle of the list.\n\n● A winner is determined according to the rules of the ‘Champion’s Fight’.\n● If the fourth round ends in a draw, a fifth round is fought\n\nFifth Round\n● The rules of the 'Champion’s Fight' are applied.\n● Teams are allowed to select a competitor to represent them in this final round.","page_from":6,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f1a83ea772998554eda29bc6c1fc2fe8b3df3463169f06870effe2d02872a6a6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.2","title":"Group stage or round robin","body":"Determination of a winner in the group stage or round robin with equal number of victories reference the Tournament Structure documents.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2a00acd9254b02e41091763075c7f0b97c479cd13cb96a98ca3fcd96589d1858","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Champion's Fight Rules","body":"The Champion's Fight follows the general rules for group fights with specific adjustments and limitations.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f7694ddf9d7ed4c83019be1a0326edc3ca6b9e9a6bdddf1154b5be937051aa3d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.1","title":"General Setup","body":"The fight begins with both competitors positioned in the middle of the list.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"edf2d652f8d22cd218ef478f5c8c1bdc69599c3bc50aa9fa7d8ad908e71ea4bf","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.2","title":"Time Limit","body":"There is no time limit for the Champion's Fight. The fight continues until a winner is determined.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"36c1e688c470be846aa9f05926cf477ded069dc88cf28055da5efe3b35a587c1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.3","title":"Prohibited Actions","body":"It is strictly prohibited to touch the barrier of the list with any part of the body, including.\n● Extremities (arms, hands, legs, feet).\n● Head.\n● Shield.\n\nA competitor who touches the barrier of the list with any of these parts is immediately declared the loser of the fight.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ae97db5f18c63b439e847ea1767819cd63563788e1ab7bce321a5fab0de07274","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.4","title":"Permitted Actions","body":"Weapons are allowed to make contact with the barrier of the list during the fight.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"05ead09bd26c1e6ca949992e15cd0e16c5705129c383be4c7e0b51e8a1acd732","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.5","title":"Victory Conditions","body":"A competitor loses the fight if:\n● They touch the barrier of the list as described above.\n● They are otherwise defeated according to the rules of group fights.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"043efab8ca9971a12b8b4f854eac245872b6667580ad06e45176afdd6bd4c937","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Preparation for the Match","body":"","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1268c830269f015d8e72c7c8d1afd15d81e352650d4222f28ebab90c1cbc0791","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Team Invitation and Preparation","body":"● The Knight Marshal (either directly or via the Secretary) invites two teams to the list and announces their preparation.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c598d99fad645db2f0000255e2b8246b54cd4af6927dbdf0036d3fb74b614301","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1.1","title":"Important","body":"● The two invited teams must report to the designated area next to the list for Invited teams are expected to report to the list within one (1) minute.\n● If a team fails to report to the list within three (3) minutes , their opponent is awarded a technical win of the match or the fight starts with an uneven number of competitors (5-4, 5-3).","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.1.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b2ad97bcff42f0aec062c1c1ad93e0d0ad21b6e0ac5f1dcce84d0f864a5c9146","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Identity Verification","body":"● The Knight Marshal can request competitors to enter the list with their helmets off.\n● Once the competitors identities are verified:\n○ They are given 90 seconds to put on their helmets and prepare for the fight.\n○ Support outside of the list may assist competitors during this preparation phase.\n● Competitors are not allowed to leave the list before the start of the fight.\n○ This measure ensures that no unregistered competitors are fielded by the team.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a8b1dc813714b487464a2a5cf5ee3ffb28e8cf1f39f6b62d35855bb694af5147","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3","title":"Enter the list","body":"The competitors enter the list prepared for the Match","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"18654db14257ef0d908f797c1cc5106dafc45749bd3c0e8e66b72621d4745bbc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.1","title":"Line up","body":"● 5v5 Competitors line up entering the list for the marshal check.\n\n● 12v12 competitors form 2 rows of 6 competitors, keeping column alignment\n\n● 30v30 competitors form 3 rows of 10 competitors, keeping column alignment.\n\n● The formations for other types of fights must be documented in the Tournament Regulations or determined by the Knight Marshal.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3487d4c09aa4572645c96fa71ea54460bc69571ffd1366a755e35da842b6aaf7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.2","title":"Preparing for the match","body":"● Everyone, except for the Knight Marshal, field marshals, competitors, and a Team Manager (captain, coach), leaves the list.\n\n● The Team Manager (captain, coach) counts their competitors and reports readiness to the Knight Marshal.\n\n● The Knight Marshal checks the number of competitors on each team.\n\n● Technical and Authenticity checks equipment before the fight.\n○ Technical check is carried out by the team of marshals and the Knight Marshal.\n○ Authenticity check is carried out by an authenticity officer.\n\n● Team Managers (captains, coaches) leave the list.\n\n● Field Marshals take positions behind the teams’ formations near the gates.\n\n● The Knight Marshal requests field marshals to signal readiness and absence of unauthorized participants in the list.\n\n● The Knight Marshal commands “Team ready.” Teams can then assume their positions.","page_from":9,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2c2ae5cd718d5b566f96db991b8cbc11cff8fdc39b1aa3eaec9868dc2f9699f9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.3","title":"Start of the Fight","body":"● The Knight Marshal signals the start of the fight with the command “Fight.”\n\n● The Knight Marshal or a field marshal accompanies the voice command with a signal of a flag.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"25ecd4e773fa381df711e2756c2b9de22ae5ec81fe303975d8536f4a1bd3dd29","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.4","title":"Role of the Knight Marshal","body":"The Knight Marshal observes the general course of the fight and assesses team engagement.\n\nThey can:\n● Return competitors to the fight (if grounded by unauthorized technique).\n● Ground competitors.\n● Break inactive clinches lasting 10 seconds or longer.\n● Give penalties (cards) to competitors.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24a18eba3f8e7cbea6f64410ecf2660eca9c63d0c221d395a05cd9b942860bd4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.5","title":"Role of Field Marshal","body":"Field marshals observe the fight in the list and ensure compliance with the rules.\n\nThey can:\n● Return competitors to the fight (if grounded by unauthorized technique).\n● Ground competitors.\n● Break inactive clinches lasting 10 seconds or longer.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6935170a013d7b248376ce88c4ca1a8a7bda0d8c7bf6ab5ea642bdf341938f15","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.6","title":"Observations by Line Marshals and Video Supervisors","body":"● Line marshals or video supervisors observe the fight in their local sectors of the list from behind the barrier.\n● They are responsible for recording any rules violations.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.6","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c3871935180b6a352769e0378980b018ae29362707f4388f2944bdc14bdd39b1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.7","title":"Important","body":"● A line marshal may only interfere with the fight under the following conditions:\n○ By direct order of the Knight Marshal.\n○ To prevent a direct threat to a competitor’s safety.\n● A line marshal may also break an inactive clinch if necessary.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.7","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9aebd97e4cd64ddd06238459b44302178cf8f6dee1cb21a0084c3f37eb0bdfc0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.4","title":"Grounding a Competitor","body":"Both the Knight Marshal and Field marshals can ground a competitor from the list in the following cases:\n\n● Multiple verbal warnings being ignored in a round.\n● Multiple Fighting Techniques or Other Prohibited Actions.\n● Grounding your opponent by an illegal action where your opponent is unable to immediately rejoin the round.\n● Being grounded does not replace other penalties (e.g., yellow or red cards)","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"684b127f374d01c3fb96001d9b5381f9a6c3f824cc0624a996f9e2427a7ae112","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.5","title":"Removing Competitor from the list","body":"Both the Knight Marshal and field marshals must withdraw a competitor from the list in the following cases:\n\n● A competitor continues offensive actions after being grounded.\n● A competitor loses their helmet.\n● A Knight marshal can remove a competitor if they deem necessary.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a3e455f141ef088227806dcadbd797355b3b2e45670e123c684a95e1706c5268","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6","title":"End of the Round","body":"● A round is finished only after the Knight Marshal’s command of \"Stop fight!\"","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"647a6c9abd06be1a235efd6dffc8599300c34d8868984392baa41aecc57d5bc8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6.1","title":"Forfeit","body":"● A team manager (captain, coach) can throw a white flag “forfeit\" to signal the Knight Marshal to stop the fight.\n● In such cases:\n○ The opponents are awarded a technical win.\n○ The number of active competitors in the list is recorded as 5-0.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"07aedc9095d1672f668a21045f16b164b5659ac300c29cbf005c98463b0ceee3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6.2","title":"Forfeits During the Tournament","body":"● The first white flag results in a round loss.\n● The second white flag results in a match loss.\n● After the third white flag, the team is withdrawn from the tournament.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c15e3cf5388ed31920f56d7b3bc5ffbe70cd908301c0d7c208f3a2e76519b08b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.7","title":"Handling Grounded Competitors","body":"● Grounded competitors must remain on the ground until the Knight Marshal commands “Rise.”\n● After the “Rise” command, teams return to their initial positions.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.7","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b2fa3f3ff6422439494cc292f3891a82d412144c247efc92139f15d44ae7e9f3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.8","title":"Post-Round Procedures","body":"● Marshals report any registered rules violations to the Knight Marshal.\n● The Knight Marshal, based on these reports and personal observations:\n○ Decide the result.\n○ Processes appeals.\n○ Announces the score of the round or fight.\n○ Imposes warnings, yellow cards, or red cards.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.8","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1199e8fe7b00efeaa6e246c85d1a3986060d49efc7e112ac4cc601056e93032a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.8.1","title":"Important","body":"● After the end of the round or fight, the Knight Marshal can:\n○ Declare the round finished and announce the score.\n\n○ Announce a rematch with full or differentiated teams (e.g., 2v3, 3v4, 4v4, 4v5) if deemed necessary.","page_from":11,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.8.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b9e746192a70f81b0f3eb5ac4d1e712be3c9d8788136a02187f9366e45932d60","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.9","title":"Record Keeping","body":"The secretary records the results. At the end of the round, the secretary registers:\n● The round win.\n● The round score (number of active competitors of the both teams at the end of the round).\n● The time of the round.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.9","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a6036babb98a4c828293f212471ca98256e9db3b271a0ec717c157bedbd3bb17","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.10","title":"Match win","body":"Is one (1) match win on the scoresheet. Round victories and standing versus grounded scores are supplementary data.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.10","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"76e4121ff570eed0faf91094068a0e0535d47bc0d44946fa926c23afe2da3857","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Penalties","body":"","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a48c49302fd8b8c33e4251f1af014cef519ae6a794946b116b798535cfa310eb","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"Verbal Warning","body":"● A verbal warning is imposed for insignificant rule violations and serves to indicate the violation to the competitor.\n● Note: Verbal warnings are not registered in the tournament protocols.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9883f8ce4988afb90430266d7f95f1bb4891b13ec5e77838d34a4781c2604331","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":54,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"Warning (Yellow Card)","body":"● A yellow card will be recorded on the scoresheet.\n● Will affect scoring.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"60ac904d90e2b6f4552f21b49945d1b73c443de0810c08f1d5c46a49545f0a9f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":55,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2.1","title":"Reasons for Receiving a Yellow Card","body":"● The competitor delivered a prohibited action listed in “Buhurt Rules” (Article 5 and 6).\n● The competitor performed an action not listed in the Authorized Fighting Techniques section listed in “Buhurt Rules” (Article 4) .\n● The competitor got to their feet from being grounded before the command “All Rise.”\n● The competitor started the fight before the “Fight” command.\n● The competitor conducted offensive actions after the “Stop Fight” command and while the yellow flag was hung in front of their helmet.\n● The competitor purposely ignored a marshal’s command.\n● The competitor continued to fight while aware that they had lost a significant element of their armor.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5","4"],"content_sha256":"a4bce6d885c546ccad65a1401a6996b10fcd33ac3403ab04406395f4bfa824c6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":56,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2.2","title":"Important","body":"● Depending on the severity of the violation, the Knight Marshal may impose one (1) or two (2) yellow cards for these actions.\n● A competitor who receives two (2) yellow cards is disqualified.\n● Two yellow cards are equivalent to a red card.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0dc9f68d759437f2f1f99f5b70a0c89766594e2c7d955a3674da97a21ea963be","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":57,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Disqualification (Red Card)","body":"● A red card is imposed for severe rule violations or as a result of receiving a second yellow card.\n● A yellow card will be recorded on the scoresheet.\n● Will affect scoring.\n● A competitor who receives a red card is withdrawn from the tournament.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0751e0a25e89564464aea1e09f999481fd1ce5f1578863701ac1c8257d9ce65f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":58,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.1","title":"Reasons for Disqualification (Red Card)","body":"● Systematic rule violations (e.g., two (2) yellow cards during the tournament).\n● Injuring an opponent with unauthorized action, resulting in the opponent's inability to continue participating in the tournament (requires confirmation by a medic).","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9b6f632dd7117dd07fe7bd89b05650ee0bf5bf3337673bb99f04fe0ec5914a83","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":59,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.2","title":"Harsh and systematic arguments","body":"Harsh and systematic arguments with marshals, groundless challenging of decisions, or rude/derogatory behavior toward opponents or participants.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7fd8c65bf6c618a2ebebbe61a878d3c3a7b2ecc856b027d5a65fb785f1a3de0a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":60,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.3","title":"Injury Clause","body":"● If an injured competitor continues competing and claims injury later in the tournament, this will not lead to a red card. If the injured competitor participates in any category, the red card will be downgraded, and the Judiciary Committee will investigate and penalties may apply.\n● If a competitor continues to fight in rounds after receiving an illegal hit but later withdraws due to an “injury” claimed to be from the illegal hit, this does not result in an upgrade to a red card.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1fd63b1d9d48dcb3b7eddd4ca2ee77b9bad402bcad48d0978d5362c2ef5ac032","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":61,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.4","title":"Red Card Consequences","body":"When a competitor is disqualified, their team fields one less competitor than their opposition (but no fewer than 3 competitors) for:\n● The match during which the disqualification was imposed.\n● The next match in the tournament.\n\nExample If the opposition cannot meet the required number of competitors (e.g., 12 in 12v12), the penalized team will be placed in a disadvantageous position. If both teams receive red cards, neither gains an advantage.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"477c733984500352f730e4cbf91961e537601b8e1f093645e107c1ce173113a9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":62,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4","title":"Infraction in Authenticity Rules (Green Card)","body":"An official authenticity warning (green card) is a penalty imposed for an authenticity rule violation that is registered in the protocol of the tournament, and affects the competitor’s rating. A green card combined with a yellow card result in a red card, and the fighter is disqualified\n\nThe competitor can receive one (1) green card only once they choose to enter the list with the appropriate infraction level based upon the Infraction classification document.\n\n5.4. Team Disqualification A team may be disqualified under the following circumstances:","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"17ed421a25a1290d5a27785e426b5e7d0fb74f7accebcc8c136132a54d9b8762","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":63,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.1","title":"Exceeding the permitted number of competitors","body":"● In such cases, their opposition is automatically awarded the victory.\n● Important: If this rule violation is detected after the fact, the violating team’s results are annulled.\n● If detected during finals, trophies are withdrawn, and other competitors move up the ladder.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24406f9dd57331220ad1b6fac4dc901c55777c9aa2ea9591a5ba0d34b4a0bfaa","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":64,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.2","title":"Card limit","body":"The team’s competitors/support receive a combination of card as followed:\n● Two red cards and one yellow card.\n● Any variation totaling five (5) yellow cards (red cards count as two yellow cards).\n\n● Note: This applies only to the category being competed in.\n● Note: green cards do not count in team disqualification","page_from":14,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0ff870234bf2f1acc4b56c7628c50c83d470a4321cf0b966033cd8ad2e16a410","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":65,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.3","title":"Harassment or Systematic Arguing","body":"● Harsh and systematic arguments with marshals.\n● Groundless challenges to decisions.\n● Rude or derogatory behavior toward opponents or participants.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e1d81b6147759c8072e878880be9da2b34bb3d4912ff4b3d689dbf2b20da0734","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":66,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.4","title":null,"body":"A competitor entered the list after the competitors were counted.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"54e04f199893855fcb389f03e3c535c00ccb53205b970d3790dac9e357010380","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":67,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.5","title":"Additional Notes on Cards","body":"● All cards are individual warnings and are observed by the Judiciary Committee.\n● Yellow cards received by a team manager (captain, coach) or support staff result in disciplinary measures per general card regulations.\n● Cards are summed regardless of the person’s role (competitor, team manager, or support).","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7e3c18d8c942df5f83c6d34f7215e4c1881aa222dc0dae3aedaa63e487a9aa4f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":68,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"6","title":"Appeal","body":"","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6261482d1e92103ab4fedce3afc24db089b60094d760d764dc2399b9aea617aa","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":69,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.1","title":"How to Appeal","body":"● The team captain or the captain’s representative may appeal a decision made by the Marshals’ Team or the Knight Marshal.\n● Appeals are submitted to the Secretary.\n● The number of appeals is determined by the Tournament Organizer. It is recommended to allow one (1) appeal.\n● Important: If an appeal is approved, the competitor may submit an additional appeal.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"187c0f0601b5af43defed6a29de37f621c046e279b08f0c72a52cffcab569f87","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":70,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.2","title":"When to Appeal","body":"● The team captain or captain’s representative must announce their intention to appeal in person to the Secretary.\n● Appeals must be submitted:\n○ Within 15 minutes after the end of the match.\n○ Before the start of the fights in the next phase of the competition.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c146ed42580ef231e4e88618bd4f398a14dabc10f65109be67b70183dc35423a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":71,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.3","title":"Why to Appeal","body":"An appeal can be filed for the following reasons:\n\n● False implementation of a penalty (reprimand, warning, or disqualification).\n● Unregistered clean blows to the legal strike zones that affect the course of the fight.\n● Unregistered rule violations by the opponent that should result in a penalty (reprimand, warning, or disqualification).","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f9705a559f97a1038153cd09641a3849eec1fbb3435eec32b1d6575330ddbc94","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":72,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.4","title":"Result of the Appeal","body":"The possible outcomes of an appeal could include:\n\n● A general rematch of the round.\n● Restart from a particular point.\n● The imposition or withdrawal of yellow cards.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"de283a983a7f5dae612a3c8927fc33ca78801e9daf917feb82028824b100917d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":73,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.5","title":"Appeal to the Judiciary Committee","body":"● If the team captain is dissatisfied with the Knight Marshal’s decision, they may appeal to the Buhurt International Judiciary Committee.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a4352f2a5720ac180a1d8840d56b7fbc5eb002a6c75885c12e3b68879f6759de","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":74,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"7","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules\n\nDatum update: February-2025 (V2025.03) Clarification: 2.3: Added competitors amount per category Add: 5.4 Infraction in Authenticity Rules (Green Card) Removed: 5.2.1: The competitor used equipment in the list that had not passed technical or authenticity checks.\nRemoved: 5.2.2: A competitor is not allowed in the list if they fail to follow the Buhurt International requirements documents.\nClarification: 5.4.2 Note: green cards do not count in team disqualification\n\nDatum update: December-2025 -add: Document created following BI Format and incorporated the document structures and rules","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:7","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d2d3749a2ce05e76aae21e501648b1fe60594c5f7e8a5f663348e83e268fae92","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"tournament/buhurt-regulations","version":{"version":"26.1","title":"Buhurt Regulations 26.1","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Title \"Buhurt Regulations 26.1\"; cover \"VER. 26.1\"; change log \"Update: January -2026.1\" above \"March-2025 (V2025.03)\". Two byte-identical files (SHA-256), one edition. Older than the current 26.4.","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1U_mlJTveTR24iJoMlC--lAPQH7bDdGwC/view","source_sha256":"d2c9760c257657120df7d3222ce20a03f1831f6b7d5b9b2d4cf392d7cb02a3c3","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":18,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8 + OCR (tesseract 5.3.4 psm4 300dpi) on 1 page(s) without a text layer","content_sha256":"04dfe0cde91eafbf5b3266b79e2d2316879ce44d8ebd38645e73f56251858be6","detected":{"version":"26.1","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":2,"edition_evidence":"Title \"Buhurt Regulations 26.1\"; cover \"VER. 26.1\"; change log \"Update: January -2026.1\" above \"March-2025 (V2025.03)\". Two byte-identical files (SHA-256), one edition. Older than the current 26.4.","source_files":[{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Buhurt Regulations 26.1.pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"d2c9760c257657120df7d3222ce20a03f1831f6b7d5b9b2d4cf392d7cb02a3c3","drive_file_id":"1U_mlJTveTR24iJoMlC--lAPQH7bDdGwC"},{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Buhurt Regulations 26.1(1).pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"d2c9760c257657120df7d3222ce20a03f1831f6b7d5b9b2d4cf392d7cb02a3c3","drive_file_id":"11zLiTg95Weot57FhIZN2ObNbsXcbgSsa"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["1 line(s) looked like a numbered heading but did not fit the sequence"],"pages":18,"source_lines":489,"assigned_lines":528,"furniture_lines":75,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99568,"provisions":73,"numbered":72,"needs_review":0,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":1,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":4,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"BUHURT\n\nVER. 26.1\n\nBuhurt Regulations","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"36eaa637a7ded14982dc55a0fbe7f7dbbfd5961dca500949fa5c02d04e10e7ea","has_figures":true,"extraction":"ocr"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General Regulations","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1c34870f9a45b95d70c2072f2b34fc7cf98feddc39bf0ef0064f9f14be3f722b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Weight Limit","body":"There are no weight categories in group battles.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7e9174cf2c0ca77c5fe747960bf5ecd6817e29242e2d6e1864dbe34dd7244ed8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"The Marshals Team Includes","body":"● Knight Marshal\n● Field Marshals (should be no less than 2 field marshals and 1 knight marshal in the list)\n● Line Marshals\n● Video Supervisors (recommended)\n● Secretary (a timekeeper)\n● Authenticity Committee Representative (AC Rep)","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"962d693da336e5305840b3ed2278811e8dc1c7850d60f8c05e5acd3cef06fbad","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"List Requirements","body":"Fights of the Buhurt International group battles category are conducted in the list with a hard surface and a rail. Depending on the type of the tournament, the size of the list may vary, provided it was agreed with Buhurt International and documented in the tournament Regulations.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fdda44ccb68d35d47f545a862fd5a26665bfbd9665b978265f1265643aec9a03","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.1","title":"Dimensions","body":"● 3v3: Length: 7 to 20 m | Width: 5 to 15 m\n● 5v5: Length: 9 to 20 m | Width: 7 to 15 m\n● 12v12: Length: 15 to 20 m | Width: 7 to 15 m\n● 30v30: Length: 25 to 30 m | Width: 12.5 to 20 m","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4399e5384c1932951d16e4cf97fe1862758ab2f799be3b08081a6fc8d3d294f3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.2","title":"List Height","body":"The height of the rail is 0.9 to 1.3 m.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"10043027de442b95f18c2d9e4a590a7c8deb07ff819c2a4e829e416086383338","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.3","title":"Safe Zone","body":"An organizer must provide a fenced, 2m wide safety zone around every side of the list.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"484a486c00bca64cc4347b5e5290dd971d180c692e11e0051216ca0e4a995f9a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.4","title":"Table top size","body":"The table top width should be between 50 - 70 cm.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2e719967307b2cb7096615600506088ef3e2c090f5b864849ab13a8614938245","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4","title":"Roles Allowed in the Safe Zone","body":"● Marshals\n● Team support (Handing over reserve weapons) in designated areas within the safe zone\n● Team manager (Captain, Coach) in designated areas within the safe zone\n● Secretaries\n● Technical staff (List maintenance)\n● Media (Only approved media staff)","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5a0a1ff1396e358e724da4e8d2233ee1c69c74c0a1b2929403c387f86fa9840e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.5","title":"Penalty","body":"● Accessing the safe zone without a designated role above may result in a penalty (yellow card) for the individual or team.\n\n● Of the above roles, only marshal teams are allowed to rest their hands on top of the list; this may result in a penalty.","page_from":4,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:1.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c853324fe1969d339c6f3bb496aa66ccacdc27ecb07951332138555d6bbeb688","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Team Structure","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"57755761a29be93b3dedeb802f5c31bdaa23a5f54974c05dd786de5d71ffc648","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"Composition","body":"Teams participating in group battles consist of the following members:\n● Team Manager (captain, coach)\n● Team Support\n● Competitors","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d26b46bb1999aacbcf20a8f24d183eeadf892fc660badf6808efb609f0a69ead","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Competitors","body":"● Competitors cannot be on multiple teams in a single category at a tournament.\n● Once the tournament has started, team rosters are locked in and can not be changed.\n● Teams may replace competitors from their tournament roster in any frequency and number between the rounds or matches.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7da3a4aabb308d29627f701a246597abc17948529f987e711ed240a6c25192ef","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Number of Reserve Competitors and Support in the Safety Zone","body":"Competitors can have a team manager or support role.\n● 3v3 Team: 5 competitors,1 team manager, 1 support\n● 5v5 Team: 8 competitors, 1 team manager, 1 support\n● 12v12 Team: 20 competitors, 1 team manager, 2 supports\n● 30v30 Team: 50 competitors, 1 team manager, 3 supports\n\nDuring the Matches the competitors are not allowed in the safety zone. They will get penalised following article 1.5.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["1.5"],"content_sha256":"b523bf728a641e680bf2f0e749b2a7e1a3f8da3a6a81e99d73a9c5c287913994","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"Alternative composition","body":"Organizers decide on the team composition for other types of group battles.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:2.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"65e0caab42399081f47226495652b9503d8324bc7d3fce9428dcddf61019cab9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"Match Structure","body":"","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3d2bda23040fd0a72ae2e031665c7a2ef6effc2ae0aa7ce3a44a981ac8bbddfd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Match Duration","body":"● A match consists of 2 rounds, each lasting 5 minutes of effective fighting time.\n● If the command \"Stop Fight\" is called the timer must be paused.\n● If the winner cannot be determined after two rounds, additional rounds are fought.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1b8ca88d10d5dc8ca219cb9ff1e175f27b2a326318f557e7afbbb28acb80de4c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Match and Round Win Criteria","body":"● A match is won when a team secures victory in two rounds before the opposing team.\n● A round is stopped when a team is outnumbered by a ratio of 3 to 1, with a round victory going to the outnumbering team. On scoresheet you will record 3-1 ratio Examples:\n● 12v12:\n1 vs. 3 = stop fight 4 vs. 12 = stop fight 3 vs. 11 = stop fight 4 vs. 11 = continue fight\n● 5v5:\n2 vs. 5 = continue fight 2 vs. 4 = continue fight 1 vs. 4 = stop fight 1 vs. 3 = stop fight","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d9b9c9fb6a8255d87cf58c70f86f7f7fc12e9ed0ecfa7534d5e8813b48dca2f6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"Group Stage","body":"● Time Limit for Each Match: 10 minutes.\n● Time Limit for Each Round: 5 minutes.\n● If the time limit is reached, the team with the most active (not grounded) competitors wins.\n● If the match ends in a draw (provided the number of round victories was a draw), record the match as a draw.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"732a0549e6b80bb89ebde18bf6ceffde991b60e8d94bdbbccda41cd27e62eebd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"Round Robin, Elimination Brackets, Semi-finals, and Finals","body":"● A match cannot end in a draw.\n● The time limit for the match is unlimited.\n● The time limit for each round is 5 minutes.\n● If the time limit is reached, the team with the most active (not grounded) competitors wins.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0ca48a87b5e5f7ba609886f2756f137de03093f1770c4447e79497c2cef8fc96","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.1","title":"Resolving a Draw in a match","body":"Initial Rounds\n● If no team wins two rounds after the set rounds, a third round is fought.\n\nThird Round\n● During the third round:\n● If both teams have only one competitor left standing, the fight stops upon a 'Break' command.\n● The timer is paused.\n● Competitors are led to the middle of the list. Then initiate the Champions Fight\n● A winner is determined according to the rules of the ‘Champion’s Fight’.\n● If the third round ends in a draw, a fourth round is fought.\n\nFourth Round\n● During the fourth round:\n● If both teams have only one competitor left standing, the fight stops upon a 'Break' command.\n● The timer is paused.\n● Competitors are led to the middle of the list. Then initiate the Champions Fight\n● A winner is determined according to the rules of the ‘Champion’s Fight’.\n● If the fourth round ends in a draw, a fifth round is fought.\n\nFifth Round\n● The rules of the 'Champion’s Fight' are applied.\n● Teams are allowed to select a competitor to represent them in this final round.\n● If a draw repeat this process","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e255527fb62a481cd12a431f027357e8dcdc346a611bf505d37931e36aa9d150","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Champion's Fight Rules","body":"The Champion's Fight follows the general rules for group fights with specific adjustments and limitations.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f7694ddf9d7ed4c83019be1a0326edc3ca6b9e9a6bdddf1154b5be937051aa3d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.1","title":"General Setup","body":"The fight begins with both competitors positioned in the middle of the list.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"edf2d652f8d22cd218ef478f5c8c1bdc69599c3bc50aa9fa7d8ad908e71ea4bf","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.2","title":"Time Limit","body":"There is no time limit for the Champion's Fight. The fight continues until a winner is determined.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"36c1e688c470be846aa9f05926cf477ded069dc88cf28055da5efe3b35a587c1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.3","title":"Prohibited Actions","body":"It is strictly prohibited to touch the barrier of the list with any part of the body, including:\n● Extremities (arms, hands, legs, feet),\n● Head,\n● Shield.\n\nA competitor who touches the barrier of the list with any of these parts is immediately declared the loser of the fight.","page_from":8,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"789a5a5a22bf00cdf655b99d1394630c4f6e632ae93593638d7d160c1183ea62","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.4","title":"Permitted Actions","body":"Weapons are allowed to make contact with the barrier of the list during the fight.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"05ead09bd26c1e6ca949992e15cd0e16c5705129c383be4c7e0b51e8a1acd732","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5.5","title":"Victory Conditions","body":"A competitor loses the fight if:\n● They touch the barrier of the list as described above.\n● They are otherwise defeated according to the rules of group fights.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:3.5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"043efab8ca9971a12b8b4f854eac245872b6667580ad06e45176afdd6bd4c937","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Preparation for the Match","body":"","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1268c830269f015d8e72c7c8d1afd15d81e352650d4222f28ebab90c1cbc0791","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Team Invitation and Preparation","body":"● The Knight Marshal (either directly or via the Secretary) invites two teams to the list and announces their preparation.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c598d99fad645db2f0000255e2b8246b54cd4af6927dbdf0036d3fb74b614301","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1.1","title":"Important","body":"● The two invited teams must report to the designated area next to the list for Invited teams are expected to report to the list within one (1) minute.\n● If a team fails to report to the list within three (3) minutes , their opponent is awarded a technical win of the match or the fight starts with an uneven number of competitors (5-4, 5-3).","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.1.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b2ad97bcff42f0aec062c1c1ad93e0d0ad21b6e0ac5f1dcce84d0f864a5c9146","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Identity Verification","body":"● The Knight Marshal can request competitors to enter the list with their helmets off.\n● Once the competitors identities are verified:\n○ They are given 90 seconds to put on their helmets and prepare for the fight.\n○ Support outside of the list may assist competitors during this preparation phase.\n● Competitors are not allowed to leave the list before the start of the fight.\n○ This measure ensures that no unregistered competitors are fielded by the team.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a8b1dc813714b487464a2a5cf5ee3ffb28e8cf1f39f6b62d35855bb694af5147","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3","title":"Enter the list","body":"The competitors enter the list prepared for the Match","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"18654db14257ef0d908f797c1cc5106dafc45749bd3c0e8e66b72621d4745bbc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.1","title":"Line up","body":"● 5v5 Competitors line up entering the list for the marshal check.\n\n● 12v12 competitors form 2 rows of 6 competitors, keeping column alignment\n\n● 30v30 competitors form 3 rows of 10 competitors, keeping column alignment.\n\n● The formations for other types of fights must be documented in the Tournament Regulations or determined by the Knight Marshal.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3487d4c09aa4572645c96fa71ea54460bc69571ffd1366a755e35da842b6aaf7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.2","title":"Preparing for the match","body":"● Everyone, except for the Knight Marshal, field marshals, competitors, and a Team Manager (captain, coach), leaves the list.\n\n● The Team Manager (captain, coach) counts their competitors and reports readiness to the Knight Marshal.\n\n● The Knight Marshal checks the number of competitors on each team.\n\n● Technical and Authenticity checks equipment before the fight.\n○ Technical check is carried out by the team of marshals and the Knight Marshal.\n○ Authenticity check is carried out by an authenticity officer.\n\n● Team Managers (captains, coaches) leave the list.\n\n● Field Marshals take positions behind the teams’ formations near the gates.\n\n● The Knight Marshal requests field marshals to signal readiness and absence of unauthorized participants in the list.\n\n● The Knight Marshal commands “Team ready.” Teams can then assume their positions.","page_from":10,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2c2ae5cd718d5b566f96db991b8cbc11cff8fdc39b1aa3eaec9868dc2f9699f9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.3","title":"Start of the Fight","body":"● The Knight Marshal signals the start of the fight with the command “Fight.”\n\n● The Knight Marshal or a field marshal accompanies the voice command with a signal of a flag.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"25ecd4e773fa381df711e2756c2b9de22ae5ec81fe303975d8536f4a1bd3dd29","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.4","title":"Role of the Knight Marshal","body":"The Knight Marshal observes the general course of the fight and assesses team engagement and compliance with the rules\n\nThey can:\n● Return competitors to the fight (if grounded by unauthorized technique).\n● Ground competitors.\n● Break inactive clinches lasting 10 seconds or longer.\n● Give penalties (cards) to competitors.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"04730d83ca4377ce8891630b46b44dbfce8413d4b0b253b289af82fc7f6023c9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.5","title":"Role of Field Marshal","body":"Field marshals observe the fight in the list and ensure compliance with the rules.\n\nThey can:\n● Return competitors to the fight (if grounded by unauthorized technique).\n● Ground competitors.\n● Break inactive clinches lasting 10 seconds or longer.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6935170a013d7b248376ce88c4ca1a8a7bda0d8c7bf6ab5ea642bdf341938f15","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.6","title":"Observations by Line Marshals and Video Supervisors","body":"● Line marshals or video supervisors observe the fight in their local sectors of the list from behind the barrier.\n● They are responsible for recording any rules violations.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.6","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c3871935180b6a352769e0378980b018ae29362707f4388f2944bdc14bdd39b1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.7","title":"Important","body":"● A line marshal may only interfere with the fight under the following conditions:\n○ By direct order of the Knight Marshal.\n\n○ To prevent a direct threat to a competitor’s safety.\n● A line marshal may also break an inactive clinch","page_from":11,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3.7","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cf3902654f2e165f5dae1a5e5b1601614e883fe95adda25f5c214c3477c29fd3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.4","title":"Grounding a Competitor","body":"Both the Knight Marshal and Field marshals can ground a competitor from the list in the following cases:\n\n● Multiple verbal warnings being ignored in a round.\n● Multiple Fighting Techniques or Other Prohibited Actions.\n● Grounding your opponent by an illegal action where your opponent is unable to immediately rejoin the round.\n● Being grounded does not replace other penalties (e.g., yellow or red cards)","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"684b127f374d01c3fb96001d9b5381f9a6c3f824cc0624a996f9e2427a7ae112","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.5","title":"Removing Competitor from the list","body":"Both the Knight Marshal and field marshals must withdraw a competitor from the list in the following cases:\n\n● A competitor continues offensive actions after being grounded.\n● A competitor loses their helmet.\n● A Knight marshal can remove a competitor if they deem necessary.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a3e455f141ef088227806dcadbd797355b3b2e45670e123c684a95e1706c5268","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6","title":"End of the Round","body":"● A round is finished only after the Knight Marshal’s command of \"Stop fight!\"","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"647a6c9abd06be1a235efd6dffc8599300c34d8868984392baa41aecc57d5bc8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6.1","title":"Forfeit","body":"● A team manager (captain, coach) can throw a white flag “forfeit\" to signal the Knight Marshal to stop the fight.\n● In such cases:\n○ The opponents are awarded a technical win.\n○ The number of active competitors in the list is recorded as 5-0.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"07aedc9095d1672f668a21045f16b164b5659ac300c29cbf005c98463b0ceee3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6.2","title":"Forfeits During the Tournament","body":"● The first white flag results in a round loss.\n● The second white flag results in a match loss.\n● After the third white flag, the team is withdrawn from the tournament.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c15e3cf5388ed31920f56d7b3bc5ffbe70cd908301c0d7c208f3a2e76519b08b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.7","title":"Handling Grounded Competitors","body":"● Grounded competitors must remain on the ground until the Knight Marshal commands “All Rise.”\n● After the “All Rise” command, teams return to their initial positions.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.7","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8aa9b3da9d8041692abcb198e69a17a27864e65f8948634cb6e7320dbf647ae9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.8","title":"Post-Round Procedures","body":"● Marshals report any registered rules violations to the Knight Marshal.\n● The Knight Marshal, based on these reports and personal observations:\n○ Decide the result.\n○ Processes appeals.\n○ Announces the score of the round or fight.\n○ Imposes warnings, yellow cards, or red cards.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.8","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1199e8fe7b00efeaa6e246c85d1a3986060d49efc7e112ac4cc601056e93032a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.8.1","title":"Important","body":"● After the end of the round or fight, the Knight Marshal can:\n○ Declare the round finished and announce the score.\n○ Announce a rematch with full or differentiated teams (e.g., 2v3, 3v4, 4v4, 4v5) if deemed necessary.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.8.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.8","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bbe253fbfb998e7b3f192a83c561c523ebed21c03a48ccd5a1ba1b342563a84f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.9","title":"Record Keeping","body":"The secretary records the results. At the end of the round, the secretary registers:\n● The round win.\n● The round score (number of active competitors of the both teams at the end of the round).\n● The time of the round.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.9","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a6036babb98a4c828293f212471ca98256e9db3b271a0ec717c157bedbd3bb17","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.10","title":"Match win","body":"Is one (1) match win on the scoresheet. Round victories and standing versus grounded scores are supplementary data.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:4.10","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"76e4121ff570eed0faf91094068a0e0535d47bc0d44946fa926c23afe2da3857","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Penalties","body":"","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a48c49302fd8b8c33e4251f1af014cef519ae6a794946b116b798535cfa310eb","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"Verbal Warning","body":"● A verbal warning is imposed for insignificant rule violations and serves to indicate the violation to the competitor. Record on the scoresheet\n● Collect belt flag number, description of warning, name of competitor\n● Cannot affect scoring","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c417d6008818c324b7b285ab656e15e80ab0d3bca7df3f96b5e0da41d209f4d1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"Warning (Yellow Card)","body":"● A yellow card will be recorded on the scoresheet. Collect belt flag number, description of incident, name of competitor\n● Can affect scoring.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"815aa75930c3fd25b28b90cebb53caae34914b1c9e8f66abf95322048740fd8d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":54,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2.1","title":"Reasons for Receiving a Yellow Card","body":"● The competitor delivered a prohibited action listed in “Buhurt Rules” (Article 5 and 6).\n● The competitor performed an action not listed in the Authorized Fighting Techniques section listed in “Buhurt Rules” (Article 4) .\n● The competitor got to their feet from being grounded before the command “All Rise.”\n● The competitor started the fight before the “Fight” command.\n● The competitor conducted offensive actions after the “Stop Fight” command and while the yellow flag was hung in front of their helmet.\n● The competitor purposely ignored a marshal’s command.\n● The competitor continued to fight while aware that they had lost a significant element of their armor.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5","4"],"content_sha256":"a4bce6d885c546ccad65a1401a6996b10fcd33ac3403ab04406395f4bfa824c6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":55,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2.2","title":"Important","body":"● Depending on the severity of the violation, the Knight Marshal may impose one (1) or two (2) yellow cards for these actions.\n● A competitor who receives two (2) yellow cards is disqualified.\n● Two yellow cards are equivalent to a red card.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0dc9f68d759437f2f1f99f5b70a0c89766594e2c7d955a3674da97a21ea963be","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":56,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Disqualification (Red Card)","body":"● A red card is imposed for severe rule violations or as a result of receiving a second yellow card.\n● A red card will be recorded on the scoresheet. Collect belt flag number, description of incident, name of competitor\n● Can affect scoring.\n● A competitor who receives a red card is withdrawn from the tournament.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f0e5bfec2fc330e12f44e77035e40a1b92956b0eb12d4cfe49315d15d19887b7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":57,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.1","title":"Reasons for Disqualification (Red Card)","body":"● Systematic rule violations (e.g., two (2) yellow cards during the tournament).\n● Injuring an opponent with unauthorized action, resulting in the opponent's inability to continue participating in the tournament (requires confirmation by a medic).","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9b6f632dd7117dd07fe7bd89b05650ee0bf5bf3337673bb99f04fe0ec5914a83","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":58,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.2","title":"Harsh and systematic arguments","body":"Harsh and systematic arguments with marshals, groundless challenging of decisions, or rude/derogatory behavior toward opponents or participants.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7fd8c65bf6c618a2ebebbe61a878d3c3a7b2ecc856b027d5a65fb785f1a3de0a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":59,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.3","title":"Injury Clause","body":"● If an injured competitor continues competing and claims injury later in the tournament, this will not lead to a red card. If the injured competitor participates in any category, the red card will be downgraded, and the Judiciary Committee will investigate and penalties may apply.\n● If a competitor continues to fight in rounds after receiving an illegal hit but later withdraws due to an “injury” claimed to be from the illegal hit, this does not result in an upgrade to a red card.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1fd63b1d9d48dcb3b7eddd4ca2ee77b9bad402bcad48d0978d5362c2ef5ac032","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":60,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3.4","title":"Red Card Consequences","body":"When a competitor is disqualified, their team fields one less competitor than their opposition (but no fewer than 3 competitors) for:\n● The match during which the disqualification was imposed.\n● The next match in the tournament.\n\nExample If the opposition cannot meet the required number of competitors (e.g., 12 in 12v12), the penalized team will be placed in a disadvantageous position. If both teams receive red cards, neither gains an advantage.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"477c733984500352f730e4cbf91961e537601b8e1f093645e107c1ce173113a9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":61,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4","title":"Infraction in Authenticity Rules (Green Card)","body":"An official authenticity warning (green card) is a penalty imposed for an authenticity rule violation that is registered in the protocol of the tournament, and affects the competitor’s rating. A green card combined with a yellow card result in a red card, and the fighter is disqualified.\n\nThe competitor can receive one (1) green card only once they choose to enter the list with the appropriate infraction level based upon the Infraction classification document.\n\n5.4. Team Disqualification A team may be disqualified under the following circumstances:","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"10e5e0843c1579c235ee032b9be877ead46a0bb7aec7d398e32d4294236ec607","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":62,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.1","title":"Exceeding the permitted number of competitors","body":"● In such cases, their opposition is automatically awarded the victory.\n● Important: If this rule violation is detected after the fact, the violating team’s results are annulled.\n● If detected during finals, trophies are withdrawn, and other competitors move up the ladder.","page_from":15,"page_to":15,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24406f9dd57331220ad1b6fac4dc901c55777c9aa2ea9591a5ba0d34b4a0bfaa","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":63,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.2","title":"Card limit","body":"The team’s competitors/support receive a combination of card as followed:\n● Two red cards and one yellow card.\n\n● Any variation totaling five (5) yellow cards (red cards count as two yellow cards).\n● Note: This applies only to the category being competed in.\n● Note: green cards do not count in team disqualification.","page_from":15,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7e3cf8aeb142df4624d1135c6edc3db470762a13cefbdf2ab3e98435b1dabc60","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":64,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.3","title":"Harassment or Systematic Arguing","body":"● Harsh and systematic arguments with marshals.\n● Groundless challenges to decisions.\n● Rude or derogatory behavior toward opponents or participants.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e1d81b6147759c8072e878880be9da2b34bb3d4912ff4b3d689dbf2b20da0734","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":65,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4.4","title":null,"body":"A competitor entered the list after the competitors were counted.","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"54e04f199893855fcb389f03e3c535c00ccb53205b970d3790dac9e357010380","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":66,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.5","title":"Additional Notes on Cards","body":"● All cards are individual warnings and are observed by the Judiciary Committee.\n● Yellow cards received by a team manager (captain, coach) or support staff result in disciplinary measures per general card regulations.\n● Cards are summed regardless of the person’s role (competitor, team manager, or support).","page_from":16,"page_to":16,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:5.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7e3c18d8c942df5f83c6d34f7215e4c1881aa222dc0dae3aedaa63e487a9aa4f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":67,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"6","title":"Appeal","body":"","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6261482d1e92103ab4fedce3afc24db089b60094d760d764dc2399b9aea617aa","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":68,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.1","title":"How to Appeal","body":"● The team captain or the captain’s representative may appeal a decision made by the Marshals’ Team or the Knight Marshal.\n● Appeals are submitted to the Secretary.\n● The number of appeals is determined by the Tournament Organizer. It is recommended to allow one (1) appeal.\n● Important: If an appeal is approved, the competitor may submit an additional appeal.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.1","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"187c0f0601b5af43defed6a29de37f621c046e279b08f0c72a52cffcab569f87","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":69,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.2","title":"When to Appeal","body":"● The team captain or captain’s representative must announce their intention to appeal in person to the Secretary.\n● Appeals must be submitted:\n○ Within 15 minutes after the end of the match.\n○ Before the start of the fights in the next phase of the competition.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.2","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c146ed42580ef231e4e88618bd4f398a14dabc10f65109be67b70183dc35423a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":70,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.3","title":"Why to Appeal","body":"An appeal can be filed for the following reasons:\n● False implementation of a penalty (reprimand, warning, or disqualification).\n● Unregistered rule violations by the opponent that should result in a penalty (reprimand, warning, or disqualification).","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.3","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6bb61c712027d31b63c1b179bffdad995b26f010d9b72b7cfb642191aa82e908","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":71,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.4","title":"Result of the Appeal","body":"The possible outcomes of an appeal could include:\n● A general rematch of the round.\n● Restart from a particular point.\n● The imposition or withdrawal of yellow cards.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.4","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9fe4aa2523d5baf8cc49139e9c2c41023f3024bccb2e1ed9738dfe5cd5a5ea74","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":72,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.5","title":"Appeal to the Judiciary Committee","body":"● If the team captain is dissatisfied with the Knight Marshal’s decision, they may appeal to the Buhurt International Judiciary Committee.","page_from":17,"page_to":17,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:6.5","parent_key":"buhurt-regulations:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a4352f2a5720ac180a1d8840d56b7fbc5eb002a6c75885c12e3b68879f6759de","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":73,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"7","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will\n\ndisplay what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules\n\nUpdate: January -2026.1 Add: 3.2 On scoresheet you will record 3-1 ratio Clarification: 3.4.1 Champions Fight Add: 5.1 Verbal Warning\n● A verbal warning is imposed for insignificant rule violations and serves to indicate the violation to the competitor. Record on the scoresheet\n● Collect belt flag number, description of warning, name of competitor\n● Cannot affect scoring Clarification: 5.2 and 5.3\n\nupdate: March-2025 (V2025.03) Clarification: 2.3: Added competitors amount per category Add: 5.4 Infraction in Authenticity Rules (Green Card) Removed: 5.2.1: The competitor used equipment in the list that had not passed technical or authenticity checks.\nRemoved: 5.2.2: A competitor is not allowed in the list if they fail to follow the Buhurt International requirements documents.\nClarification: 5.4.2 Note: green cards do not count in team disqualification\n\nupdate: December-2025 -add: Document created following BI Format and incorporated the document structures and rules","page_from":17,"page_to":18,"stable_key":"buhurt-regulations:7","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"59d6e3f506f296905121d79c408e5eb82680a24245912af8dbc1218ac6945117","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"tournament/duel-regulations","version":{"version":"2024.12","title":"Duel Rules and Regulations 2024.12","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Cover \"VER. 2024.12\" (heading \"Rules and Regulations\"), footer \"Duel Rules and Regulations\"; change log \"December 2024 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2024.12)\" — the same entries continue in the later Duels Regulations editions, so it is the same document. Two byte-identical files.","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pYTCc0lnljqT7VAE-tQLWFnVwUY21myn/view","source_sha256":"e0089cb358f1807fe91eda47c63b8b18049806f2daff3b4a9d4150064af373b8","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":11,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8 + OCR (tesseract 5.3.4 psm4 300dpi) on 1 page(s) without a text layer","content_sha256":"e6490c9c74f80e59e25f5ab9f2423525c09952137c2dfffb3aeeb864b617b292","detected":{"version":"2024.12","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":1,"edition_evidence":"Cover \"VER. 2024.12\" (heading \"Rules and Regulations\"), footer \"Duel Rules and Regulations\"; change log \"December 2024 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2024.12)\" — the same entries continue in the later Duels Regulations editions, so it is the same document. Two byte-identical files.","source_files":[{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Duels Regulations V2024.12.pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"e0089cb358f1807fe91eda47c63b8b18049806f2daff3b4a9d4150064af373b8","drive_file_id":"1pYTCc0lnljqT7VAE-tQLWFnVwUY21myn"},{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Duels Regulations V2024.12(1).pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"e0089cb358f1807fe91eda47c63b8b18049806f2daff3b4a9d4150064af373b8","drive_file_id":"1kzsupdQyoHU1Ho8SYQfZ_msyHfuZ44NR"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["4 line(s) looked like a numbered heading but did not fit the sequence","2 provision(s) need review against the official document"],"pages":11,"source_lines":270,"assigned_lines":280,"furniture_lines":65,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99938,"provisions":51,"numbered":50,"needs_review":2,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[],"rejected_numbers":4,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":3,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"VER. 2024.12\n\nRules and Regulations Duel rules and regulations","page_from":1,"page_to":2,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6be88c0378fb7876894050b37da696c668e47d4b9e8be1d77c38b4825278d5d3","has_figures":true,"extraction":"mixed"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General Provisions","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d3460a1bce22168eb4fc581713c7f54838f7f6aa5be599e1b9b2b4e8ddc14938","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"List Regulations","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c3f0115386bb4274756fb2ea4ddb8735bb7cca466a21741310ef0108a780b825","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.1","title":null,"body":"Fights of the Buhurt International duel categories Triathlon, Sword and Buckler, Sword and Shield, Polearm are held in hard-surface lists, with a barrier measuring 5–10m wide and 5–10m long. The height of the barrier is 0.9–1.3m.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.1.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3b199aa37f95f4a30c88e487174dcc44ee1c57e15ddaab3257899449b83f2045","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.2","title":null,"body":"There must be a fenced, 2m-wide safety zone around every side of the list.\nOnly the Marshal Brigade, support of the competitors, Team Managers, technical brigade and accredited photo/videographers are permitted into the safety zone during the fights. Any extra competitor or non-combatant of the team entering the safety zone during fights will result in a penalty (yellow card) for the individual or their team (club).","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.1.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cbcf8a767c0315b31daa110551b8762cdb8384445ab9e4a41ad41f03b3cccd09","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Weight categories","body":"There are no weight categories in the duel category.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"50561c1faedb2e69e10b3ffff6ab52b4f6c60b3143169a526b33f858eac4e89d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Marshals Committee","body":"The team of Marshals includes:","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4be8b2ffda8ea3a9f4c559ee9ce488d01f38840e4838fdfdfda8ad7c92fbbc80","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"One (1) Knight Marshal (Chief Official/Head Referee)","body":"● Observes the general course of the fight and assesses actions of the competitors in the list.\n● In case of disagreement, the Knight Marshal makes the final decision.\n● Only the Knight Marshal can interfere with the course of the fight.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6c5b09dab886f13939fcc26c3ffb6267fd62279bab18e237fc15b83fe5ba38a5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Four (4) Line Marshals (Fight Officials/Referees)","body":"● Supervise the fight and score the clean blows delivered to the permitted strike zones.\n● Take note of rule violations committed during the fight.\n● Cannot interfere with the fight.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5e6ca1a35b7ce7756a58a28d36e2068e1b271e6b6755c4c44f23ebc83d58ba46","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"One (1) Timekeeper","body":"● Times the rounds of the fight.\n● If the Knight Marshal halts the fight, the Timekeeper stops timing the round and resumes timing when the fight resumes\n● Registers the results of the round in rating protocol.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0400db351f677a7b2e15806dce2b9f41a7e5baf44cf71df313ea412bf8b0e869","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"One (1) Authenticity Committee Representative (AC Rep)","body":"● Authenticity representative who will preform on location AC checks","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1f16bae93051958277637cd08ae24cb478165db3ec7987c46c6e09138d51987b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.5","title":"One (1) Videos Supervisor","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f2af5bec0f4995d220240a6bd1d66e136113d9883a921ba182e042027d9c2e2b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"Fight Proceedings","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"176af81a5c990c7e8f3f01362a9a04513591ed7ec464da362b11ecc3c2c206c8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Preparation for the fight","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"992f60bd5675857ce1fb9593723d84af660608273f7b56cc521f76026fffbe9b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.1","title":"The Knight Marshal invites the competitors to report to the designated area of the","body":"list to pass pre-fight, authenticity, aesthetic, and technical equipment checks. They announce the competitors preparing for the next fight.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b54f0f13c07fcded21f205afc422ab7df6266cd49b61ed294d3d281745fc5349","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.2","title":null,"body":"Invited competitors are granted up to sixty (60) seconds to report to the list.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"81d976ae3ec701c1a3ef80b3cc8c48a23ed296b6e6fcb908a467b667b0936a33","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.3","title":null,"body":"The Knight Marshal can ask the competitors to enter the list with their helmets off.\nWhen the correspondence between the competitors present in the list and competitors registered for the fight has concluded, they will then be given an additional 30 seconds to put on their helmets and prepare for the fight. Seconds (assistants) outside the list can assist the competitors in preparation. The competitors are not allowed to leave the list before the start of the fight. This measure excludes the possibility of team roster replacement.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d2efe34602f9a1805ebed11d3e894e45682d5bd8a80397e7fc2b8dab40c1040e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.4","title":"The Knight Marshal requests marshals and competitors to confirm their","body":"readiness.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"985addafa7124f9d8afc9e2e8ed634f7c4d5bb3fe51b697276e28a9fdd38981c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.5","title":"The Knight Marshal signals the beginning of the fight with the command “Fight!”","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"79f283c4148ca9c52dd78b30bb7299eaf2e27a05e8a6b114675baa77147f2a22","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Characteristics of each category","body":"The organizers can alter the length of the fights/number of rounds/orders of the rounds (one category, triathlon, four fights type of competition) provided this decision is coordinated with the Head Organization and is registered in the Tournament Regulations.\nBreak between Technical\nCategory End of round Fight victory rounds win Longsword Total score from two (2) main rounds and an Sword and shield additional 30-second\n60 seconds of effective 30 seconds to rest round in case of a tie. 10-0 time and the “Stop fight”\nPolearms command of the Knight The score must have at Marshall least a 2 point difference.\n120 seconds to Total score from three (3) Triathlon change their main rounds equipment Achieve two (2) round 5 clean blows delivered by victories one competitor during the\nSword and buckler No break 2-0 round or 60 seconds of An additional round may effective time be fought in case of a tie.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bc3f492652c5f899ee427f575c033e0e2b3c913b8384f007c63e7e72ad7d8d74","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"End of the round","body":"All marshals in the list report to the Knight Marshal to announce the score and any rule violations. Based on the marshals’ reports and personal observations, the Knight Marshal makes a decision about the result of the round by :\n● Processing the appeals (if any were submitted).\n● Issuing penalties (reprimands, warnings, and disqualification) to the competitors.\nAnnouncing the result of the round.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"af076feaeab7fa6c8d760b54f0a5516bfeb7c6b7d6cb60b7ac2d6e7cf4dcadb5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"End of the fight","body":"When the conditions of fight victory are reached, the winner of the fight is announced.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d3981634061ac76d586110faf956f5c8e0000434e1600bd1334c6fdbe3c6b235","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.1","title":null,"body":"The Secretary registers the results of the rounds in rating protocol :\n● The round victory\n● The round score\n● Match victory\n● 2 point difference for Polearm | Sword and Shield | Longsword examples: total score competitor A 10, competitor B 11 no winner additional round needed total score competitor A 15, competitor B 13, winner is competitor A\n● Yellow and red cards in the competitor’s rating 2.5 One (1) Authenticity Committee.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cb7b893bdabd7eeb98ea5334ece1c87f294b8f96359bf4b5920addd738a5cea9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.2","title":"The winner is documented on the scoresheet. The rest of the rating scores","body":"(victories in the rounds, loss of the points because of yellow cards) are considered only in case of a draw in points.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"89db9aad74484a570ea2d55220ee172ee3ecb61211f248df5993f961a71149c8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.3","title":null,"body":"provided the competitors are informed in advance, the number of rounds and break time can be decreased under extraordinary circumstances.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"26dede1b5c49df2a72dd5fa941513d78019b6200ee3523940230ff8aeebc3054","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Technical win","body":"A technical victory is awarded to one of the competitors in the following cases:\n● If the opponent withdraws from the fight before it starts.\n● If the opponent fails to report to the list upon the Knight Marshal’s call. Competitors who fail to report to the list for the fight are penalized with a yellow card.\n● If the opponent fails to prepare the equipment within the designated time.\n● If the opponent cannot participate in the competition because of an injury or disqualification (two (2) Yellow cards or Red card). If the opponent injures the competitor with an illegal strike, the competitor receives a penalty of double yellow cards and is disqualified.\n● If the opponent has an equipment failure (weapon and armor) that is impossible to fix in one (1) minute. Assessment is made by the Knight Marshal.\n● If the opponent gains three (3) reprimands during one fight.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f6adbb41e68e1828069a5a23af50aa292099832e7096fb1c5e639d0e9293fd25","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Penalties","body":"","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bcfa77d805fe5b0fc96ec3b2f7e2d5ca1e73ea0a3a85f245c34f8e0b9e69aabd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Verbal warning","body":"A verbal warning is a penalty imposed for insignificant rules violation, aiming at indicating the rules violation to the competitor. A verbal warning is not registered in protocols.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c3df64f72642259e3b1b105c0671c17c80f16e2545be1e17f59dbcc90cfe6604","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Reprimand","body":"A reprimand to a competitor will result in three (3) points added to their opponent’s score. The points gained because of the reprimand are registered separately in the rating. Reprimands are not noted in the tournament protocol and personal records of the competitors. The competitor receives a reprimand in case of :","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c8753acf5951763cd464326e3455603099a071fc7b0e55be1cbf2fc9ea1d766e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.1","title":null,"body":"Failing to report to the list within the designated time frame (one (1) minute).","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"85bf3f942ed59ad788febda13d6fefde5fae9ff281fbeb91cc368556461f51c7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.2","title":"A fall that was caused by offensive actions of the opponent, provided they were","body":"conducted in accordance with the ruleset.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f0c73674f3e701c0dbd6e5b6f782abc74279b363bc603afa12a4b33d4c220edc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.3","title":"Armor (not weapon or shield) failure that prevents the competitor from continuing","body":"the fight. If the issue was fixed within the time limit (set by the knight marshal), the fight can continue. The decision on the severity of the Armor failure and time limit is made by the Knight Marshal.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7d7874413468ba29a3009739a03a176019cdca805470c310adf82fa0404e14f1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.4","title":null,"body":"Weapon loss during the fight.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"abc5ef63738c67fd8e45fbea6e814651ff189415dcbe5947dd56c2bc44b38e36","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.5","title":"Passive attitude. A competitor’s refusal to conduct offensive actions during the","body":"length of time (not less than 15 seconds) is considered a passive attitude.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"477f4df25c723c9368a7c7bdb601f9bf7bf36150683eae181770202f542a3776","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.6","title":null,"body":"Falling or stepping outside the boundaries of the list.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.6","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9f606223008b73af0dc417cdd91178dc4de9a7be9adaf13bd0663afa7a7d1c6a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3","title":"Yellow Card","body":"An official warning (yellow card) is a penalty imposed for a rule violation that is registered in the protocol of the tournament, and affects the competitor’s rating. A competitor can receive up to two (2) Yellow cards within a tournament before disqualification.\nThe competitor can receive one (1) or two (2) yellow cards for all following actions, depending on the severity of the violation and the Knight Marshals’ decision :","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b8dedb25a982bb232a4343be3b1efc76562979fdef485dfb399ca40d8ae28067","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.1","title":null,"body":"A competitor performs any illegal action listed in the Rules for the Triathlon, Longsword, Sword and Buckler, Sword and shield, and Polearm categories.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bf2ffc1938f18f64f2a4d0fa04fdd7cc36889218e8e05b772149d238b85a9d56","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.2","title":"A competitor performs any action not listed in the authorized techniques section","body":"of the Rules for the Triathlon, Longsword, Sword and Buckler, Sword and shield, and Polearm categories.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0aab0b96394294baece0b7ec30bcb659afa7c752a48988001c344cf74f36ced9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.3","title":null,"body":"A competitor enters the list with unauthorized equipment (see section 5).","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5"],"content_sha256":"12a60bd43a2b1e1d4250d2f8a5835a52a0a03a71b30da3f11429ebbee256d407","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.4","title":"For a demonstration of poor sportsmanship, derogatory behaviour, obscene","body":"language, comments directed at marshals, opponents, or spectators.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5d1682e16dc9ba686b75902a8fdb4836afe914e8058fd3e254072a3b36e285c6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.5","title":null,"body":"A competitor enters the safety zone during fights.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"38d7f0f10c4bbcb345d73c4f6480df704705eb1df2aa4853965790252d4ebf67","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.6","title":null,"body":"A competitor starts the fight before the ‘Fight’ command.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.6","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"566751d5323e07d0b776d487fd5b1540b317b5edecc8260978bc39765af7d118","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.7","title":null,"body":"A competitor performs offensive actions after the ‘Stop Fight’ command.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.7","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cd06a35054b87e1cd6ad13ef6e3a00d9427e6cf67b74eca693c6118768b406e9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.8","title":null,"body":"A competitor ignores the Knight Marshals’ orders.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.8","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8fded9566bdeee8bc2de1e7612d70d45ca24f992057653c26187dc7c49ea8851","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.4","title":"Red Card","body":"Disqualification (red card) is a penalty resulting from severe or regular (second yellow card) rule violations and is registered in the tournament protocol. The red carded competitor will be withdrawn from the tournament. Only the Knight Marshal of the tournament can apply red cards. The competitor receives a disqualification in case of\n● Systematic rule violations (two (2) yellow cards during the tournament).\n● Injuring the opponent with illegal strikes. However, if marshals or medics ascertain that an injury has been simulated, the struck competitor may receive a red card as a result of serious foul play.\n● Harsh and systematic arguments with marshals, groundless challenging of Marshals’ decisions, rude and derogatory attitude to the opponents and other participants of the competition.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"82225f0fff860cb8f10b43f6120ba08daa3d45ac48e304dcce33071aa9993800","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Appeal","body":"","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5b97781591e96230dc64f8bb2091874eeb25c23fb84afa7a290cc5a3624ee200","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"How to appeal","body":"The competitor or the competitor’s representative (or a Team Captain) can appeal a decision made by the Marshals’ Brigade or the Knight Marshal. The appeal is submitted to the Secretary. The number of appeals is determined by the Tournament organizer. It is recommended 1 appeal. If the appeal is approved then the competitor may make an additional appeal","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24fc312243d93a45b881df2345b5605c5d544d600adf233eed22cc644ba7b9d0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"When to appeal","body":"The competitor’s representative (or a Team Captain) must announce the intention to appeal to the Secretary in person.\nAn appeal must be submitted within 15 minutes after the end of the fight, before the start of the fights of the next phase of the competition","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"32a901b2dd39c9191d41df78036ba259ab07343e9311218934a98357871e719c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Why to appeal","body":"An appeal can be filed according to the following reasons :\n6.3.1 False implementation of a penalty (reprimand, warning, or disqualification).\n6.3.2 Unregistered clean blows to the legal strike zones that affect the course of the fight.\n6.3.3 Unregistered rule violations by the opponent that should result in a penalty (reprimand, warning, disqualification).\n6.4 Result of the appeal The possible results of the appeal are :\n● A general rematch of the round.\n● Imposing, or withdrawal of yellow cards","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e9cf157a41e72733371d77bc8cbd2227b48b55bea18e0954116e637383244b29","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.5","title":"Appeal to Judiciary Committee","body":"If the Team Captain is dissatisfied with the Knight Marshall's decision, they can appeal to the Buhurt International Judiciary Committee.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"numbering skips to 5.5 (expected 5.4): check the official document for a missing provision","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5ca709d7a199e99dc665211261514109fc30a642447bc77b2049fefee37e5c6b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"6","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules\n\nDecember 2024 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2024.12)\n- Add: 6.2 to the Secretary in person\n- Delete: 6.2 to the Knight Marshal in person\n- Delete: 5: Authorized equipment (moved to Duels rules document)\n- Delete: 6.2 An appeal is submitted directly after the end of the fight and is announced when the Knight Marshal requests for any objections before the competitor has left the list.\n- Delete: 6.1 The appeal is submitted to theTournament Organizer/Secretary March 2024 (Version update from 2024.01 to 2024.06)\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"33f2603b1b84b606134a460123dc2843a5909509602c6caed6cb6e0694aaa4fd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_historical_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","history":"archive-2026-10-06","inventory_key":"tournament/duel-regulations","version":{"version":"2025.03","title":"Duels Regulations 2025.03","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Title \"Duels Regulations\"; cover \"VER. 2025.03\" while the change log says \"February 2025 (Version update from 2024.12 to 2025.02)\": the label is the cover's, the disagreement is recorded. The unversioned \"Duels Regulations.pdf\" is byte-identical (SHA-256).","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GfVrh4knqdG7txsIXn0LFPWmEcbp3gPI/view","source_sha256":"ec7ad0283f6cec6852db08892a8026ebb8c53f66812635cf5abe0c0dd8b8f9ca","retrieved_at":null,"page_count":11,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"287b33112a1746daeee10503302a0a0644073a1239f1fc105d01ebe6f3bae358","detected":{"version":null,"date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 historical import), read from the archived PDF: cover (OCR of the page image), footers and change log","historical":true,"edition_seq":2,"edition_evidence":"Title \"Duels Regulations\"; cover \"VER. 2025.03\" while the change log says \"February 2025 (Version update from 2024.12 to 2025.02)\": the label is the cover's, the disagreement is recorded. The unversioned \"Duels Regulations.pdf\" is byte-identical (SHA-256).","source_files":[{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Duels Regulations 2025.03.pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"ec7ad0283f6cec6852db08892a8026ebb8c53f66812635cf5abe0c0dd8b8f9ca","drive_file_id":"1GfVrh4knqdG7txsIXn0LFPWmEcbp3gPI"},{"file":"Tournament/Archive/Duels Regulations.pdf","archive":"Tournament","sha256":"ec7ad0283f6cec6852db08892a8026ebb8c53f66812635cf5abe0c0dd8b8f9ca","drive_file_id":"1yTtWKDJwBDfwfn7SIywaqC5Bv2Jl9T5s"}],"reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["page(s) without extractable text: 1","4 line(s) looked like a numbered heading but did not fit the sequence","2 provision(s) need review against the official document"],"pages":11,"source_lines":278,"assigned_lines":288,"furniture_lines":66,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99941,"provisions":53,"numbered":51,"needs_review":2,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[1],"rejected_numbers":4,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"figure","number":null,"title":null,"body":"","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:page-1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":"cover page: artwork only, no text","topics":["cover"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"Duel regulations","page_from":2,"page_to":2,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9d55c5711935e07df2fb68aac38d71e6a11b9142e565bc86f965cb076926ea53","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General Provisions","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d3460a1bce22168eb4fc581713c7f54838f7f6aa5be599e1b9b2b4e8ddc14938","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"List Regulations","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c3f0115386bb4274756fb2ea4ddb8735bb7cca466a21741310ef0108a780b825","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.1","title":null,"body":"Fights of the Buhurt International duel categories Triathlon, Sword and Buckler, Sword and Shield, Polearm are held in hard-surface lists, with a barrier measuring 5–10m wide and 5–10m long. The height of the barrier is 0.9–1.3m.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.1.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3b199aa37f95f4a30c88e487174dcc44ee1c57e15ddaab3257899449b83f2045","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.2","title":null,"body":"There must be a fenced, 2m-wide safety zone around every side of the list.\nOnly the Marshal Brigade, support of the competitors, Team Managers, technical brigade and accredited photo/videographers are permitted into the safety zone during the fights. Any extra competitor or non-combatant of the team entering the safety zone during fights will result in a penalty (yellow card) for the individual or their team (club).","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.1.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cbcf8a767c0315b31daa110551b8762cdb8384445ab9e4a41ad41f03b3cccd09","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Weight categories","body":"There are no weight categories in the duel category.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:1.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"50561c1faedb2e69e10b3ffff6ab52b4f6c60b3143169a526b33f858eac4e89d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Marshals Committee","body":"The team of Marshals includes:","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4be8b2ffda8ea3a9f4c559ee9ce488d01f38840e4838fdfdfda8ad7c92fbbc80","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"One (1) Knight Marshal (Chief Official/Head Referee)","body":"● Observes the general course of the fight and assesses actions of the competitors in the list.\n● In case of disagreement, the Knight Marshal makes the final decision.\n● Only the Knight Marshal can interfere with the course of the fight.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6c5b09dab886f13939fcc26c3ffb6267fd62279bab18e237fc15b83fe5ba38a5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Four (4) Line Marshals (Fight Officials/Referees)","body":"● Supervise the fight and score the clean blows delivered to the permitted strike zones.\n● Take note of rule violations committed during the fight.\n● Cannot interfere with the fight.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5e6ca1a35b7ce7756a58a28d36e2068e1b271e6b6755c4c44f23ebc83d58ba46","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"One (1) Timekeeper","body":"● Times the rounds of the fight.\n● If the Knight Marshal halts the fight, the Timekeeper stops timing the round and resumes timing when the fight resumes\n● Registers the results of the round in rating protocol.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0400db351f677a7b2e15806dce2b9f41a7e5baf44cf71df313ea412bf8b0e869","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"One (1) Authenticity Committee Representative (AC Rep)","body":"● Authenticity representative who will preform on location AC checks","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1f16bae93051958277637cd08ae24cb478165db3ec7987c46c6e09138d51987b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.5","title":"One (1) Videos Supervisor","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:2.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f2af5bec0f4995d220240a6bd1d66e136113d9883a921ba182e042027d9c2e2b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"Fight Proceedings","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"176af81a5c990c7e8f3f01362a9a04513591ed7ec464da362b11ecc3c2c206c8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Preparation for the fight","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"992f60bd5675857ce1fb9593723d84af660608273f7b56cc521f76026fffbe9b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.1","title":"The Knight Marshal invites the competitors to report to the designated area of the","body":"list to pass pre-fight, authenticity, aesthetic, and technical equipment checks. They announce the competitors preparing for the next fight.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b54f0f13c07fcded21f205afc422ab7df6266cd49b61ed294d3d281745fc5349","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.2","title":null,"body":"Invited competitors are granted up to sixty (60) seconds to report to the list.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"81d976ae3ec701c1a3ef80b3cc8c48a23ed296b6e6fcb908a467b667b0936a33","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.3","title":null,"body":"The Knight Marshal can ask the competitors to enter the list with their helmets off.\nWhen the correspondence between the competitors present in the list and competitors registered for the fight has concluded, they will then be given an additional 30 seconds to put on their helmets and prepare for the fight. Seconds (assistants) outside the list can assist the competitors in preparation. The competitors are not allowed to leave the list before the start of the fight. This measure excludes the possibility of team roster replacement.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d2efe34602f9a1805ebed11d3e894e45682d5bd8a80397e7fc2b8dab40c1040e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.4","title":"The Knight Marshal requests marshals and competitors to confirm their","body":"readiness.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"985addafa7124f9d8afc9e2e8ed634f7c4d5bb3fe51b697276e28a9fdd38981c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1.5","title":"The Knight Marshal signals the beginning of the fight with the command “Fight!”","body":"","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.1.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"79f283c4148ca9c52dd78b30bb7299eaf2e27a05e8a6b114675baa77147f2a22","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Characteristics of each category","body":"The organizers can alter the length of the fights/number of rounds/orders of the rounds (one category, triathlon, four fights type of competition) provided this decision is coordinated with the Head Organization and is registered in the Tournament Regulations.\nBreak between Technical\nCategory End of round Fight victory rounds win Longsword Total score from two (2) main rounds and an Sword and shield additional 30-second\n60 seconds of effective 30 seconds to rest round in case of a tie. 10-0 time and the “Stop fight”\nPolearms command of the Knight The score must have at Marshall least a 2 point difference.\n120 seconds to Total score from three (3) Triathlon change their main rounds equipment Achieve two (2) round 5 clean blows delivered by victories one competitor during the\nSword and buckler No break 5-0 round or 60 seconds of An additional round may effective time be fought in case of a tie.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"layout looks like a table or columns: compare with the official page","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"913f4d4f6f98b26edcffa26b5a622962d32e27b8b95a6a4a0dd9178eb0514cfc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"End of the round","body":"All marshals in the list report to the Knight Marshal to announce the score and any rule violations. Based on the marshals’ reports and personal observations, the Knight Marshal makes a decision about the result of the round by :\n● Processing the appeals (if any were submitted).\n● Issuing penalties (reprimands, warnings, and disqualification) to the competitors.\nAnnouncing the result of the round.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"af076feaeab7fa6c8d760b54f0a5516bfeb7c6b7d6cb60b7ac2d6e7cf4dcadb5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"End of the fight","body":"When the conditions of fight victory are reached, the winner of the fight is announced.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d3981634061ac76d586110faf956f5c8e0000434e1600bd1334c6fdbe3c6b235","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.1","title":null,"body":"The Secretary registers the results of the rounds in rating protocol :\n● The round victory\n● The round score\n● Match victory\n● 2 point difference for Polearm | Sword and Shield | Longsword examples: total score competitor A 10, competitor B 11 no winner additional round needed total score competitor A 15, competitor B 13, winner is competitor A\n● Yellow and red cards in the competitor’s rating 2.5 One (1) Authenticity Committee.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cb7b893bdabd7eeb98ea5334ece1c87f294b8f96359bf4b5920addd738a5cea9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.2","title":"The winner is documented on the scoresheet. The rest of the rating scores","body":"(victories in the rounds, loss of the points because of yellow cards) are considered only in case of a draw in points.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"89db9aad74484a570ea2d55220ee172ee3ecb61211f248df5993f961a71149c8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4.3","title":null,"body":"provided the competitors are informed in advance, the number of rounds and break time can be decreased under extraordinary circumstances.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.4.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3.4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"26dede1b5c49df2a72dd5fa941513d78019b6200ee3523940230ff8aeebc3054","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Technical win","body":"A technical victory is awarded to one of the competitors in the following cases:\n● If the opponent withdraws from the fight before it starts.\n● If the opponent fails to report to the list upon the Knight Marshal’s call. Competitors who fail to report to the list for the fight are penalized with a yellow card.\n● If the opponent fails to prepare the equipment within the designated time.\n● If the opponent cannot participate in the competition because of an injury or disqualification (two (2) Yellow cards or Red card). If the opponent injures the competitor with an illegal strike, the competitor receives a penalty of double yellow cards and is disqualified.\n● If the opponent has an equipment failure (weapon and armor) that is impossible to fix in one (1) minute. Assessment is made by the Knight Marshal.\n● If the opponent gains three (3) reprimands during one fight.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:3.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f6adbb41e68e1828069a5a23af50aa292099832e7096fb1c5e639d0e9293fd25","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Penalties","body":"","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bcfa77d805fe5b0fc96ec3b2f7e2d5ca1e73ea0a3a85f245c34f8e0b9e69aabd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Verbal warning","body":"A verbal warning is a penalty imposed for insignificant rules violation, aiming at indicating the rules violation to the competitor. A verbal warning is not registered in protocols.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c3df64f72642259e3b1b105c0671c17c80f16e2545be1e17f59dbcc90cfe6604","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Reprimand","body":"A reprimand to a competitor will result in three (3) points added to their opponent’s score. The points gained because of the reprimand are registered separately in the rating. Reprimands are not noted in the tournament protocol and personal records of the competitors. The competitor receives a reprimand in case of :","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c8753acf5951763cd464326e3455603099a071fc7b0e55be1cbf2fc9ea1d766e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.1","title":null,"body":"Failing to report to the list within the designated time frame (one (1) minute).","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"85bf3f942ed59ad788febda13d6fefde5fae9ff281fbeb91cc368556461f51c7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.2","title":"A fall that was caused by offensive actions of the opponent, provided they were","body":"conducted in accordance with the ruleset.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f0c73674f3e701c0dbd6e5b6f782abc74279b363bc603afa12a4b33d4c220edc","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.3","title":"Armor (not weapon or shield) failure that prevents the competitor from continuing","body":"the fight. If the issue was fixed within the time limit (set by the knight marshal), the fight can continue. The decision on the severity of the Armor failure and time limit is made by the Knight Marshal.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7d7874413468ba29a3009739a03a176019cdca805470c310adf82fa0404e14f1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.4","title":null,"body":"Weapon loss during the fight.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"abc5ef63738c67fd8e45fbea6e814651ff189415dcbe5947dd56c2bc44b38e36","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.5","title":"Passive attitude. A competitor’s refusal to conduct offensive actions during the","body":"length of time (not less than 15 seconds) is considered a passive attitude.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"477f4df25c723c9368a7c7bdb601f9bf7bf36150683eae181770202f542a3776","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2.6","title":null,"body":"Falling or stepping outside the boundaries of the list.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.2.6","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9f606223008b73af0dc417cdd91178dc4de9a7be9adaf13bd0663afa7a7d1c6a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3","title":"Yellow Card","body":"An official warning (yellow card) is a penalty imposed for a rule violation that is registered in the protocol of the tournament, and affects the competitor’s rating. A competitor can receive up to two (2) Yellow cards within a tournament before disqualification.\nThe competitor can receive one (1) or two (2) yellow cards for all following actions, depending on the severity of the violation and the Knight Marshals’ decision :","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b8dedb25a982bb232a4343be3b1efc76562979fdef485dfb399ca40d8ae28067","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.1","title":null,"body":"A competitor performs any illegal action listed in the Rules for the Triathlon, Longsword, Sword and Buckler, Sword and shield, and Polearm categories.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bf2ffc1938f18f64f2a4d0fa04fdd7cc36889218e8e05b772149d238b85a9d56","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.2","title":"A competitor performs any action not listed in the authorized techniques section","body":"of the Rules for the Triathlon, Longsword, Sword and Buckler, Sword and shield, and Polearm categories.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0aab0b96394294baece0b7ec30bcb659afa7c752a48988001c344cf74f36ced9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.3","title":null,"body":"A competitor enters the list with unauthorized equipment (see section 5).","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5"],"content_sha256":"12a60bd43a2b1e1d4250d2f8a5835a52a0a03a71b30da3f11429ebbee256d407","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.4","title":"For a demonstration of poor sportsmanship, derogatory behaviour, obscene","body":"language, comments directed at marshals, opponents, or spectators.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5d1682e16dc9ba686b75902a8fdb4836afe914e8058fd3e254072a3b36e285c6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.5","title":null,"body":"A competitor enters the safety zone during fights.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"38d7f0f10c4bbcb345d73c4f6480df704705eb1df2aa4853965790252d4ebf67","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.6","title":null,"body":"A competitor starts the fight before the ‘Fight’ command.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.6","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"566751d5323e07d0b776d487fd5b1540b317b5edecc8260978bc39765af7d118","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.7","title":null,"body":"A competitor performs offensive actions after the ‘Stop Fight’ command.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.7","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cd06a35054b87e1cd6ad13ef6e3a00d9427e6cf67b74eca693c6118768b406e9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3.8","title":null,"body":"A competitor ignores the Knight Marshals’ orders.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.3.8","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8fded9566bdeee8bc2de1e7612d70d45ca24f992057653c26187dc7c49ea8851","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.4","title":"Red Card","body":"Disqualification (red card) is a penalty resulting from severe or regular (second yellow card) rule violations and is registered in the tournament protocol. The red carded competitor will be withdrawn from the tournament. Only the Knight Marshal of the tournament can apply red cards. The competitor receives a disqualification in case of\n● Systematic rule violations (two (2) yellow cards during the tournament).\n● Injuring the opponent with illegal strikes. However, if marshals or medics ascertain that an injury has been simulated, the struck competitor may receive a red card as a result of serious foul play.\n● Harsh and systematic arguments with marshals, groundless challenging of Marshals’ decisions, rude and derogatory attitude to the opponents and other participants of the competition.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.4","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"82225f0fff860cb8f10b43f6120ba08daa3d45ac48e304dcce33071aa9993800","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.5","title":"Green Card","body":"An official authenticity warning (green card) is a penalty imposed for a rule violation that is registered in the protocol of the tournament, and affects the competitor’s rating. A competitor can only receive a (1) green card and then a yellow card within a tournament before disqualification.\nThe competitor can receive one (1) green card only once they choose to enter the list with the appropriate infraction level based upon the Infraction classification and application document.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:4.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6191585e71383951f7490dd2557ae82990d314b428fa89c4b9fd3726e3f375d8","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Appeal","body":"","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5b97781591e96230dc64f8bb2091874eeb25c23fb84afa7a290cc5a3624ee200","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"How to appeal","body":"The competitor or the competitor’s representative (or a Team Captain) can appeal a decision made by the Marshals’ Brigade or the Knight Marshal. The appeal is submitted to the Secretary. The number of appeals is determined by the Tournament organizer. It is recommended 1 appeal. If the appeal is approved then the competitor may make an additional appeal","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.1","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24fc312243d93a45b881df2345b5605c5d544d600adf233eed22cc644ba7b9d0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"When to appeal","body":"The competitor’s representative (or a Team Captain) must announce the intention to appeal to the Secretary in person.\nAn appeal must be submitted within 15 minutes after the end of the fight, before the start of the fights of the next phase of the competition","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.2","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"32a901b2dd39c9191d41df78036ba259ab07343e9311218934a98357871e719c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Why to appeal","body":"An appeal can be filed according to the following reasons :\n6.3.1 False implementation of a penalty (reprimand, warning, or disqualification).\n6.3.2 Unregistered clean blows to the legal strike zones that affect the course of the fight.\n6.3.3 Unregistered rule violations by the opponent that should result in a penalty (reprimand, warning, disqualification).\n6.4 Result of the appeal The possible results of the appeal are :\n● A general rematch of the round.\n● Imposing, or withdrawal of yellow cards","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.3","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e9cf157a41e72733371d77bc8cbd2227b48b55bea18e0954116e637383244b29","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.5","title":"Appeal to Judiciary Committee","body":"If the Team Captain is dissatisfied with the Knight Marshall's decision, they can appeal to the Buhurt International Judiciary Committee.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:5.5","parent_key":"duel-regulations:5","review_status":"needs_review","review_note":"numbering skips to 5.5 (expected 5.4): check the official document for a missing provision","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5ca709d7a199e99dc665211261514109fc30a642447bc77b2049fefee37e5c6b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"6","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules\n\nFebruary 2025 (Version update from 2024.12 to 2025.02)\n- Add: Green card rules\n- Adjustment: sword buckler technical win from 2 to 5 points\n\nDecember 2024 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2024.12)\n- Add: 6.2 to the Secretary in person\n- Delete: 6.2 to the Knight Marshal in person\n- Delete: 5: Authorized equipment (moved to Duels rules document)\n- Delete: 6.2 An appeal is submitted directly after the end of the fight and is announced when the Knight Marshal requests for any objections before the competitor has left the list.\n- Delete: 6.1 The appeal is submitted to theTournament Organizer/Secretary March 2024 (Version update from 2024.01 to 2024.06)\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"duel-regulations:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"55839675d79e04fcb77777416a2dda882599208f271cb904c816ddeb7ff2d7f1","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
